    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-Biomedical-Sciences_R19889": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure Track Assistant Professor Biomedical Sciences Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Biomedical Sciences at the Iowa State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor. These are full-time, 9-month positions with salary commensurate with qualifications. The successful candidates will join a department with active research programs in pharmacology, neuroscience, vaccine development, infectious disease, and molecular and cell biology. These individuals will be expected to establish a dynamic, extramurally-funded research program within these or a complementary field pertinent to human and/or animal health. The successful candidates will also teach pharmacology to professional and/or graduate students. Research programs in pharmacology-relevant disciplines are of particular interest, including neurobiology, cellular signaling, drug mechanism and mode of action, endocrinology, toxicology, and receptor or antimicrobial pharmacology.   Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD with research experience relevant to Biomedical Sciences Preferred Qualifications: Research plans and experience relevant to Pharmacology or other Biomedical Sciences Strong record of publication in peer-reviewed journals relative to appointment Demonstrated success obtaining extramural funding Evidence of effective research mentoring experience Teaching engagement at a university or professional school Department/Program & College Description: The Biomedical Sciences department supports the mission of the College of Veterinary Medicine by teaching a basic science curriculum to veterinary medical students, conducting state-of-the-art basic and translational research relevant to the health of animals and humans, and educating graduate students through both the departmental graduate program and several multidisciplinary interdepartmental programs at Iowa State University. Departmental faculty research programs span a range of One Health disciplines including pharmacology, neuroscience, microbial and helminth infectious disease and vaccine development. Iowa State University and Central Iowa Iowa State University is a Carnegie Foundation R1 institution with a student enrollment exceeding 30,000 located in Ames, a progressive community just 30 miles north of Des Moines. Ames offers extensive parks and trails, strong public schools, a comparatively low cost of living and convenient access to the cultural and recreational opportunities of one of the fastest-growing metro areas in the Midwest . More information about the university and city can be found here: https://www.provost.iastate.edu/faculty-success/prospective   Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/bms/ https://vetmed.iastate.edu/about/about-the-college/cvm-employment/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Cover Letter 2) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 3) Research Statement detailing past accomplishments and future goals (3 pages maximum) 4) Teaching Statement detailing pedagogy, experience and future plans (1 page maximum) 5) Contact information for Three Professional References external to Iowa State University If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before October 05, 2026. This position will be open until filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19889 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Veterinary-Technician-I_R19892": {
      "title": "Veterinary Technician I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Veterinary Technician I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Associate or Bachelor’s degree in a veterinary technology program accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA) or the Canadian Veterinary Medical Association (CVMA), and • Registered, licensed, or certified as a veterinary technician within one year of the start date. Job Description: Whether you're launching your veterinary technician career or looking to advance your expertise in a specialty area, the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center offers the opportunity to grow your skills, work alongside leading specialists, and make a meaningful impact on animal health.  The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC) at Iowa State University is seeking Veterinary Technicians to join our team. We are hiring across multiple specialty areas, including Emergency & Critical Care, Anesthesia, and the Large Animal Hospital.  As Iowa's premier veterinary teaching hospital, the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center provides advanced medical and surgical care for companion and large animals from across Iowa and the surrounding region. Our board-certified specialists, residents, interns, veterinary technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work together to deliver exceptional patient care while advancing veterinary medicine through education, research, and clinical excellence.  Apply once and be considered for multiple Veterinary Technician opportunities across Emergency & Critical Care, Anesthesia, and the Large Animal Hospital.  Successful candidates hired into a Veterinary Technician I, II, or III position within Emergency & Critical Care, Anesthesia, or the Large Animal Hospital between May 1, 2026 and June 30, 2027 may be eligible for a $1,000 recruitment incentive. Payment terms and conditions will be outlined in a payment agreement at the time of hire.  Why Join the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center?  At Iowa's premier veterinary teaching hospital, you'll be part of a collaborative team dedicated to exceptional patient care, education, and innovation. Working alongside board-certified specialists, clinicians, residents, interns, and veterinary students, you'll gain hands-on experience with advanced medical and surgical cases while continuing to develop your technical and clinical skills.  Whether your passion is emergency medicine, anesthesia, or large animal care, you'll have the opportunity to make a direct impact on patient outcomes while helping educate the next generation of veterinarians.  What You'll Do  Responsibilities vary by specialty area but may include:  Provide compassionate, high-quality nursing care to hospitalized, emergency, critical care, and surgical patients.  Perform veterinary technical procedures under the direction of licensed veterinarians.  Monitor patient status, recognize changes in condition, and communicate findings to the veterinary team.  Administer medications, treatments, and fluid therapy.  Assist with emergency procedures, anesthesia, surgery, diagnostics, and patient recovery.  Collect and process diagnostic samples.  Safely handle and restrain companion and/or large animal patients.  Operate, maintain, and troubleshoot specialized medical equipment.  Maintain accurate and thorough medical records.  Collaborate with faculty clinicians, residents, interns, veterinary students, and fellow technicians to coordinate patient care.  Demonstrate clinical techniques and support the educational experience of veterinary students.  Specialty Areas: Emergency & Critical Care (ECC)  Provide nursing care for emergency and critically ill patients in a fast-paced environment that delivers advanced care 24 hours a day, 365 days a year. Technicians play an essential role in triaging patients, supporting emergency procedures, and providing continuous monitoring for hospitalized patients.  Anesthesia  Support all phases of anesthesia, including patient assessment, anesthetic preparation, induction, monitoring, pain management, and recovery while working alongside board-certified anesthesiologists and experienced anesthesia technicians.  Large Animal Hospital  Support the care of equine and food animal patients in emergency, intensive care, medical, and surgical settings. Technicians work closely with clinicians and students to provide comprehensive patient care while developing advanced large animal nursing and technical skills.  Work Environment  These positions are fully onsite at the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center and involve hands-on patient care in a collaborative clinical environment. Depending on the specialty area, schedules may include rotating shifts, on-call responsibilities, weekends, holidays, and physically active work with companion and/or large animal patients. Candidates in positions requiring on-call coverage must live within a reasonable distance of the hospital to meet response-time expectations.  Preferred Qualifications Experience working with small and/or large animal patients in a veterinary clinical setting. Experience in a veterinary teaching hospital, specialty/referral hospital, or high-volume general practice, including completion of clinical rotations in these settings. Experience providing nursing care to veterinary patients, including patient restraint, handling, monitoring, and treatment in emergency, anesthesia, medical, or surgical environments. Experience assisting with anesthesia, surgical procedures, emergency and critical care, or large animal procedures, including patient monitoring and recovery. Experience performing technical skills such as venipuncture, intravenous (IV) catheter placement, medication administration, collection of diagnostic samples, and operation of common veterinary equipment under appropriate supervision. . Department Unit/Website: http://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/ Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 7601a Original Posting Date: September 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 30, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19892 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Tenure-or-Clinical-Track---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-Anesthesiology_R19820": {
      "title": "Tenure or Clinical Track – Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Anesthesiology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure or Clinical Track – Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Anesthesiology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University (ISU) is seeking qualified applicants for a full time, clinical or tenure track faculty appointment in Anesthesiology in the Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS) and the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC). The LVMC is a state-of-the-art teaching hospital providing specialized care for companion and production animals throughout Iowa and the surrounding states. The candidates will join an anesthesia team comprised of 3 faculty Anesthesiologists that are complemented by 9 veterinary anesthesia technicians and 1 anesthesia residents. The department is seeking candidates to provide excellent patient care, teach didactic and laboratory courses in veterinary anesthesiology, provide clinical training for technicians and house officers, and enhance the national prominence of the LVMC’s Anesthesiology section. The successful candidate will help develop creative programs in scholarship, didactic and laboratory teaching in anesthesiology, academic service, and outreach activities. Clinical duties will include weekends, holidays, and after-hours service that are shared amongst the anesthesia faculty. Please elaborate on your ability to meet these preferred qualifications in your application. Start date is negotiable depending on the candidate. Second and third year ACVAA/ECVAA residents are encouraged to apply.   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent degree. Successful completion of an American College of Veterinary Anesthesia and Analgesia (ACVAA) or European College of Veterinary Anesthesia and Analgesia (ECVAA) residency program before first day of employment. State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before first day of employment. Preferred Qualifications: Diplomate of the American College of Veterinary Anesthesia and Analgesia (DACVAA) . Experience working with veterinary technicians and/or veterinary students in a clinical teaching setting. Experience running a clinical anesthesia service with a moderate to high caseload. Please elaborate on your ability to meet these preferred qualifications in your application. Department/Program & College Description: The LVMC is a state-of-the-art facility designed to provide specialized care and comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. Our clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work collaboratively to provide 24-hour, high-quality care to animal patients. As the nation’s first public veterinary school, Iowa State University’s College of Veterinary Medicine takes pride in its heritage while shaping the future of veterinary professional practice, education, research and service. At Iowa State, we translate our core values into action by seeking individuals who have experience working with students, colleagues, and constituents in various settings while performing to a high standard. Ames, Iowa is a progressive community of 60,000, located approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines, and has been named one of the best college towns in the nation with much to do and discover.   Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/small-animal/support-services/anesthesiology/ https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before September 24, 2026. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 25, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19820 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
