    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Associate-Professor-of-Practice_R19836": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Associate Professor of Practice Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Urban Planning and Development at Iowa State University invites applications for the position of Associate Professor of Practice to teach community-focused undergraduate and graduate studio courses. The initial appointment for this position will be one semester with a start date of January 1, 2027, and ending on May 15, 2027. Additional teaching opportunities may be available based on departmental needs and the candidate's interests. This is a part-time position. Planning studios are professional experiences in the curriculum. Working in partnership with external clients, students function as a professional planning consulting team to address real-world planning topics. The instructor guides students through all phases of the planning process, including project design, applied research, stakeholder engagement, data collection and analysis, development of planning recommendations, and preparation of professional planning products. The studios emphasize experiential learning, collaboration, project management, professional ethics, and client communication. The candidate will be expected to contribute meaningfully to the department's teaching mission. We are looking for individuals with strong communication skills who share our commitment to fostering excellence. Additional expectations are: Develop and oversee a client-based planning project in collaboration with a community partner. Mentor students through applied planning research, community engagement, plan development, and professional presentations. Supervise student project teams and foster a collaborative studio environment. Coordinate meetings, field visits, and communication with community partners and stakeholders. Evaluate student performance and provide timely feedback on individual and team work. Produce a high-quality professional planning product that meets client expectations and supports student learning outcomes. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in urban planning, or a closely related field. 10 or more years of professional planning experience in public, private, or nonprofit practice. Preferred Qualifications: AICP certification Demonstrated knowledge of planning processes, public engagement, and project management. Expertise in one or more planning practice areas such as comprehensive planning, housing, economic development, sustainability, resilience, transportation, land use, or community development. Experience working with interdisciplinary teams and community partners. Department/Program & College Description: About the Department of Urban Planning and Development The Department of Urban Planning and Development is one of only 16 accredited undergraduate planning programs in the United States, and we have an outstanding faculty who are committed to excellence in the teaching of planning at both undergraduate and graduate levels. Through the department's degree programs, students develop the skills and experience to become practicing planning professionals. Some of the major areas of expertise include: land-use planning and zoning environmental planning transportation planning site planning urban design In addition, our students regularly work with communities in Iowa to understand the issues and challenges and how planners play a role in addressing them. We also undertake high-quality research on behalf of federal and state government, business, the nonprofit sector, and other funding agencies, all of which feed into the courses we teach to give our students a well-rounded foundation for their future careers. Department Unit/Website: For more information about our department's design program, see https://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/upd/ Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by October 1, 2026 . All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at http://jobs.iastate.edu to Job Requisition Number R19836. The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format: 1) Letter of application that briefly discusses how the candidate meets each of the preferred qualifications. 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Contact information for three references, including name, their position, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information Direct questions to Biswa Das, Chair, Department of Urban Planning and Development, at bdas@iastate.edu. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 24, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19836 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Early-Childhood-Teacher-Assistant_R19686": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Teacher Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Early Childhood Teacher Assistant Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree Job Description: The Child Development Laboratory School in the Department of Human Development and Family Studies is seeking an Assistant Early Childhood Teacher. The Assistant Early Childhood Teacher fosters a safe, engaging, and inclusive learning environment, communicates with families as needed, and works with the classroom teachers and other program staff to support high-quality early childhood education. Collaborates with faculty, staff, and students within the Department of Human Development and Family Studies and across Iowa State University to support research, teaching, student learning, and interdisciplinary initiatives. The Child Development Laboratory School is accredited by the National Association for the Education of Young Children (NAEYC), licensed by the Iowa Department of Health and Human Services, and maintains a 5-Star rating through Iowa Quality for Kids (IQ4K). The program also serves as a teaching and learning laboratory for students in the Early Childhood Education Program. Example of Duties Collaborates with the teachers in the room to supervise the classroom. Serves as a role model for best practice in the classroom. Observe, document, and communicate children's behavioral and developmental needs while collaborating with families and colleagues. Maintains a safe classroom through adherence to HHS, NAEYC, IQ4K, CACFP, Caring for Our Children, and other safety standards recognized by the field of early childhood. Maintains adherence to state “teacher to child” ratios for their age group. Engages with parents’ daily, initiating written and/or face-to-face communication taking into consideration the communication needs of those with varied cultural and ethnic backgrounds. Assists in partnerships with departments on campus to encourage non HDFS student use of the Lab School. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with children from birth through age five in group early childhood settings, including supporting children with special needs. Demonstrated knowledge of developmentally appropriate practices and early childhood development. Experience planning, implementing, and assessing developmentally appropriate curriculum and learning experiences. Strong collaboration and teamwork skills, with the ability to work effectively with children, families, and colleagues. State of Iowa teaching license (initial, standard, or master) in Early Childhood Education or Early Childhood Special Education or Elementary Education with an Early Childhood Education Endorsement (endorsement 100, 1001, 262 and/or 103). Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS804 Original Posting Date: August 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19686 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Term-Faculty-of-Teaching-or-Practice-for-the-Department-of-Finance_R19832": {
      "title": "Term Faculty of Teaching or Practice for the Department of Finance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Term Faculty of Teaching or Practice for the Department of Finance Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Finance in the Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University is now accepting applications for a full-time term (i.e., non-tenure track) faculty position at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Teaching Professor, or Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Practice. This position will teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels in Finance beginning Spring semester, January 2027. Anticipated course load is four courses per semester (i.e., a 4-4 teaching load). This position will consist primarily of in-person classroom instruction on the Ames, IA campus, with the possibility of some online course delivery. The successful candidate will additionally contribute to departmental service and/or student activities (such as case competition preparation, etc., depending on course load assignment). The initial term length will be for one year, ending December 31, 2027, with the possibility for renewal.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s Degree in Business or closely related field Qualified candidates must meet the college’s standards to be qualified under AACSB accreditation standards Preferred Qualifications: Prior collegiate teaching experience of at least five years in finance or closely related field Professional industry experience (e.g., financial services, corporate finance) Professional credentials in finance (e.g., CFA) PhD in Finance or closely related field Solid technological skills to support use of online instructional tools Department/Program & College Description: The Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University, established in 1984, furthers Iowa State University’s land-grant ideals by training students to be knowledgeable and ethical communicators, leaders, collaborators, and problem solvers through impactful research, innovative teaching, and community engagement. With the largest undergraduate business program in the state of Iowa and nationally ranked graduate programs, the Ivy College of Business is home to over 5000 students with a strong growth trajectory. We pride ourselves on our high ethical standards and our drive to promote an environment where all individuals may succeed academically, professionally, and personally. Each member of our community is committed to the college’s mission to link theory with practice for tomorrow’s business leaders. The college offers undergraduate, graduate, and Ph.D. programs and is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). Less than five percent of business schools worldwide receive this accreditation. Department Unit/Website: https://www.ivybusiness.iastate.edu/about-ivy/academic-d Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: December 31, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References To be fully considered for this position, please apply on or before October 14, 2026 . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. For questions regarding this position, please contact the Department Chair, Dr. Bidisha Chakrabarty at bidisha@iastate.edu. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 24, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19832 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Lecturer-in-Counseling-Psychology_R19827": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Counseling Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Lecturer in Counseling Psychology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Psychology in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa, invites applications for a part-time, term faculty position at the rank of Lecturer to teach a graduate course in group counseling in the department’s Counseling Psychology Ph.D. program. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching an in-person graduate-level course focused on the theory and practice of group counseling. Responsibilities include preparing and delivering course instruction, facilitating experiential learning activities, evaluating student learning, and providing students with feedback and guidance consistent with doctoral-level training in counseling psychology. The appointment is for the Spring 2027 semester, with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in counseling or clinical psychology by the start date of the appointment Training or professional experience in group counseling or group psychotherapy Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in counseling or clinical psychology Experience providing group counseling or psychotherapy Experience working with or training doctoral students in counseling psychology Evidence of effective teaching Current licensure as a psychologist Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Psychology at Iowa State University offers thriving Ph.D. programs in social, cognitive, and counseling psychology and is home to the largest number of undergraduate majors in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. Consistent with the university’s land-grant mission, our research builds psychological theory through empirical investigations and applies scientific findings to benefit individuals, communities, and society. Our department is highly collegial, supportive, and collaborative. The Counseling Psychology Ph.D. program prepares students for professional practice, research, and teaching in counseling psychology. Students receive broad training in psychological science and professional practice through coursework, research, supervised clinical experiences, and other professional development opportunities. Iowa State University is located in Ames, a vibrant community of approximately 66,000 in central Iowa, about 30 miles north of Des Moines. Ames offers extensive parks and trails, strong public schools, a comparatively low cost of living, and convenient access to the cultural and recreational opportunities of the state’s largest metropolitan area. More information about the university and city can be found here: https://www.provost.iastate.edu/faculty-success/prospective Department Unit/Website: https://psychology.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References To ensure full consideration, applications should be received by October 1, 2026, but will be accepted until the position is filled . If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19827 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Seed-Pathology_R19814": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Seed Pathology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Seed Pathology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Plant Pathology, Entomology and Microbiology and the Seed Science Center in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at Iowa State University invite applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the area of seed pathology. We seek candidates with broad expertise in seed pathology whose research will support the development of state-of-the-art diagnostic tools that facilitate the detection of seedborne pathogens with particular emphasis on viruses, bacteria, and fungi. Candidates whose expertise encompasses the use of high-throughput sequencing and associated computational pipelines are of particular interest. The position is 65% research, 30% teaching, and 5% service. The successful candidate is expected to develop an externally funded, high-impact research program that engages students in the broad areas of plant pathology, seed pathology and bioinformatics while also participating in service to the university. ISU has extensive shared facilities for biological research, including -omics technology for genetics, genomics and microbiome studies and high-performance computing. The collaborative environment is enhanced by interdisciplinary and disciplinary graduate majors that promote cross-fertilization within labs. The successful candidate will have an office and laboratory in the Seed Science Building, which houses the Seed Science Center. The Seed Science Center is a globally recognized hub of excellence in seed testing, research, education, systems, and international programs. It is a leader in developing science to inform policy to benefit the world seed trade. The Center is home to the Seed Lab, one of the largest public testing laboratories in the U.S. that has provided accurate and professional seed testing services to growers and the seed industry for more than 130 years. The Department of Plant Pathology, Entomology and Microbiology serves as home to the ISU Plant and Insect Diagnostic Clinic, has access to numerous field research facilities, and administers a vibrant and experiential undergraduate microbiology program. Faculty have strengths in extension, teaching, and the scholarship of teaching and learning, and research across the full spectrum from fundamental to applied.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Plath Pathology, Plant Science or a closely related field with experience in the broad area of seed pathology   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of strong potential for conducting innovative research in seed pathology that includes the development of diagnostic tests for pathogens Evidence for the use of high-throughput sequencing and associated computational pipelines Evidence of a strong publication record in internationally recognized journals Evidence of strong potential for research mentoring Evidence of strong potential for collaborative research Evidence of strong potential for securing extramural funding Evidence of strong potential for evidence-based, innovative teaching  Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on \"Apply\" and complete the Employment Application. The application should include: 1) Cover Letter describing the qualifications for the position (2 pages max) 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Research Statement detailing experience and future plans (3 pages max) 4) Teaching Statement detailing philosophy, experience, and future plans (2 pages max) 5) Names and contact information for three references For guaranteed consideration, applications should be received by January 4th, 2027. Questions regarding this position should be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Scott Heuchelin ( scott3@iastate.edu ), or the Chair of the Department of Plant Pathology, Entomology and Microbiology, Steven Harris ( stevenh1@iastate.edu ). Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19814 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Statistics-1_R19800": {
      "title": "Two Assistant Professors in Statistics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Two Assistant Professors in Statistics Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Statistics, at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa, seeks two tenure-track assistant professors with expertise in statistics and data science beginning August 16, 2027. One of the positions will have a particular emphasis on sports analytics. The successful candidates will develop and sustain a high-quality and high-impact research program, successfully compete for external funding, and collaborate with world-class researchers at Iowa State in statistics and other disciplines.  Further, the successful candidates will engage in professional and institutional service, teach graduate and undergraduate students, and advise graduate students in one of the first and largest statistics graduate programs in the country. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD or equivalent degree in statistics or closely related discipline by appointment start date Preferred Qualifications: Foundational training in statistics and data science Ability to teach statistics and data science classes at the undergraduate and graduate levels Ability to develop and sustain a high-impact research program with the potential to secure external research funding Ability to contribute to Iowa State University’s growing strength in data science Ability to contribute to Iowa State University's growing strength in data science and, for one position, sports analytics Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Statistics is jointly administered by the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences and the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences.  The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences is one of the world’s leading institutions of agriculture, with more than 160 years of leadership in science, education and extension. The college educates future leaders, conducts mission-oriented research, and shares new knowledge for the betterment of Iowa and the world. The college is one of eight colleges at Iowa State University, which is one of the most influential land grant universities in the nation.   Central to Iowa State University’s mission, the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS) is a collaborative, vibrant community of faculty, students and staff, committed to learning, research, and innovation. With 21 departments, one professional school, 49 majors, and over 20 interdisciplinary programs, LAS faculty support student success and engage in pathbreaking research across a wide range of fields.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.stat.iastate.edu   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References 4) Additional documents submitted as one combined PDF:  Research Statement Teaching Statement For guaranteed consideration, please apply before October 1, 2026 .  Position is open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. If you have questions regarding the position, please contact Kathy Kiesling (kiesling@iastate.edu). Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 20, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19800 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Electrician-I_R19721": {
      "title": "Electrician I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Electrician I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Requires State of Iowa Class A or B Journeyman Electrician license. • Must possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. Job Description: Department Description – Utility Services Utility Services is a 24-hour, 365-day-a-year operation dedicated to meeting the energy needs of the Iowa State University community. The department operates and maintains four energy production facilities, as well as an extensive network of utility distribution systems that serve the entire Iowa State campus. Through a commitment to operational excellence, safety, and sustainability, Utility Services works to provide reliable, economical, and environmentally responsible utility services that support the university's teaching, research, and outreach mission. Its primary goal is to safely deliver dependable utility services while continuously advancing sustainability and efficiency across campus operations. Preferred Qualifications Experience reading blueprints and electrical schematics Experience installing, maintaining, and repairing Utility electrical systems.  Experience working electrical maintenance in utility plant or process plant environment. Click below to learn more about our team: https://www.fpm.iastate.edu/utilities/energy_production_facilities.asp Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots, repairs and replaces electrical systems and electrical operated equipment (generally less than 600V), including but not limited to circuit breakers, relays, switches, wiring, conduit, receptacles, and magnetic starters and controls. • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots, repairs and replaces electrical equipment, including but not limited to electric motors, transformers, generators, lights, fixtures, bulbs, tubes, motor control systems and meters. • Draws layouts, reads and interprets blueprints, schematics and other drawings. • As required, estimates materials needed and records time and materials expended on each work order. • Performs preventive maintenance on electrical equipment and systems. • Requires the knowledge of and ability to interpret local, state and national electrical codes. • Requires the ability to interpret instructions, design specifications and blueprints. • Perform other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of the principles, methods and techniques used in the electrical trade. • Knowledge of the tools and equipment of the electrical trade and skill in their safe use. • Knowledge of the occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trade. • Knowledge of safety precautions mandated by OSHA, NFPA, NEC, and the EPA. • Knowledge of and ability to interpret local, state and national electrical codes. • Ability to interpret instructions, specifications and blueprints. • Ability to plan and perform work involving the installation, modification, troubleshooting and repair of new and existing electrical systems, and related equipment. • Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. • Ability to work outdoors in all types of weather conditions or in areas where there is exposure to excessive noise, dirt and fumes and at elevated heights from ladders, scaffolds, or hydraulic lifts. • Ability to work independently during normal work hours and after hours. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5071a Original Posting Date: August 11, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 17, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19721 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Track-Position-in-Equine-Emergency-Surgery-and-Critical-Care_R19742": {
      "title": "Clinical Track Position in Equine Emergency Surgery and Critical Care",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Track Position in Equine Emergency Surgery and Critical Care Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Clinical Sciences, College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University is seeking qualified applicants for a 12-month, full-time, renewable clinical term-track position for Equine Emergency Surgery and Critical Care. The objective of this position is to provide clinical services in Equine Emergency Surgery and Critical Care by implementing new and current diagnostics, performing surgical and non-surgical procedures, and providing medical care and patient management to equine cases presented to the hospital. In this role, the faculty member will supervise and instruct students, interns, and residents assigned to the equine emergency service and provide didactic lectures and labs in your area of expertise to students within the DVM curriculum. The faculty member will also collaborate with the equine surgery, internal medicine, theriogenology, and ambulatory services to facilitate equine emergencies. The faculty member will have some capacity to pursue other areas of academic interests such as clinical duty (daytime), collaborative research and scholarly activity, and/or teaching, based on the candidates interest and needs of the department. We value a collaborative, team-oriented, and collegial individual with excellent communication skills to fill this role and to participate in departmental, college, or university committees.   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM Completion of an approved American College of Veterinary Surgeons - Large Animal (ACVS-LA), or American College of Veterinary Emergency & Critical Care – Large Animal (ACVECC-LA) residency program. State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before first day of employment Preferred Qualifications: Board certification by the ACVS-LA, and/or ACVECC-LA (equine) Advanced degree (MS, PhD) Previous experience teaching/instructing Department/Program & College Description: Iowa State University’s (ISU’s) Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center’s Equine Hospital is one of the state’s premier facilities which includes: an intensive care unit (ICU), isolation facility, general hospitalization wards, multiple examination rooms, and a climate controlled performance arena. We routinely work collaboratively with other large and small animal services including: equine surgery, equine theriogenology, farrier, equine ambulatory, equine internal medicine, small animal emergency & critical care, cardiology, dermatology and ophthalmology. Currently, the ISU LVMC is the process of expanding with a new addition for equine ICU, theriogenology, and equine rehabilitation. Current equipment includes, ultrasound machines, digital radiography, MRI, CT, endoscopy, and additional equipment for equine emergency and critical care. The ISU LVMC serves the state of Iowa and adjacent states with boarded certified specialists in equine internal medicine (4), equine surgery (3), equine theriogenology (2), equine field services (3), and farriery (2). Faculty collaborate together to provide the best veterinary care possible to the patients and are actively involved in developing new methods for equine treatment and management.   Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/equine/   Proposed Start Date: October 1, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: June 30, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before 09 /07/2026. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 10, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19742 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Ceramics_R19688": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Ceramics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Ceramics Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Art and Visual Culture in the College of Design at Iowa State University is offering a full-time tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Ceramics starting August 16, 2027. Qualified candidates for this studio-based position will bring an in-depth knowledge in ceramics arts, including processes, histories, and related materials and practices. Areas of expertise will include contemporary and traditional techniques embracing sculptural, functional, and installation-based approaches to making. Special attention will be given to candidates who bring an innovative and/or community-engaged approach to ceramic art, along with a critical knowledge of related materials to their teaching and creative work. Candidates with ethical and environmentally responsible approaches to their discipline and teaching are strongly encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching in the department of Art and Visual Culture and have opportunities to contribute to the interdisciplinary collegiate programs in the College of Design. The position includes working with students from a broad range of disciplinary backgrounds and abilities, including graduate students. Pedagogically adaptive and innovative approaches in teaching are expected. The position responsibilities also include scholarship and research in the area of the candidate's expertise; undergraduate and graduate student advising; service on department, college and university committees; and maintenance of the ceramic studio and related equipment. The Department of Art and Visual Culture is committed to sustaining a collegial, positive, and productive environment for each individual and the collective benefit of all. All faculty members are expected to exhibit and convey good citizenship within department, college, and university activities, interact collegially and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Master of Fine Arts (MFA) degree or equivalent in ceramics or related field Preferred Qualifications: Portfolio with evidence of critical approaches to ceramic-based art and craft Ability to work collaboratively with other disciplines and/or communities Demonstrated evidence of professional accomplishment, such as exhibition record, scholarship, and/or community-engaged practice Knowledge of contemporary and traditional practices in ceramic art and related art and design disciplines Experience in ethical and environmentally responsible art and design practices Experience maintaining a ceramics studio and related equipment Demonstrated ability to teach college-level introductory to advanced ceramics courses Department/Program & College Description: As a land grant and Research institution, Iowa State University upholds and advocates for the impact of creative activities, scholarship, and education both on-and off-campus. We embrace and value community and the people and knowledge that preceded the formation of our institution and that inform our current-day practices. The College of Design celebrates and builds on long-standing success as a comprehensive design school that embodies knowledge-sharing and innovation. The Department of Art and Visual Culture exemplifies these qualities through the creativity and entrepreneurship of its community of makers, educators, and scholars. With an integrated and cross-disciplinary approach to teaching and collaborating, we are committed to contributing to the excellence of the academic community and to building a culturally vibrant environment. We are especially seeking candidates who uphold and promote this purpose and who apply the above qualities in their teaching and research practice.   Department Unit/Website: Department of Art and Visual Culture Website: http://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/art-visual-culture/ Department of Art and Visual Culture - Ceramics: http://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/art-visual-culture/avc-art-studios/ceramics/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following as PDF files of no more than 5 MB each: 1) Letter of Application 2) Curriculum Vitae with contact information for three professional references 3) Research and Creative Activities Statement 4) Teaching Philosophy Statement 5) Two sample course syllabi, if applicable (consolidated into a single document) And the following portfolios should be uploaded to: https://iastate.app.box.com/f/6783419d8cff45f2a86aabe2192f38df , no more than 25 MB for each portfolio. 1) Portfolio of Creative Work: 20-page PDF portfolio of creative work including title, date, media 2) Teaching Portfolio: 20-page PDF portfolio of work by your students including student name, title, date, media and course. For full consideration, please apply by October 15, 2026. Sarah Kyle, Professor and Chair, AVC, 146 College of Design, Iowa State University, Ames, IA 50011-3093 If you have questions regarding this vacancy, please email Sarah Kyle, skyle@iastate.edu  or call 515-294-9985. If you have questions regarding the application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: July 29, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19688 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Psychology_R19700": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Psychology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Psychology in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in cognitive psychology. We welcome applicants with a record of research excellence in cognitive psychology and related disciplines. We are particularly interested in candidates who would bring a distinct area of expertise beyond the cognitive psychology program’s existing strengths in learning and long-term memory, spatial cognition, legal psychology, and judgment and decision making. Areas of particular interest include attention, perception, working memory, cognitive control, psycholinguistics, and quantitative modeling, although other areas that add breadth will also be considered. We also welcome applied work that advances understanding of cognitive processes in real-world contexts. Responsibilities include establishing and maintaining an active program of research, pursuing external funding, teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in cognitive psychology, mentoring undergraduate students, providing doctoral training in cognitive psychology, and contributing service to the department, college, university, and profession. The start date for the position is August 16, 2027. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in psychology or a closely related field, conferred by the start date of the appointment Preferred Qualifications: Record of excellence in research/scholarship in cognitive psychology using behavioral methods Evidence of or potential for securing external research support Research expertise in cognitive psychology that adds breadth beyond the program’s existing strengths in learning and long-term memory, spatial cognition, legal psychology, and judgment and decision making Evidence of or potential for effective undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentoring Department/Program & College Description: The psychology department at Iowa State University offers thriving Ph.D. programs in social, cognitive, and counseling psychology and is home to the largest number of undergraduate majors in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. Consistent with the university’s land-grant mission, our research builds psychological theory through empirical investigations and applies scientific findings to benefit individuals, communities, and society. With outstanding doctoral students, extensive support for research and grant writing, and a research-friendly teaching load (standard teaching load is 3 scheduled courses per year), Iowa State provides an ideal environment for professional growth and academic success. Our department is highly collegial, supportive, and collaborative. The cognitive psychology doctoral program has existing strengths in learning and memory, spatial cognition and navigation, and judgment and decision making, with applications in areas including AI, education, virtual environments, and legal psychology. Faculty and students have opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration through programs and initiatives in human-computer interaction, neuroscience, statistics, gerontology, and psychology and law. Iowa State University is located in Ames, a vibrant community of approximately 66,000 in central Iowa, about 30 miles north of Des Moines. Ames offers extensive parks and trails, strong public schools, a comparatively low cost of living, and convenient access to the cultural and recreational opportunities of the state’s largest metropolitan area. More information about the university and city can be found here: https://www.provost.iastate.edu/faculty-success/prospective.    Department Unit/Website: https://psychology.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 2) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 3) Statement of Research Interests 4) Statement of Teaching Interests and/or Philosophy 5) Contact information for three references To ensure full consideration, applications should be received by September 21, 2026, but will be accepted until the position is filled . For questions, please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Jason Chan, at ckchan@iastate.edu Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19700 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Assistant-Professor-of-Nursing_R19710": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-04\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Simulation Coordinator is responsible for the planning, coordination, implementation, and evaluation of simulation-based learning experiences for Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) students. This role supports the integration of simulation throughout the nursing curriculum to enhance clinical judgment, critical thinking, communication, and professional practice competencies. The Simulation Coordinator collaborates with faculty, students, standardized patients, and simulation staff to ensure high-quality, evidence-based simulation experiences that support program outcomes, accreditation standards, and regulatory requirements. The position will be a two-year term with renewal based on performance and department needs.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications:  Doctoral degree in nursing or related field and 3 years of clinical experience 2 years simulation experience Current unencumbered RN license. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in nursing education, simulation-based learning, or clinical education. Knowledge of healthcare simulation standards and best practices. Certification in healthcare simulation (CHSE or CHSE-A) preferred or willingness to obtain certification. Experience with high-fidelity simulation equipment, audiovisual technologies, and simulation management software. Knowledge of nursing IBON and accreditation standards and regulatory requirements. Strong organizational, communication, collaboration, and project management skills. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with faculty, students, healthcare partners, and interdisciplinary teams. Experience with concept-based curriculum design, competency-based nursing education, and the integration of learning experiences that support the development and assessment of clinical judgment. Experience with learning management systems and educational technologies. Department/Program & College Description: Our mission is to enhance sustainable food, nutrition and healthcare systems that promote human well-being and improve the quality of life through education, research and outreach in food science, nutritional sciences, dietetics and nursing. Our vision is to be a global leader in food science, nutritional sciences and human health by integrating outcomes-driven education, innovative and multidisciplinary research, as well as dissemination and translation of knowledge. Department Unit/Website: https://nursing.iastate.edu/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: August 15, 2028 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before 8/10/2026 . Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19710 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
