    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Professor-of-Information-Systems-and-Business-Analytics--ISBA-_R19605": {
      "title": "Professor of Information Systems and Business Analytics (ISBA)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Professor of Information Systems and Business Analytics (ISBA) Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Information Systems and Business Analytics (ISBA) in the Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University invites applications for a tenured position at the rank of Professor. The position includes an endowed chair for a distinguished candidate with an exceptional record of research excellence and leadership in Information Systems and Business Analytics. The position holder will demonstrate the ability to maintain an active, high-quality research program that contributes to leading journals in MIS and related fields, demonstrate effectiveness in teaching, provide leadership in advancing the department's research and academic reputation, and fulfill normal service expectations. This is a full-time, 9-month appointment beginning August 16, 2027 . A later start date may also be considered. Initial review of applications will begin on September 30, 2026 , but applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. The position holder will conduct high-impact scholarly research suitable for publication in leading MIS journals such as Information Systems Research , Management Information Systems Quarterly , and The Journal of Management Information Systems . The holder will also be expected to contribute to mentoring Ph.D. students, and teaching ISBA-related courses at the Ph.D. level, as well as undergraduate or Master's levels. In addition, the position holder is expected to play a key role in advancing the department's research reputation through collaboration, mentorship, and leadership, helping to further enhance the department's national and international standing in ISBA research and education. The appointment also carries the expectation of typical institutional and professional service for the rank of Professor. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in MIS or a closely related field An outstanding record of scholarship, eligible for a tenured position at Iowa State University An established and active record of publishing research in top-tier IS journals such as Information Systems Research , Management Information Systems Quarterly , and The Journal of Management Information Systems . Preferred Qualifications: An influential scholarly reputation, as evidenced by scholarly citations and service to the profession An active research pipeline, including papers targeted or invited for revision at premier journals Experience in mentoring junior faculty and doctoral students Experience as a full-time, tenure track or tenured faculty member A record of effective teaching of ISBA-related courses Department/Program & College Description: The Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University, established in 1984, furthers Iowa State University’s land-grant ideals by training students to be knowledgeable and ethical communicators, leaders, collaborators, and problem solvers through impactful research, innovative teaching, and community engagement. With the largest undergraduate business program in the state of Iowa and nationally ranked graduate programs, the Ivy College of Business is home to over 5000 students with a strong growth trajectory. We pride ourselves on our high ethical standards and our drive to promote an environment where all individuals may succeed academically, professionally, and personally. Each member of our community is committed to the college’s mission to link theory with practice for tomorrow’s business leaders. The college offers undergraduate, graduate, and Ph.D. programs and is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). Less than five percent of business schools worldwide receive this accreditation. The faculty in the Department of Information Systems and Business Analytics are active in their field. They have published in premier journals such as Information Systems Research , MIS Quarterly , Journal of Management Information Systems , Management Science , the Journal of the Association for Information Systems , and Decision Sciences Journal . They serve or have served as editors, associate editors, and members of editorial boards for leading information systems journals. ISBA faculty have received doctorates from premier programs such as Arizona, Carnegie Mellon, Indiana, Northwestern University, and UT Dallas. ISBA faculty have active research projects in business analytics, cybersecurity, healthcare, IT strategy, artificial intelligence, and other IS and analytic areas. Ph.D. students graduating from the ISBA department have been placed at schools such as Notre Dame, Alabama, Oklahoma, Oklahoma State, Mississippi State, University of Cincinnati, and Florida Atlantic University. Department Unit/Website: www.ivybusiness.iastate.edu/information-systems-and-business-analytics/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before September 30, 2026 . If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: July 15, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19605 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Supply-Chain-Management_R19606": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Supply Chain Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Supply Chain Management Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Supply Chain Management in the Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University welcomes applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Supply Chain Management (SCM). Primary responsibilities include both research and teaching in SCM at the undergraduate, masters, and Ph.D. levels. Successful applicants will be expected to develop and maintain an outstanding research program targeting leading journals in supply chain management. The applicant is also expected to demonstrate strong teaching abilities. The ability to communicate effectively with prospective and current students, industry personnel, and the wider community is essential to this position. This full-time faculty position is on campus and in person. The expected start date for this position is August 2027. Required Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must currently have, or expect to complete by 8/16/27, an earned doctorate in business administration, with a concentration in supply chain management, transportation, logistics, operations, or a related specialization. Demonstrated ability to produce strong scholarly research. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduates. Candidates must meet the college’s standards to be Scholarly Academic qualified under AACSB standards. Preferred Qualifications: Very strong research record in supply chain management evidenced by publications in leading peer-reviewed supply chain management journals. Significant research in progress targeted at top SCM journals Work experience with professional responsibilities related to supply chain management. Sustained record of excellence in teaching and the ability to teach a variety of SCM courses at undergraduate, masters, and Ph.D. levels. Department/Program & College Description The Department of Supply Chain Management is composed of 12 tenured and tenure-track faculty members and four-term faculty members. Our department enjoys a strong reputation for faculty research and student focus. We are consistently ranked among the top 10 in the world for empirical supply chain management research. And we offer nationally ranked undergraduate and graduate supply chain management programs. Our department actively engages with industry partners in different ways, including through the Ivy Supply Chain Forum. The Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University, established in 1984, furthers Iowa State University’s land-grant ideals by training students to be knowledgeable and ethical communicators, leaders, collaborators, and problem solvers through impactful research, innovative teaching, and community engagement. With the largest undergraduate business program in the state of Iowa and nationally ranked graduate programs, the Ivy College of Business is home to over 5000 students with a strong growth trajectory. We pride ourselves on our high ethical standards and our drive to promote an environment where all individuals may succeed academically, professionally, and personally. Each member of our community is committed to the college’s mission to link theory with practice for tomorrow’s business leaders. The college offers undergraduate, graduate, and Ph.D. programs and is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). Less than five percent of business schools worldwide receive this accreditation. Our department prides itself on a warm, collegial, and intellectually vibrant environment where faculty support one another's growth and success. We foster a culture of open collaboration, mutual respect, and shared enthusiasm for advancing the field of supply chain management. Faculty members actively engage with one another across research interests, creating a close-knit community that values both scholarly excellence and meaningful relationships. We believe that a positive and supportive work atmosphere is the foundation for producing impactful research and delivering an exceptional educational experience for our students. Department Unit/Website: https://www.ivybusiness.iastate.edu/about-ivy/academic-departments/supply-chain-management/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Statement of Research 3) Statement of Teaching 4) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 5) Contact Information for Three References For guaranteed consideration, applications must be received by August 31, 2026. For questions regarding this position, please contact Search Committee Chair, Dr. Yoshi Suzuki at ysuzuki@iastate.edu For questions regarding this application, please contact employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: July 14, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19606 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-for-Management-and-Entrepreneurship_R19492": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor for Management and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor for Management and Entrepreneurship Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship in the Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University invites applications for a tenure-eligible Assistant Professor position in the fields of Organizational Behavior (OB)/Human Resources (HR) or Entrepreneurship, to begin August 2027. The selected candidate will be expected to publish high-impact research in top-tier Management and/or Entrepreneurship journals. New hires typically teach an undergraduate course in their respective field (OB/HR or Entrepreneurship) in their first years (usually a single prep) and can later teach courses in the MBA or PhD programs. This full-time faculty position is on campus and in person. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Management, Organizational Behavior, Human Resources, Entrepreneurship, or related field prior to starting the position. Demonstrated ability to produce strong scholarly research. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduates. Must meet the college’s standards to be Scholarly Academic Qualified under AACSB Accreditation standards. Preferred Qualifications: A record of publications in high-quality journals and papers presented at major conferences. Significant research in progress targeted at top Management or Entrepreneurship journals. A record of high-quality teaching in the areas of Organizational Behavior/Human Resources or Entrepreneurship. Evidence of engagement with and service to the profession and field. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship is a supportive and productive group of 40+ faculty members (20 tenure-track and 22 term), currently chaired by Chad Murphy. With research interests spanning the areas of OB, HR, Entrepreneurship, Strategy, and Healthcare Management, our faculty have published research in a wide variety of top journals, including the Academy of Management Journal , Academy of Management Review , Strategic Management Journal , Organization Science , Journal of Management , Journal of Applied Psychology , Journal of Business Venturing , Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice , and Strategic Entrepreneurship Journal . The department offers undergraduate degrees in Management, Entrepreneurship, Human Resource Management, and Healthcare Management. The department also offers a Masters in Entrepreneurship and PhD programs in Management as well as Entrepreneurship. The Ivy College of Business was established in 1984. It conducts and shares research to educate tomorrow’s business leaders so they are prepared to overcome multi-disciplinary global, technological, and ethical challenges. The college is accredited by The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). It enrolls over 5,000 students and offers numerous degree programs, including an MBA program, which is ranked #16 in the country among public universities, and an entrepreneurship undergraduate program ranked #9 in the nation.     Tied to the Ivy College of Business is the Pappajohn Center for Entrepreneurship , which serves the ISU campus with educational workshops, experiential learning, student business venture incubation, and ongoing venture support, as well as the Small Business Development Center, which offers startup assistance to students, faculty, and the community. The center has earned prestigious national and international recognition, including the Global Consortium of Entrepreneurship Centers’ Exceptional Contributions in Entrepreneurship Research (2024), the NASDAQ Center for Entrepreneurial Excellence Award (2022), the Accreditation Council for Entrepreneurial and Engaged Universities’ Entrepreneurial University of the Year (Americas) (2023), and the United States Association for Small Business and Entrepreneurship’s Model Program Award (2021). The larger entrepreneurial ecosystem at Iowa State University, under the Vice President for Economic Development & Industry Relations, includes a 500+ acre Research Park that houses more than 100 companies, a year-long startup accelerator, and a top-tier technology transfer research foundation. Department Unit/Website: https://www.ivybusiness.iastate.edu/about-ivy/academic-departments/management-and-entrepreneurship/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Curriculum Vitae 2) Cover Letter 3) Research Statement 4) Teaching Statement 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485.\\ For more information regarding the posted position, please contact the Chair of the search committee, Professor Melissa Chamberlin, at mc6@iastate.edu. Full consideration will be given to applications received before August 16, 2026 . Review of applications will begin on August 16, 2026; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: June 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19492 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Research-Scientist-III_R19337": {
      "title": "Research Scientist III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Research Scientist III Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: The Center for Nondestructive Evaluation (CNDE) at Iowa State University is seeking a Research Scientist III to lead and support innovative research in experimental ultrasonics and nondestructive evaluation (NDE). This role will focus on developing and conducting ultrasonic measurements and imaging techniques using immersion, contact, and non-contact transducers to address real-world challenges across a variety of industries. The successful candidate will collaborate with industry sponsors, government partners, faculty, researchers, and students to advance ultrasonic NDE technologies and microstructure characterization methods. The Research Scientist III will lead experimental research efforts, develop sponsored research proposals, design and validate experiments, analyze results, and publish findings in scholarly journals and conferences. Additional responsibilities include mentoring students, managing and upgrading ultrasonic laboratory equipment, supporting instructional activities, engaging with sponsors and professional organizations, and helping shape future research directions for CNDE. This position requires strong technical expertise, the ability to work independently, and a commitment to advancing the field of ultrasonic nondestructive evaluation. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated experience in the basic theory of ultrasonic methods and wave propagation for a wide range of materials for a variety of NDE applications including imaging and materials characterization Demonstrated experience with ultrasonic measurement hardware, including transducers, motion-control systems, robots, or drones Experience with project management High working knowledge and experience with various relevant ultrasonic measurement equipment M.S. degree (or higher) in mechanical engineering, aerospace engineering, electrical engineering, materials engineering, or a closely related field Ability to work on projects with access restrictions. About the Department: The Center for Nondestructive Evaluation (CNDE) at Iowa State University is a leading research center focused on advancing nondestructive evaluation science and technology. CNDE partners with industry and government to develop innovative inspection and sensing solutions that improve the safety, reliability, and performance of critical materials and systems. The center brings together interdisciplinary experts to solve complex engineering challenges and translate research into practical applications across industries such as aerospace, energy, manufacturing, and defense. To learn more visit the CNDE Website . This is a term position with an end date of June 30, 2028, with the potential for renewal based on funding availability. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Applications received by July 31, 2026, will receive guaranteed consideration; however, the position will remain open until it is filled. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: June 30, 2028 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: June 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19337 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Chemical-Engineering---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor_R19314": {
      "title": "Chemical Engineering - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-03\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Chemical Engineering - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering in the College of Engineering at Iowa State University (ISU) invites applications for the position of tenure-track assistant professor. Exceptional candidates with commensurate experience and proven track record will be considered for tenure and advanced rank of associate professor and professor. Successful candidates will be expected to establish, sustain, and grow a world-class research program that complements or aligns with the department's research strengths through both independent and collaborative efforts. Additionally, the candidate is expected to establish a record of scholarship at the highest levels, contribute to the teaching missions in chemical engineering at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and engage in institutional service as well as service to the profession. Candidates should have strong communication skills and exhibit the potential for long term leadership in supporting the mission of the department, college, and university. The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering is committed to sustaining a collegial, positive, and productive environment for each individual and for the collective benefit of all. All faculty members are expected to exhibit and convey good citizenship within department, college, and university activities, interact collegially, and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in chemical engineering and Ph.D. or equivalent degree in chemical engineering or a closely aligned field Associate professor candidates must also meet the university standards for appointment to the rank, including significant experience/accomplishments in the candidate's area of expertise Professor candidates are required to have national distinction, international recognition, and a substantial scholarly record in their area of expertise, in addition to the aforementioned requirements Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of collaboration and leadership in research and education Published research expertise in fields related to chemical engineering Potential to establish an externally funded research program Ability to teach graduate and undergraduate courses in chemical engineering Ability to mentor research trainees Strong and effective communication skills to a range of audiences  Department/Program & College Description: About the Chemical and Biological Engineering (CBE) Department The CBE Department offers B.S., M.S., M.Eng., and Ph.D. degree programs in chemical engineering. CBE has an undergraduate enrollment of approximately 420 students, a graduate enrollment of 100, 20 scientific staff, 12 administrative staff, and 26 faculty. CBE demonstrates a commitment to broadly supporting faculty, staff, and students in order to achieve University objectives in the areas of research, teaching, and service. With annual research expenditures exceeding $14M, the faculty are involved in a broad range of research topics. The College of Engineering supports the Dual Career Services Program, which serves as a focal point for efforts to find career options for the partners of incoming faculty. Iowa State University and the College of Engineering are invested in increasing the participation of those traditionally under-represented among engineering faculty. About Iowa State University and the Ames Community Iowa State University is classified as a Carnegie Foundation Doctoral/Research University-Extensive and is ranked by U.S. News and World Report as one of the top public universities in the nation. More than 30,000 students are enrolled and are served by over 62,00 faculty and staff. The College of Engineering consists of eight departments with annual research expenditures exceeding $105 million. Iowa State University is located in Ames, IA , a progressive community of 66,000, located approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines , one of the fastest-growing metro areas in the Midwest, and is beaming with community pride and accolades . Iowa State University and the College of Engineering are responsive to the needs of dual-career couples and are dedicated to work-life balance through an array of flexible work policies. Department Unit/Website: For more information about our department's engineering program, see www.cbe.iastate.edu . Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by Tuesday, November 17th, 2026 . All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at http://jobs.iastate.edu to Job Requisition Number R19314 . The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format: 1) Letter of application (including information about the desired rank) that briefly discusses how the candidate meets each of the preferred qualifications. 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information 4) Other documents: - One-page statement of teaching interests and expertise - Three-page research plan Direct questions to Search Committee Chair, Dr. Andrew C. Hillier at hillier@iastate.edu  or call (515) 294-7642. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: June 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19314 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Applied-Linguistics-and-Artificial-Intelligence--AI-_R19304-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Applied Linguistics and Artificial Intelligence (AI)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-28\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Applied Linguistics and Artificial Intelligence (AI) Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of English in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Applied Linguistics and Artificial Intelligence (AI). We seek a faculty member who specializes in at least one of the following areas: the use of AI and language-generating technologies in first- and second- language learning, teaching, or assessment; linguistics-based qualitative and quantitative research on the humanlike language generated by AI; the study of generative AI in human-computer language interaction; or the role of language in the subjective experience of generative AI users. The ideal applicant will have an established or emerging research agenda focusing on AI with expertise relevant to natural language processing (NLP), generative AI, applied linguistics, or a related area. We are especially interested in scholars who are using AI in innovative ways in applied linguistics. At the undergraduate level, the faculty member will teach general courses in linguistics and applied linguistics, courses that serve as electives in the university’s minor in Applied Artificial Intelligence, and new course offerings that integrate AI technologies into linguistics. At the graduate level, the faculty member will have the opportunity to teach courses in applied linguistics and technology, and may contribute to interdisciplinary programs such as Human Computer Interaction, depending on area of specialization. Potential graduate courses include seminars on AI-assisted technologies and generative AI for language learning and assessment, language-based analytics, automated dialogue systems, and speech-driven user interfaces, as well as courses on programming for NLP, computational and/or corpus-based text analysis, statistical analysis of language, or other areas related to the candidate’s expertise. The successful candidate will join a community of faculty in applied linguistics who are exploring the uses and implications of AI in the field. This faculty member will strengthen cross-disciplinary efforts in an area of excellence in the Department of English—the use of technology for teaching, assessing, and researching language. In addition, the faculty member will have opportunities to forge connections with faculty from other department programs specializing in AI, as well contribute to campus-wide strategic initiatives related to trusted innovation and artificial intelligence . The position begins August 16, 2027. All faculty members are expected to exhibit and convey good citizenship within the program, the department, college, and university activities and collegial interactions, and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in applied linguistics, linguistics, natural language processing, computational linguistics, or a related field conferred by time of appointment. Preferred Qualifications: Established or emerging applied linguistic research agenda in the development and/or use of artificial intelligence applications; Demonstrated ability or potential to apply AI in innovative ways for the teaching, assessment, and/or analysis of language; Potential to contribute to the teaching needs of the undergraduate and graduate programs in linguistics and applied linguistics; Experience in teaching and/or assessing language/communication at the college level; Existing record of and/or substantive potential for interdisciplinary collaboration; Demonstrated ability or potential to develop a high-impact, externally funded research program Department/Program & College Description: The Department of English at Iowa State University offers a PhD program in Applied Linguistics and Technology, an MA program in Teaching English as a Second Language/Applied Linguistics, and a BA in Linguistics. As leaders in the advanced study of technology use in language learning and assessment, the Applied Linguistics and Technology program is the ideal context for developing expertise in the development and use of language-related AI applications. In addition to applied linguistics, the Department of English administers graduate and undergraduate programs in English literature, English Education, Rhetoric and Professional Communication, Technical Communication, and Creative Writing. The Department is a growing locus of AI-related expertise, and this position is part of a strategic initiative to further build Iowa State’s research strength and degree programs in key areas. The Department of English is committed to its faculty, staff and students that enrich University objectives in the areas of research, teaching, and service. For more information, see http://www.engl.iastate.edu/ .   ISU is responsive to the needs of dual career couples, is dedicated to work-life balance through an array of policies and is an NSF ADVANCE institution. Department Unit/Website: https://engl.iastate.edu/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of application/cover Letter that addresses the required and preferred qualifications 3) Please attached the following required materials as one document/PDF A research statement (maximum 2 pages) that provides a summary of accomplishments and interests in AI for applied linguistics A teaching statement (maximum 2 pages) that discusses specific undergraduate and graduate courses the candidate would like to teach (existing ISU courses and potential new courses) 4) Contact information for three references 5) Research-based writing sample (for co-authored writing samples, please include a brief description of the candidate’s contributions to the manuscript) If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For guaranteed consideration, applications should be received by August 16, 2026 , but will be accepted until the position is filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: May 28, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19304 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Tenure-Track-or-Clinical-Term-Track-Faculty-Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor---Radiation-Oncology_R18597": {
      "title": "Tenure Track or Clinical Term Track Faculty Assistant-Associate-Full Professor – Radiation Oncology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-28\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure Track or Clinical Term Track Faculty Assistant-Associate-Full Professor – Radiation Oncology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Clinical Sciences, College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University is seeking qualified applicants for a 12-month, full-time, tenured or tenure-track, or renewable clinical term-track position in Radiation Oncology. Applications are being accepted at the levels of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. The successful candidate will be expected to be actively engaged in growing and enhancing the regional prominence of our expanding oncology program and contribute significantly to the teaching, service, and research/scholarship missions of the oncology team, including active participation in outreach activities. Excellent collaborative opportunities for research activities are available within the College of Veterinary Medicine and Iowa State University, as well as the University of Iowa Holden Comprehensive Cancer Center. The successful candidate will be joining a team that includes two medical oncologists (DACVIM), one remote radiation oncologist (DACVR-RO), four medical oncology residents, three technicians, one radiation therapist, and a local consulting team of radiation physicists. The oncology service is very active in research with multiple ongoing clinical studies in both medical and radiation oncology. The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center is a newly constructed and renovated building providing a state-of-the-art teaching, learning, and working facility. Available equipment includes a Varian Clinac iX linear accelerator (with 120 leaf Millenium multileaf collimator and onboard imaging including cone beam CT); ARIA Record and Verify system; Varian Eclipse treatment planning system; 1.5T MRI; and helical multi-slice CT. In addition, plans for a Small Animal Cancer Clinic at the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center are scheduled to begin construction in 2026.  The Small Animal Cancer Clinic will feature dedicated Oncology workspaces, including a centralized lobby, fully equipped exam rooms, clinician and technician offices, and a designated rounds room for student teaching. This position offers a unique opportunity to grow and shape the radiation oncology program at ISU, which has a strong clinical caseload, varied teaching opportunities, and the potential to reinstitute a Radiation Oncology residency training program.  The role also offers flexible opportunities to engage in additional consulting practices, enabling professional growth tailored to individual interests. At the rank of Tenured or Tenure-track Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor, the position will consist of 50- 60% on clinics/hospital service, 25-30% collaborative or independent research, 5-10% teaching professional DVM and graduate student courses, and 5% institutional service. At the rank of Clinical Term Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor, the position will consist of 75-80% on clinics/hospital service, 10- 15% collaborative or independent research, 5% teaching professional DVM and graduate student courses, and 5% institutional service. Actual percentages are flexible depending on the candidate’s expertise and departmental needs. The successful candidate will be expected to develop an active scholarly program. For appointment in the tenure-track, the selected individual should have a strong record of training and experience in radiation oncology, experience with teaching, hypothesis-driven research, and prior grant writing experience. Collaborative or independent research resulting in peer-reviewed publications and external grant submissions is expected. For an individual in the clinical term-track, scholarship could include advancing the discipline of radiation oncology through the creation and dissemination of new knowledge or participating in collaborative research. Additional information on faculty advancement and review can be found here: https://www.provost.iastate.edu/faculty-success/advancement Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM/VMD or equivalent degree  Completion of an approved radiation oncology residency program with credentials accepted by the American College of Veterinary Radiology (RO) to participate in the board certification examination process. State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before the first day of employment ASSOCIATE OR FULL PROFESSOR: Experience in radiation oncology as an ACVR (RO) board-certified radiation oncologist Documented record of productive scholarship (e.g., grant funding), peer-reviewed publications A record of successful clinical and didactic teaching, and resident training CLINICAL TERM ASSOCIATE OR FULL PROFESSOR: Experience in radiation oncology as an ACVR (RO) board-certified radiation oncologist Commensurate experience Preferred Qualifications: Expertise in intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT).  Expertise in stereotactic radiation therapy (SRT).   Board Certification by the American College of Veterinary Radiology (RO)  Experience with didactic, clinical teaching, and resident training.  Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/small-animal/specialty-care/oncology/   Proposed Start Date: March 9, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References For guaranteed consideration, please apply before 07/28/2026.  Position is open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: February 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R18597 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-in-Political-Science_R19287": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Political Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-26\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor in Political Science Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Political Science in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University is seeking a term faculty member at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor to teach in our Law, Justice, and Politics career path and help prepare and mentor pre-law students in the major. Initial appointment length is three years, starting August 16, 2027. An earlier start date of January 1, 2027 will also be considered. Renewal parameters are determined by performance and department need. This position involves a courseload of 6 courses per year, which translates to 75% FTE. The successful candidate will be expected to teach three courses in the fall and three courses in the spring each year. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree or equivalent in political science or closely related disciplines  Minimum of three years of higher education teaching experience in Law, Justice, and Politics or close related disciplines Preferred Qualifications: PhD in political science or closely related field. Demonstrated ability to teach classes in the Department’s Law, Justice and Politics track, including US Constitutional Law.  Demonstrated ability to prepare and mentor pre-law students for law school. Demonstrated ability to teach across American politics and political theory subfields. Evidence of teaching excellence. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Political Science has 19 Tenure-Track and Term faculty, a vibrant MA program which serves over 20 students, and an undergraduate major with over 200 majors.  Department Unit/Website: https://pols.iastate.edu Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter and Contact Information for Three References (uploaded as one pdf) 3) Teaching Statement 4) Sample syllabi (no more than 3) 5) Student Rating of Teaching scores for classes taught For guaranteed consideration, please apply before September 1, 2026. Position is open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: May 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19287 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Freshwater-Ecology_R19216": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Freshwater Ecology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Freshwater Ecology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Ecology, Evolution & Organismal Biology (EEOB) seeks applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Freshwater Ecology. We define freshwater ecology broadly (including lake, river, stream, and wetland ecosystems) but will give preference to candidates whose research includes a pathway for application to lakes and reservoirs in Iowa and the midwestern USA. The successful candidate will develop an externally funded, research-intensive program that contributes foundational knowledge in freshwater ecology—spanning organismal, population, community, ecosystem, or biogeochemical perspectives—while addressing processes and mechanisms relevant to inland waters of agricultural and human-dominated landscapes. Research may be at any biological scale (genes, individuals, communities, populations, ecosystems), with any group of organisms. We are particularly excited about candidates who use innovative empirical, analytical, computational, or modeling approaches in their research. The successful candidate will also contribute to undergraduate and graduate education, including the teaching of a course in aquatic ecology. Research programs that integrate basic ecological discovery with use-inspired or management-relevant questions are particularly encouraged.  There will be opportunities for leveraging ongoing partnerships with state and federal agencies, as well as collaborations with a large assemblage of ISU scientists involved in research on water and environmental resources and with the Iowa Nutrient Research Center, the Iowa Water Center, and the Leopold Center for Sustainable Agriculture, all located at ISU in Ames, IA. This is a tenure-track position in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at the rank of assistant professor. The distribution of effort for this position is 70% research, 25% teaching, and 5% service   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent in ecology, environmental science, limnology, aquatic biology, or closely related fields. Publications in nationally or internationally recognized journals.  Research experience in freshwater ecology.    Preferred Qualifications: A research vision that includes interest in lakes or reservoirs aligned with the mission of a land‑grant university, i.e., research that contributes foundational knowledge with relevance to regional, state, or stakeholder‑defined challenges. Ability to conduct impactful research. Commitment to effective teaching and mentoring. Ability and commitment to contribute to the Department and University’s Principles of Community.    Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology is a collaborative and collegial community of about 80 faculty, graduate students, post-doctoral researchers, and staff addressing a wide range of research questions using multiple, often integrative, approaches that bridge traditional scientific disciplines and spans multiple levels of biological organization.  E EOB is jointly administered by the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) and the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS). The department co-administers undergraduate programs in Biology, Environmental Science, and Genetics and administers the Ecology & Evolutionary Biology Graduate Program. Our faculty participate actively in multiple interdepartmental graduate programs, including Environmental Science, Bioinformatics and Computational Biology, and Genetics and Genomics.    Department Unit/Website: https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Full consideration is guaranteed for applications received by October 4, 2026 . All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu to Job Requisition Number R19216. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: A cover letter A curriculum vitae Contact information for three references Other documents (submitted as one combined PDF) a. A research statement demonstrating research experience and interests in freshwater ecology, a thoughtful research plan, and strategies for funding (up to three pages) b. A statement of teaching and mentoring, demonstrating a thoughtful approach and knowledge of issues related to teaching and learning, including mentoring efforts (up to three pages) For questions about the application process or position, please contact Samantha Smith at samsmith@iastate.edu. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: May 15, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19216 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Chemical-and-Biological-Engineering---Assistant-Associate-Full-Teaching-Professor_R19189": {
      "title": "Chemical and Biological Engineering - Assistant/Associate/Full Teaching Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Chemical and Biological Engineering - Assistant/Associate/Full Teaching Professor Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering, in the College of Engineering at Iowa State University (ISU), invites applications for the full-time (nine-month) renewable term position of Assistant Teaching Professor. Exceptional candidates with commensurate experience and proven track record will be considered for the advanced rank of Associate or Full Teaching Professor. The appointment for this position is anticipated to begin January 1, 2027 or August 16, 2027 and the initial length of the appointment will be three years.   The candidate is expected to provide high quality instruction in core undergraduate chemical engineering courses, including lecture and laboratory courses, as well as support the teaching mission of the university through committee work, mentoring of undergraduate students, and assistance with curriculum and assessment coordination. Candidates should have strong written and oral communication skills and share our departmental mission to provide outstanding education and training in the chemical engineering discipline.   The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering is committed to sustaining a collegial, positive, and productive environment for each individual and the collective benefit of all. All faculty members are expected to interact collegially and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior within department, college, and university activities.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in chemical engineering and doctoral degree in chemical engineering or a related discipline Associate or Full Teaching Professor candidates must also meet the university standards for appointment to the rank, including experience and accomplishments in chemical engineering education   Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience in core undergraduate chemical engineering courses. Development of course and assessment materials. Formal pedagogical training. Ability to communicate effectively in written and oral format. Ability to independently coordinate multiple activities and projects. Industrial experience in the field of chemical engineering. Evidence of collaboration and leadership in engineering education for applicants at the rank of Associate or Full Teaching Professor.   Department/Program & College Description: About the Chemical and Biological Engineering Department The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering (CBE) offers B.S, M.Eng., M.S., and Ph.D. degree programs in chemical engineering. CBE has approximately 400 undergraduate students, 90 graduate students, 20 postdoctoral and scientific staff, 10 administrative staff, and 28 faculty. CBE demonstrates a commitment to broadly supporting faculty, staff, and students to achieve University objectives in the areas of research, teaching, and service.   Department Unit/Website: For more information about our department’s engineering program, see cbe.iastate.edu . Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by September 18, 2026. All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at http://jobs.iastate.edu . The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format: 1) Letter of application that states desired rank and briefly discusses how the candidate meets each of the preferred qualifications 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information 4) Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (not to exceed two pages) Direct questions to Dr. Jennifer Heinen at jmheinen@iastate.edu , or call (515) 294-1891. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: May 13, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19189 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Vet-Tech-I-Temporary---Large-Animal-Intensive-Care-Unit_R18988": {
      "title": "Vet Tech I Temporary – Large Animal Intensive Care Unit",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-05\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Vet Tech I Temporary – Large Animal Intensive Care Unit Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Associate or Bachelor’s degree in a veterinary technology program accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA) or the Canadian Veterinary Medical Association (CVMA), and • Registered, licensed, or certified as a veterinary technician within one year of the start date. Job Description: Job Description: At Iowa State University’s Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC), you’ll work alongside a collaborative team of experts dedicated to excellence in diagnosis, treatment, and education—while making a meaningful impact on the future of veterinary medicine. Under the direction and supervision of a licensed veterinarian, this position provides advanced care for ill and injured equine and farm animal patients. The technician supports a wide range of medical and surgical procedures and plays an integral role in a dynamic teaching environment that includes veterinary students, interns, and residents. This role offers the opportunity to work with a diverse population of large animal species in a fast‑paced hospital setting, contributing to high-quality patient care, efficient hospital operations, and hands-on clinical training. Under the direction and supervision of a licensed Veterinarian, provides intermediate care for ill and injured animal patients or animals used in a research or hospital setting. May perform veterinary care, animal husbandry, and basic technical skills with fourth-year veterinary students. Provides assistance to students, Veterinarians, and investigative staff in their treatment of animals, teaching, or research functions. Position operates within standard guidelines and alternatives that are known, and any deviation from such requires prior approval. Guidance and mentorship can be provided by Veterinary Technician II or III. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Assists with basic nursing care on American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) physical status classification level I and II patients, which are considered healthy or with mild systemic disease. Nursing care to include but not limited to: monitoring body functions (temperature, respiration, heartbeat, amount and frequency of food consumptions, defecation, urination etc.) and noting abnormalities; placing and maintaining intravenous catheters; administering fluids and medications orally, parenterally, and enterally; and performing other basic treatments. • Collects and processes samples for research, diagnostic, and clinical purposes. • Assists with basic preparatory procedures on various animal species and assists staff members in surgical, medical, or laboratory procedure preparation, including instrument and supply set up. • Administers anesthesia and monitors patient response through the recovery period for ASA I-II patients. • Maintains orderly and sanitary work areas for clinical, teaching, and research facilities. • Stocks and organizes patient exam rooms, treatment areas, holding areas and operating rooms. • May assist with entering hospital costs and medical records into the computer to create accurate records for billing accounts. • Assists with set up, inventory, maintenance, security, and repairs for equipment and instruments used in surgical procedures, emergencies and/or lab sessions. • Utilizes ultrasound machines and x-rays, assist with MRI, or other related imaging equipment for patient diagnostics. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of animal health and welfare - animal isolation, sample collection, medical treatment, nursing and monitoring, pre & post-surgical requirements including room and supply preparation. • Knowledge of pharmacology - dosage, calculations, and usage. • Knowledge of animal husbandry - animal feeding, watering, grooming, handling, safe transporting, and environmental requirements. • Knowledge of record maintenance - collecting and recording data. • Knowledge of trimming, clipping, or grooming animals. • Knowledge of teaching and/or demonstration of safe animal handling. • Knowledge of regulatory requirements (Animal Welfare Act, Public Health Service, etc.). • Ability to handle, restrain, move, load, and unload animals. • Ability to administer medication - topical, injectable, oral, and rectal. • Ability to check and interpret vital signs. • Ability to lift, carry, push, or pull up to 70 pounds. • Ability to instruct and demonstrate veterinary techniques in handling, grooming, and nursing animals. • Ability to interact in a professional capacity. • Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others. • Ability to prioritize daily tasks. • Ability to work in high stress environments. • Knowledge of computers, computerized medical record systems, and word processing software, such as Microsoft Word and Excel. Preferred Qualifications Experience with restraining animals. Experience working in veterinary setting. Prior experience with large animals Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: April 27, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: 7601a Original Posting Date: April 14, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R18988 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Radiation-Therapist---PRN---Oncology-Temporary_R18843": {
      "title": "Radiation Therapist – PRN - Oncology Temporary",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-27\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Radiation Therapist – PRN - Oncology Temporary Appointment Type: Professional & Scientific Job Description: The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC) in the College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University is accepting applications for a Radiation Therapist within the hospital’s oncology section. The LVMC provides specialized care and comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion, equine, and food animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. Our clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work collaboratively to provide 24‑hour, state‑of‑the‑art care. This position will provide radiation therapy support during intermittent absences of the full‑time Radiation Therapist. Work hours will be Monday through Friday, 7:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m., on an as‑needed basis for periods of up to 1–2 weeks at a time. Responsibilities include delivering ionizing radiation treatments to veterinary patients in accordance with prescriptions and instructions from the radiation oncologist; assisting dosimetrists and radiation physicists with treatment parameter calculations and computerized dosimetry; maintaining accurate patient records; and providing radiation therapy monitoring across clinical areas. The position will also support functional teaching for interns, residents, technicians, and students. Additional duties include manufacturing individualized immobilization devices and shielding forms, maintaining quality control standards within the oncology department, assisting with preventive maintenance to minimize equipment malfunctions, and making appropriate adjustments to equipment and patients in the event of equipment failure. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong work ethic, be self‑motivated, and able to work both independently and as part of a team. Excellent interpersonal skills, attention to detail, confidentiality, and effective written and verbal communication skills are essential. The ideal candidate will exhibit professional maturity, contribute positively to workplace culture, and demonstrate compassion and empathy toward the clients and patients of the LVMC. The incumbent will be required to work regularly with radiation. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Radiation Therapy or equivalent. Certification by the American Registry of Radiological Technologists in radiation therapy procedures or radiography. Permit to practice in the State of Iowa. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience administering ionizing radiation to patients Experience creating immobilization and shielding devices for patients Experience utilizing stereotactic radiation therapy equipment. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: April 6, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: P&S Temporary Original Posting Date: April 1, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R18843 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Research-Assistant-Professor---Electrical-and-Computer-Engineering_R18719": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Research Assistant Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering ( ece.iastate.edu ), in the College of Engineering at Iowa State University, invites applications for the position of Research Assistant Professor.  This is a 3-year term research faculty position that holds responsibilities primarily contributing to the research mission of the department through scholarly impact and an externally funded research program in the areas of wireless and network systems.  Specifically, besides contributing to the research, education, and innovation projects led by the Center for Wireless, Communities and Innovation ( wici.iastate.edu ), the responsibilities include mentoring graduate and undergraduate students working on research and design projects. Term Faculty hold limited-term, full or part-time, renewable appointments that are not eligible for tenure, but have the potential to be reviewed for advancement into senior ranks.  Research faculty must secure extramural funding to fully support their research program and at least 80% but no more than 90% of their salary, with the remainder salary provided by the department. Successful candidates will have experience that demonstrates exceptional ability or potential to produce scholarship, compete for and secure funding from external sources, and the capability for long-term leadership in their research field.  They will also exhibit excellent communication skills. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph. D. in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications: Research experience and quality publications in advanced wireless and network systems (e.g., safety-critical wireless, URLLC, Open RAN, 6G/NextG); Hands-on experience with cellular network platforms (e.g., O-RAN, srsRAN, OpenAirInterface, Aether/SD-RAN), edge/cloud computing platforms (e.g., Kubernetes, OpenStack), SDN, and/or VNF; Hands-on experience in designing, developing, deploying, and/or operating field-deployed wireless, network, and/or distributed systems; Hands-on experiences in edge/cloud systems management, virtual machines/containers, Linux systems administration, shell scripting, etc; Capability of building systems prototypes based on reference publications and/or open-source software; Knowledge of wireless systems, networked/distributed systems, operating systems, virtualization, systems and network security; Programming skills: Python, C, C++, Java, Web etc. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Iowa State University is home to 60 faculty and is associated with 11 research centers and institutes, for instance, the Center for Wireless, Community and Innovation (WiCI). The department boasts 20 IEEE Fellows, over $15.4M in research expenditures (FY20), and one of the largest ECpE enrollments in the nation. About Iowa State University and the Ames Community Iowa State University is classified as a Carnegie Foundation Doctoral/Research University-Extensive . More than 30,000 students are enrolled and are served by over 6,200 faculty and staff. The College of Engineering consists of eight departments with annual research expenditures exceeding $105 million. Iowa State University is located in Ames, IA , a progressive community of 66,000, located approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines , one of the fastest-growing metro areas in the Midwest, and is beaming with community pride and accolades . Iowa State University and the College of Engineering are responsive to the needs of dual-career couples and are dedicated to work-life balance through an array of flexible work policies. Department Unit/Website:   For more information about our department’s engineering programs, go to www.ece.iastate.edu . Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by May 31st, 2026. All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu . The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter that briefly discusses how the candidate meets each of the preferred qualifications Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information Research statement Inquiries regarding this position may be directed to Hongwei Zhang ( hongwei@iastate.edu ) or Sara K. Harris ( skharris@iastate.edu ). Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: March 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R18719"
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Tenure-Track-or-Clinical-Track-Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor---Dermatology_R18834-1": {
      "title": "Tenure Track or Clinical Track Assistant-Associate-Full Professor – Dermatology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure Track or Clinical Track Assistant-Associate-Full Professor – Dermatology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences in the College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University, located in Ames, Iowa, invites applications for a full-time, clinical-track or tenure-track faculty position in Dermatology. The qualiﬁcations, documented experience, and interests of the selected candidate will determine appointment rank. The primary responsibilities of this position will be to collaborate with the current accomplished team of veterinary dermatologists and allied specialists in the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC). The primary responsibilities of this position will be divided between clinical duty, didactic and laboratory teaching, development of scholarly works, academic service and outreach activities. The percentage of effort dedicated towards these duties is dependent on the applicant, chosen track, department, and service’s needs.  The selected candidate will be committed to the delivery of exceptional patient care, share an enthusiastic dedication to education, and will contribute to the enhancement of the national prominence of the Dermatology and other sections practicing in the LVMC. The successful candidate will also have a collegial, collaborative attitude and willingness to participate in all levels of technician, student, and house ofﬁcer education. The ideal candidate will be highly motivated, innovative, and possess excellent communication skills and experience working with a varied population. Furthermore, the candidate will demonstrate professional maturity with a leadership style that contributes to a positive culture and have a compassionate and empathetic nature towards the clients and patients of the LVMC. All employees are expected to exhibit and convey good citizenship within the program, the department, college, university activities, collegial interactions, and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior.   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent degree. Successful completion of an American College of Veterinary Dermatology (or equivalent) approved residency training program.  Candidates in an approved dermatology residency training program will also be considered and are encouraged to apply. State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before the ﬁrst day of employment. In addition, the following positions will require: ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR, CLINICAL ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR, FULL PROFESSOR OR CLINICAL FULL PROFESSOR: Candidates must meet the requirements commensurate for each rank at the ISU College of Veterinary Medicine regarding Professional Practice, Teaching, Research and Scholarly Activities, and Institutional Service .    Preferred Qualifications: Board certiﬁed by the American College of Veterinary Dermatology (ACVD), European College of Veterinary Dermatology (ECVD), Fellows of the Dermatology Chapter of the Australian and New Zealand College of Veterinary Scientists (DCANZCVS) or the Asian College of Veterinary Dermatology (AICVD). An advanced degree (MS, PhD, or equivalent degree). Documented experience in veterinary dermatology practices and standards of care. A record of scholarship obtained through manuscript publication/preparation; or national scholarly, clinical, educational presentations; or evidence of having applied for, received, or completed grants/funding. Experience with clinical instruction of professional students or other trainees.   Department/Program & College Description: The Dermatology Section of the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center is housed in an 8-room suite that includes a general treatment room, a surgical suite for laser surgery and video-otoscopy, a microscope room with multiple Olympus microscopes, a dedicated rounds/teaching room, a technician/resident office, and two dedicated examination rooms designated for the Dermatology Service.  The service works closely with allied specialty services and the primary care service.  Additionally, the Dermatology Service has a generous endowment that allows for outstanding annual funding for equipment, travel, and resident activities.  A full description of equipment and virtual tour may be found here .    Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vcs Proposed Start Date: June 1, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: June 1, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References (References will not be contacted without prior notice to the candidate) 4) Teaching Philosophy Statement: The letter of application should include a statement of career goals, philosophy of leadership and teaching, and vision statement regarding veterinary dermatology. For guaranteed consideration, please apply before May 30, 2026 .  Position will remain open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: March 18, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R18834"
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Adjunct-Assistant-Professor-of-Economics-of-Agriculture-Processing-and-Contracts_R19914": {
      "title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor of Economics of Agriculture Processing and Contracts",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Adjunct Assistant Professor of Economics of Agriculture Processing and Contracts Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Economics seeks to hire a non-tenure-track Adjunct Assistant Professor in Agricultural Economics with interests in the economics of agricultural processing and agricultural contracts. The approximate division of responsibilities for this position is 15% research, 25% teaching, 55% extension and outreach, and 5% institutional service. The appointment term is three years, renewable upon satisfactory performance. The home college for the position is the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences. The individual in this position is expected to develop a nationally recognized research and outreach program in the economics surrounding agricultural processing, including contract design and industrial organization. The research and outreach program will be expected to address critical issues for Iowa’s evolving agricultural processing sector.  The individual will maintain one or more active projects under the auspices of the Iowa Agriculture and Home Economics Experiment Station. The successful candidate will be expected to collaborate across departments, extension units, and university centers. The research and teaching activities are envisioned to be synergistic with the outreach activities. A natural outcome of these activities will be applied outreach materials targeting producers, agribusiness professionals, and other relevant groups; original research in agricultural economics leading to publications in appropriate refereed journals and other professional outlets; and presentations at professional conferences. The successful candidate will be expected to generate extramural funds to support outreach and research activities. Opportunities will exist to serve on graduate academic plan committees. The candidate will also possess excellent written and verbal communication skills. The teaching assignment is expected to be approximately 2 courses per year. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Economics, Agricultural Economics or related field   Preferred Qualifications: Strong training in microeconomics and quantitative methods Strong evidence of research interests in one or more of the following fields: agricultural processing, contract design, and industrial organization Demonstrated ability to communicate economic ideas in public forums Demonstrated potential for accomplishment in extension and outreach Demonstrated potential for accomplishment in college teaching of commodity marketing and risk analysis Demonstrated potential for accomplishment in research Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Economics, with approximately 35 faculty, has a long tradition of excellence in education, research, and engagement with the community. Our undergraduate program is the academic home to about 500 students in three different majors. Our graduate program offers M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in economics and agricultural economics, and has placed graduates in vital positions in academia, government, and industry throughout the world. Faculty research covers a broad spectrum ranging from theoretical analyses to applied policy studies. The department is jointly administered by the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences, and the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. The Iowa State College of Agriculture and Life Sciences is one of the world’s leading institutions of agriculture, with more than 160 years of leadership in science, education and extension. The college educates future leaders, conducts mission-oriented research and shares new knowledge for the betterment of Iowa and the world. The college is one of eight colleges at Iowa State University, which is one of the most influential land grant universities in the nation. Central to Iowa State University’s mission, the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS) is a collaborative, vibrant community of faculty, students and staff, committed to learning, research, and innovation. With 21 departments, one professional school, 49 majors, and over 20 cross- disciplinary programs, LAS faculty support student success and engage in pathbreaking research across a wide range of fields Department Unit/Website: https://www.econ.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. To guarantee full consideration, applications should be received by  November 1, 2026 . All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online by submitting or attaching the following:  1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application addressing your qualifications for the position 3) Recent example of research (job paper) 4) Contact information for at least three references 5) Contact Information including email addresses for three references to provide Letters of Recommendation (these may be the same contacts as item #4 or different). If you have questions about this position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, John Crespi, at jcrespi@iastate.edu . If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19914 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Veterinary-Teaching-Hospital-Assistant-II_R19780": {
      "title": "Veterinary Teaching Hospital Assistant II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Veterinary Teaching Hospital Assistant II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Customer service or receptionist experience which totals two years. • Knowledge of medical terminology or animal disease symptoms, or, Post high school education that provides the knowledge and skills to perform the job duties. • Data entry skills. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Are you passionate about animals and providing outstanding customer service? Do you thrive in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment where every day brings new challenges and opportunities to make a difference? If so, we want YOU to join our veterinary hospital team as a Large Animal  Veterinary Teaching Hospital Assistant II ! Hours:  The position requires working Monday through Friday from 6:30 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. Some holiday shifts will also be required. Why You’ll Love This Position: Meaningful Work:  Help clients navigate their pet’s care journey and play a vital role in their health and happiness. Team Atmosphere:  Collaborate with skilled doctors, students, and support staff in a positive and supportive environment. Exciting Responsibilities:  Take on important tasks such as client communication, administrative duties, and service coordination to keep every day engaging. Fast-Paced Energy:  Stay active and focused in a role that keeps you on your toes with 200+ calls a day and a variety of tasks to accomplish. Key Job Duties Customer Service/Client Communication Welcome clients and update patient information in the hospital database. Schedule appointments, handle emergencies, and provide detailed instructions for visits. Explain hospital policies, payment procedures, and consent requirements. Manage high call volumes, transfer calls to appropriate departments, and address client inquiries. Collect deposits for inpatient care and explain credit and billing policies. Administrative Tasks Manage communications for faculty, students, and staff. Train and supervise students in office procedures and medical record handling. Support doctors and students by providing access to client records, contact details, and visit history. Service Coordination Organize and maintain medical records. Deliver food, supplies, and lab samples. Prepare and send out billing statements and other client communications. Maintain the reception area with necessary forms and supplies. Sort and distribute mail and assist with database updates. Join us and be part of a team that makes a real difference in the lives of animals and their families. Apply today to become a  Veterinary Teaching Hospital Assistant  and start a career you’ll be proud of! Required Minimum Qualifications: Customer service or receptionist experience totaling two years. Knowledge of medical terminology or animal disease symptoms, or post-high school education that provides the knowledge and skills to perform the job duties. Data entry skills. Preferred Qualifications: Prior receptionist experience within a large or small animal clinic. Customer service experience in high-volume or fast-paced environments. Experience with payment processing, invoicing and/or bookkeeping. Familiarity with scheduling systems or client management software. Associate's degree or coursework in veterinary technology, animal science, or related field. Department/Program & College Description: The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center at Iowa State University is a premier veterinary teaching hospital providing expert specialty, emergency, and routine care for small and large animals while supporting veterinary education, research, and outreach Department Unit/Website: Home - Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter   If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: March 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: 08 Original Posting Date: August 17, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 18, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19780 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Sports-Media-and-Communication_R19927": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Sports Media and Communication",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Sports Media and Communication Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Greenlee School of Journalism and Communication in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa seeks a dynamic candidate for an Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of sports media and communication to engage in research, teaching, and leadership related to its new Sports Media and Communication (SMC) major. The SMC program instructs students with hands-on training in creating content using industry-standard and emerging digital tools, including areas such as broadcasting, writing, social media and public relations. The successful candidate will hold a Ph.D. (or relevant terminal degree) by the time of appointment or a master’s degree with at least five years of full-time professional experience. Preferred qualifications include relevant teaching experience and demonstrated ability, commensurate with rank, to produce nationally/internationally recognized, peer-reviewed scholarship or recognized creative work. As a student-centered, research-intensive (R1) university of science and technology in the Big 12, ISU offers high-level opportunities for collaboration and scholarly analysis of sports communication. Applicants at all ranks, including recent graduates, are encouraged to apply. This position is a full-time (9-month) appointment starting August 16, 2027. The adherence to programmatic goals and curriculum objectives is required, as the school is accredited by the Accrediting Council on Education in Journalism and Mass Communications (ACEJMC). Required Minimum Qualifications: M.S. in journalism, advertising, public relations, or related field and five years of relevant, full-time professional experience, or Ph.D. or relevant terminal degree in journalism, advertising, public relations, or related field. Additionally, for Associate/Full rank: Associate/Full Professor candidates must also meet the university standards for appointment to the rank, including a record of peer-reviewed scholarship or juried creative works in the candidate’s area of expertise commensurate with rank. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated teaching excellence in higher education Demonstrated ability to teach a variety of courses in sports media and/or advertising, digital storytelling, journalism, or public relations. Demonstrated ability, commensurate with rank, to produce nationally/internationally recognized, peer-reviewed scholarship or recognized creative work Professional experience beyond the required amount related to sports media and communication in journalism, advertising, public relations, or related field.  Department/Program & College Description: The Greenlee School of Journalism and Communication has a dynamic ACEJMC-accredited undergraduate program and a strong Master’s program. The School has undergraduate majors in Journalism and Mass Communication, Advertising, Public Relations, Sports Media and Communication, and Digital Storytelling. Additional information about the School is available at www.greenlee.iastate.edu. Department Unit/Website: www.greenlee.iastate.edu   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References For guaranteed consideration, please apply before October 18, 2026 . Position is open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 15, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19927 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/High-Voltage-Electrician-I_R19977": {
      "title": "High Voltage Electrician I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: High Voltage Electrician I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Must have a high school diploma or GED • Six years of experience in the trade, including apprenticeship, of which two years must be working with high voltage (over 600 volts) or successfully completed the site-specific high voltage training program for the High Voltage Electrician I. Job Description: Are you an experienced High or Medium Voltage Electrician looking for a great career move with a consistent work that fosters work-life balance? Step up to a role where your journey-level skills can make a real impact! We’re seeking a skilled professional to join our team, installing, maintaining, and repairing high-voltage electrical distribution systems (5kV to 15kV). Generous benefits starting from Day 1 All holidays off Opportunity to work on a dynamic team that’s committed to maintaining a safe, efficient, and thriving campus environment. About the Role: Installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting medium-voltage distribution systems, including transformers, generators, switchgear, and control systems. Repairing and calibrating equipment like circuit breakers, relays, substation gear, and more. Leading on safety protocols, coordinating outages, and generating switching procedures. Conducting power system tests and using tools like phase meters, hi-potential testers, and infrared thermometers. About You: In-depth knowledge of electrical/electronic theory and techniques. Strong ability to read schematics and electrical documentation. Excellent communication skills to work effectively with colleagues and apprentices. Solid experience in electrical maintenance and installation. About Us: At Facilities Planning and Management, we’re all about making campus a safe, efficient, and welcoming place for everyone. Our Utilities Services team plays a vital role in keeping our infrastructure in top shape, ensuring smooth operations across campus. Preferred Qualifications State of Iowa Electrical license or other applicable electrical certifications Journeyman lineman three-phase electrical trade experience Experience installing and maintaining medium voltage system equipment up to 15,000 volts Experience splicing/terminating medium voltage cables Experience working on underground electrical systems and in confined spaces Experience using high voltage electrical system testing and diagnostic equipment About the department – Utility Services Utility Services is a 24-hour, 365-day-a-year operation dedicated to meeting the energy needs of the Iowa State University community. The department operates and maintains four energy production facilities, as well as an extensive network of utility distribution systems that serve the entire Iowa State campus. Through a commitment to operational excellence, safety, and sustainability, Utility Services works to provide reliable, economical, and environmentally responsible utility services that support the university's teaching, research, and outreach mission. Its primary goal is to safely deliver dependable utility services while continuously advancing sustainability and efficiency across campus operations. Copy and paste the link below to learn more about our team! https://www.fpm.iastate.edu/utilities/energy_production_facilities.asp Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots, calibrates, repairs and replaces high voltage electric distribution systems and related equipment, including but not limited to switchgear, circuit breakers, relays, substation equipment, solid state control systems, power and distribution class transformers, generators, capacitor banks, solid state meters, protection and monitoring systems, cable and conduit. Jobs may require one day to several weeks to complete depending on complexity.  • Energizes and operates high voltage electrical distribution equipment. • Determines jobsite work sequences and safety procedures required, procures materials, coordinates outages, completes work, and places systems back into service. • Generates basic switching procedures to allow de-energization of portions of the electrical distribution systems to safely isolate equipment to complete required tasks. • Tests power systems utilizing equipment such as phase meters, hi-potential testers, meggers, and infrared thermometers. • Assists in directing the work of apprentices and other workers.  • May perform other electrical duties as required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities •  Knowledge of the principles of electrical theory, methods and techniques used in the high voltage electrical trade.  • Knowledge of the tools and equipment of the high voltage electrical and electronic trade and detailed skill in their safe use, proper care and maintenance.  • Knowledge of the trade occupational hazards and safety precautions while working in confined spaces, aerial or elevated locations, extreme temperatures, excavations, and other environmental caused conditions.  • Knowledge of electrical codes, utility standards, and safety programs as governed by rules, regulations and guidelines of OSHA, EPA, NFPA, ANSI, equipment manufacturers, and others.  • Knowledge of proper bending and lifting techniques and ability to lift and carry at least 100 pounds.  • Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing with other department personnel, vendors and suppliers, students, staff, and the general public.  • Ability to plan and perform work involving the installation, modification and repair of new and existing high voltage electrical systems and related electronic control and protective equipment with minimal guidance by others while maintaining work continuity when unplanned events cause disruptions.  • Skill to read, understand and interpret installation manuals, specifications, and construction drawings for the basic installation, maintenance and operation of high voltage equipment. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5073a Original Posting Date: September 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 29, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19977 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Biomedical-Engineering-Program---Assistant-Associate-Full-Teaching-Professor_R19957": {
      "title": "Biomedical Engineering Program - Assistant/Associate/Full Teaching Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Biomedical Engineering Program - Assistant/Associate/Full Teaching Professor Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Biomedical Engineering Program in the College of Engineering at Iowa State University (ISU) invites applications for a full-time (nine-month) renewable term position of Assistant Teaching Professor. Exceptional candidates with commensurate experience and proven track record will be considered for the advanced rank of Associate or Full Teaching Professor. This appointment for this position is anticipated to begin August 16, 2027 and the initial length of the appointment will be three years. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the teaching and administration of the biomedical engineering capstone design course. The successful candidate will also be expected to teach undergraduate courses in prosthetics/orthotics/robotics, biomedical engineering laboratory courses or other courses in the biomedical engineering program as needed. As a faculty member, the successful candidate will be expected to engage in institutional service and/or service to the profession. Candidates should have strong communication skills, share our commitment to excellence in engineering education, and exhibit the potential for long-term leadership in supporting the mission of the program, college, and university. Minimum Required Qualifications (Assistant Teaching Professor): One of: Bachelor’s degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline and 5 years of relevant work experience Master’s degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline and 3 years of relevant work experience Doctoral degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline. Minimum Required Qualifications (Associate Teaching Professor): Record of teaching experience and one of: Bachelor’s degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline and 10 years of relevant work experience. Master’s degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline and 8 years of relevant work experience. Doctoral degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline and 5 years of relevant work experience. Minimum Required Qualifications (Teaching Professor): Record of teaching experience and one of: Bachelor’s degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline and 15 years of relevant work experience. Master’s degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline and 13 years of relevant work experience. Doctoral degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline and 10 years of relevant work experience. Closely related engineering disciplines for this position include: chemical, mechanical, materials or electrical engineering.   Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Biomedical Engineering Industrial or teaching experience in biomedical engineering design, including FDA regulations Teaching experience in biomedical engineering laboratory experiences Teaching, research or industrial experience in prosthetics, orthotics or robotics Evidence of ability to communicate with a range of audiences Evidence of collaboration and leadership in engineering education Department/Program & College Description: About the Biomedical Engineering Program The Biomedical Engineering Program is an interdepartmental undergraduate program that is administratively housed in the Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering. It was launched in the fall of 2023. It currently has an enrollment of 200 students and is moving toward classes between 60 and 70 students. The Biomedical Engineering Program is committed to a student-centered education that emphasizes experiential learning and a strong foundation in engineering, biology, and health sciences. Unique collaborations with the Veterinary College showcase our strengths in the areas of drug and vaccine delivery, biomechanics across multiple scales and biosensing that provide our students with a strong interdisciplinary education.   Department Unit/Website: For more information about our department’s program, see https://www.engineering.iastate.edu/bme/ . Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by December 1st, 2026 . All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu to Job Requisition Number R19957 . 1) Letter of application (including information about the desired rank) that briefly discusses how the candidate meets the preferred qualifications 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Contact Information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information 4) Two-page teaching statement including teaching experience, interest and philosophy Direct questions to Ian Schneider at ians@iastate.edu , or call (515) 294-4050. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19957 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Electrician-II_R19974": {
      "title": "Electrician II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Electrician II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Requires State of Iowa Class A Journeyman Electrician license with at least four years as an apprentice plus two years of experience as a journeyman electrician; or State of Iowa Class B Journeyman Electrician license with eight years in the electrical trade in maintenance or construction. • Must possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. Job Description: Under general supervision, applies knowledge, skills and abilities at the journey level to install and repair electrical systems and equipment (generally less than 600V). Demonstrates Journeyman Electrician qualifications, training, experience and technical knowledge. Responsible for the coordination and accomplishment of maintenance, operations and modifications. Performs the duties peculiar to, and normally required in, the trade of electrician, following recognized procedures and techniques for such work. Utilizes special tools, equipment, and processes (such as insulation testers, thermal imaging cameras and Thermal/Infrared (TIR) Predictive Testing procedures) to collect, perform initial diagnostics, and respond to data through established guidelines for preventive and predictive maintenance to ensure equipment reliability. About the department – Utility Services Utility Services is a 24-hour, 365-day-a-year operation dedicated to meeting the energy needs of the Iowa State University community. The department operates and maintains four energy production facilities, as well as an extensive network of utility distribution systems that serve the entire Iowa State campus. Through a commitment to operational excellence, safety, and sustainability, Utility Services works to provide reliable, economical, and environmentally responsible utility services that support the university's teaching, research, and outreach mission. Its primary goal is to safely deliver dependable utility services while continuously advancing sustainability and efficiency across campus operations. Copy and paste the link below to learn more about our team! https://www.fpm.iastate.edu/utilities/energy_production_facilities.asp About the role: Maintain and repair campus site lighting and low-voltage power distribution systems. Install conduit, cable, switchboards, panels, and circuit breakers. Perform maintenance and installation of variable frequency drives, campus mass warning signals, traffic/pedestrian control signals, utility electric meters, and mechanical flow meters. Utilize utility locating equipment to identify and troubleshoot underground infrastructure. Assist Utility High Voltage staff with cable pulls, switch replacements, and vault maintenance. Read and interpret schematics, drawings, and instruction books. Communicate effectively, professionally, and positively with colleagues and campus community members. You will receive training to use utility locating equipment for the identification and troubleshooting of underground infrastructure Install and maintain motor starters and motor control centers. Perform maintenance on circuit breakers protecting circuits that range from 120V to 15,000V. Other duties as assigned. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Performs all duties listed under Electrician I. • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots, repairs and replaces 600 volts and less electrical distribution systems and related equipment, including but not limited to main panel board control systems, programmable controls, solid state control systems, step up and down transformers, current and potential transformers, protective field devices, line monitoring equipment and VFD’s. • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots and repairs control systems including lighting, programmable controllers, and building heating and cooling system programmable controllers. • Performs preventive maintenance on electrical equipment systems and control systems. • As required, will commission 600 volts and less electrical distribution systems and related equipment, and control systems. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of the occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trade. • Knowledge of safety precautions mandated by OSHA, NFPA, NEC and the EPA. • Demonstrates all knowledge, skills, and abilities listed under Electrician I. • Knowledge of electrical control systems, including variable frequency drives. • Ability to use and interpret specialty tools and equipment used to troubleshoot electrical equipment and systems. • Ability to plan and perform work involving the installation, modification, troubleshooting and repair of new and existing control systems and related equipment. • Ability to work in all types of environmental conditions or in areas where there is exposure to excessive noise, dirt, and fumes and at elevated heights from ladders, scaffolds, or hydraulic lifts. Preferred Qualifications -Experience working with Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs), including troubleshooting and installation -Experience with commercial/industrial and three-phase electrical systems -Familiarity with Building Automation Systems (e.g., Metasys) -Experience using electrical system testing and diagnostic tools such as insulation testers, thermal imaging, or power analyzers Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5070a Original Posting Date: September 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 29, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19974 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Lecturer-for-Interior-Design_R19965": {
      "title": "Lecturer for Interior Design",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Lecturer for Interior Design Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Interior Design, in the College of Design at Iowa State University (ISU), invites applications for the position of Lecturer. The position will teach undergraduate studios and lecture courses addressing topics such as the design process, spatial design, materials and finishes, lighting design, color theory and applications, and cultural and historical contexts. Teaching responsibilities will also include integration of technologies and communication methods related to the field, such as Revit, AutoCAD, rendering software, building codes, and construction documentation. In addition to teaching, this position will serve as a professional mentor to students supporting their academic and professional growth through guidance and engagement in design education. The appointment for this position is anticipated to begin January 1, 2027, and the initial length of the appointment will be part-time for the Spring 2027 semester. The candidate will be expected to contribute meaningfully to the department's teaching mission and participate in institutional service. We're looking for individuals with strong communication skills who share our commitment to fostering excellence. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the potential for long-term leadership in advancing the goals of the department, college, and university. The Department of Interior Design is committed to sustaining a collegial, positive, and productive environment for each individual and the collective benefit of all. All faculty members are expected to exhibit and convey good citizenship within department, college, and university activities, interact collegially and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior.   Required Minimum Qualifications: A Master's degree   Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of current professional standards, practices, and trends in commercial interior design, including client collaboration and documentation processes. Demonstrated experience in the execution of professional interior design projects, including the application of building codes, preparation of construction documents, project management, and presentation materials. Experience in curriculum development, implementing assessment strategies, and using student learning outcomes to inform and enhance teaching effectiveness. NCIDQ certification, certification in progress, or eligibility for certification Proficiency with industry-standard design technologies, including Revit, AutoCAD, and rendering or visualization software.   Department/Program & College Description: About the Interior Design Department The Department of Interior Design is a vibrant program in the College of Design at Iowa State University, along with Architecture, Industrial Design, Graphic Design, Art and Visual Culture, Landscape Architecture, and Urban Planning and Development. The Department of Interior Design is a CIDA accredited program that offers a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Interior Design (BFA), a Master of Arts in Interior Design (MA), a Master of Fine Arts in Interior Design (MFA). The department offers experiential learning in immersive study abroad programs, a professional internship program, many interdisciplinary opportunities, and strategic collaborations with other highly ranked colleges and departments.   Department Unit/Website: For more information about our department’s program, see: https://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/interior-design/ Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by October 15, 2026. All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu to Job Requisition Number R19965. The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format: 1) An application letter addressing how the candidate's experience and qualifications align with some or all of the preferred qualifications 2) A curriculum vitae or professional resume 3) Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information 4) Other documents: A professional portfolio showcasing relevant work in interior design. Applications may include examples from professional projects and/or teaching examples. A one-page teaching statement, describing your teaching philosophy, approach, and potential contributions to student learning. Applications with limited or no formal teaching experience should focus on their perspectives and ideas. Direct questions to Kotaro Nakamura, Chair, Department of Interior Design, at kotaro@iastate.edu. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 22, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19965 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-of-Mathematics_R19959": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Mathematics Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Mathematics in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the areas of discrete mathematics and optimization inclusive of operations research, starting August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will have a strong research portfolio and demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate mathematics courses; developing and maintaining an excellent, internationally recognized research program; advising and mentoring students; contributing service to the department and the broader mathematical community; and pursuing external research funding.  Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD or equivalent degree in mathematics or a related discipline by the appointment start date Research background in discrete mathematics, optimization or operations research Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated potential for superior achievements in research in the areas of discrete mathematics and optimization inclusive of operations research. Demonstrated ability to collaborate with other researchers and work with students. Excellent teaching record as evidenced by at least one recommendation letter specifically addressing teaching. Accomplishment in research in addition to the Ph.D., typically achieved through a postdoctoral position.  Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Mathematics resides in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences offering B.S., B.A., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees in Mathematics and Applied Mathematics.  The Department is also active in interdepartmental programs in Data Science at the undergraduate level as well as Bioinformatics and Computational Biology, Human-Computer Interaction, and Information Assurance at the graduate level.  The department participates in many interdisciplinary research collaborations, including partnerships with faculty in bio-sciences, computer science, and several engineering programs.  The Department of Mathematics has 45 faculty professionals, 70 Ph.D. students, 5 postbaccalaureate and M.S. students, and 240 undergraduate mathematics majors and minors.  We have strong research and educational programs in discrete mathematics, algebra, logic, analysis and probability, numerical analysis, mathematical biology, geometric analysis and PDE’s.  In addition to our faculty, we have a robust postdoctoral program with 10 associates.  The Department has over $2 million in active awards, and we contribute to active interdisciplinary research and training grants totaling approximately $5 million.  Our tenure eligible faculty regularly teach graduate courses; annually the Department offers 35 graduate courses.  The faculty also engage in weekly research seminars—currently the department offers 10 active seminars.  The teaching load for untenured faculty is 3 courses per year.  The standard teaching load for tenured faculty is 4 courses per year. Highly productive research active faculty have opportunities for course releases. Iowa State University is located in Ames, Iowa, a vibrant mid-sized community offering an exceptional quality of life, a stable economy, and a welcoming environment for new professionals. Department Unit/Website :  https://math.iastate.edu/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Application materials will be collected through both the ISU Application portal and mathjobs.org.  A complete application will consist of the following documents: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three Professional References 4) Statement of Research Interests 5) Statement of Teaching Interests 6) Four recommendation letters (one of which should address the candidate’s teaching), submitted to mathjobs.org. Please attach the documents in items 1-5 through the ISU Application portal as individual PDF files. Please attach all documents in the required documents section. The documents in items 1, 2, 4-6 will also be submitted through mathjobs.org .  Please find the job posting under the heading of Iowa State University.  Complete the AMS cover sheet and ensure that your references have submitted their recommendation letters to mathjobs.org . For guaranteed consideration, please apply before October 31, 2026.   Position is open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19959 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Track-Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor---Clinical-Educator_R19963": {
      "title": "Clinical Track Assistant/Associate/Full Professor – Clinical Educator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Track Assistant/Associate/Full Professor – Clinical Educator Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS) in the College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University, located in Ames, Iowa, is seeking qualified candidates for a full-time, term (clinical-track) faculty position to support the clinical education of professional students in veterinary medicine and surgery. The qualifications, documented experience, and interests of the selected candidate will determine appointment rank. The successful candidate will have a unique opportunity to teach throughout all four years of the veterinary curriculum as a member of the Surgery, Anesthesia, and Community Outreach team. Primary efforts in this position will focus on didactic and laboratory surgical teaching, patient care, course organization and development, and outcomes assessment. This position will also support clinical skill development in the Clinical Skills laboratory.  Some educational responsibilities occur after standard business hours and after-hours obligations are shared with another faculty member. The remaining efforts will be in collaborative clinical and educational research activities and institutional service. The percentage effort associated with each professional obligation will be determined by mutual agreement between the candidate and the Department Chair of VCS. We are seeking an individual with a collegial, collaborative philosophy and dedication to participate in all levels of student and technician education. The successful candidate will be self-motivated, innovative, adaptable, team-orientated, and possess excellent interpersonal communication skills.  Optimal professional skills and knowledge for the position would include: Documented post-graduate training experiences in surgical procedures commonly performed in general practice or in shelter organizations Experience with basic surgery skills in academic, private practice, or shelter settings  Knowledge of current AAHA Anesthesia Guidelines Experience with small animal primary patient care including pre- and post-operative care management and managing medical or surgical complications in clinical patients Documented excellence in compassionate patient care  Collegial interactions with colleagues and team members   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent degree Three years of clinical practice experience in an academic, private practice, or shelter setting State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before the first day of employment   Preferred Qualifications: Additional years of clinical experience   Documented surgical experiences in an academic, private practice, or shelter setting.    Documented experiences in didactic and/or clinical teaching  Documented post-graduate continuing education in surgery or shelter medicine and surgery  Advanced certifications (ex. Fear Free)  Board certification or eligibility in either an American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA) or European Board of Veterinary Specialization (EBVS) acknowledged clinical specialty  An advanced degree (MS, PhD, or equivalent degree)  Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences provides significant clinical educational training for professional students. The educational opportunities for students have been expanded within the last few years to enhance clinical competency achievement. The Surgery, Anesthesia, and Community Outreach team focuses on producing “practice ready” graduates with competent veterinary skills. The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center is a state-of-the-art facility designed to provide specialized care and comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. Our clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work collaboratively to provide 24-hour, high-quality care to animal patients. As the nation’s first public veterinary school, Iowa State University’s College of Veterinary Medicine takes pride in its heritage while shaping the future of veterinary professional practice, education, research and service.  Ames, Iowa is a progressive community of 60,000, located approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines, and recently voted one of the best college towns in the nation.   Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vcs https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vcs/academics/community-outreach/ https://vetmed.iastate.edu/future-dvm-students/prospective-student-information/vm4-species-track-options/years-1-4/small-animal-option/surgical-training / Proposed Start Date: July 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: June 30, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three (3) external to Iowa State References  For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before November 6, 2026. This position is open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19963 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Motor-Vehicle-Operator-I---Temporary_R19960": {
      "title": "Motor Vehicle Operator I - Temporary",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Motor Vehicle Operator I - Temporary Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. • Possession of Iowa Motor Vehicle Operator’s license. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Operates motor vehicles to transport materials, supplies, etc. to and from offices, job sites and other specifies destinations upon instructions from dispatcher or according to established routes. Loads, unloads, and secures cargo. Hauls trash, refuse, and debris to disposal sites as required. Services vehicles, both interior and exterior, including cleaning and washing with power equipment, refueling and other minor items of vehicle maintenance as required. Performs as a Laborer when not driving. Responds to calls for emergency service, including snow removal, as required. Candidates should have: Ability to lift up to 100 pounds. Ability to operate moving equipment such as pallet movers and forklifts. Ability to safely operate and insure proper maintenance of vehicles. Knowledge of proper cargo loading and securing techniques. Knowledge of the rules and regulations governing operation of state vehicles. Knowledge of motor vehicle laws. Preferred Qualifications: Class D Chauffeur’s License Endorsement. Experience operating as a chauffeur using a passenger vehicle, light truck, or delivery vehicle. Customer service experience. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: June 30, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: 0004a Original Posting Date: September 18, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19960 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-in-Art-Education_R19942": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Art Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor in Art Education Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Art and Visual Culture (AVC) in the College of Design at Iowa State University (ISU), in coordination with the School of Education in the College of Health and Human Sciences, invites applications for a part-time (50% FTE) position at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor in Art Education, with salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. The appointment is anticipated to begin in January 2027 (Spring 2027 semester) and to continue through December 31, 2027, with the possibility of renewal contingent on performance, curricular need, and funding. Art education at Iowa State prepares pre-service teachers to teach visual art across K–12 settings through art-centered, interdisciplinary, and community-engaged approaches. The successful candidate will teach two undergraduate courses each semester, in consultation with the Chair, primarily in the department’s art education (ARTED) offerings—including ARTED 2090 (Methods of Teaching in and Through Art) and ARTED 2110 (Introduction to Art Education). These courses introduce discipline-specific and interdisciplinary methods that foster creativity, collaborative learning, aesthetic sensitivity, and appreciation of art across cultures. Teaching responsibilities include preparing syllabi, course materials, and assessment tools; holding office hours; and participating in relevant program and faculty meetings. Pedagogically adaptive and innovative approaches to teaching are expected. The School of Education offers a Master of Arts in Teaching (M.A.T.) in Secondary Education, which now includes an art endorsement area at the 5–12 level. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to contribute to curriculum planning for the art endorsement and to the continued growth of art education at Iowa State. The Department of Art and Visual Culture is committed to sustaining a collegial, positive, and productive environment for each individual and the collective benefit of all. All faculty members are expected to exhibit and convey good citizenship within department, college, and university activities, interact collegially, and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an education-related or art-related field — including art education, or art history — completed by the start date of the appointment Completion of a teacher preparation program Licensure or certification to teach at the K-12 level (in any state), currently or previously held A minimum of three years of K-12 teaching experience Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in art education Three or more years of experience teaching visual art at the K-12 level, any grade span; experience at the 5-12 level is of particular interest K-12 visual art teaching licensure or certification Experience preparing, mentoring, or supervising pre-service art teachers Familiarity with current visual art education standards, such as the National Core Arts Standards and the Iowa Academic Standards for the Visual Arts, and with evidence-based art pedagogy Demonstrated commitment to culturally responsive and community-engaged teaching Evidence of effective teaching at the K-12 or college level, including college-level teaching beyond a graduate assistantship Terminal degree (Ph.D., Ed.D., or M.F.A) in art education, art, or a related field, which would establish eligibility to teach graduate-level courses in the art endorsement area of the Secondary Education M.A.T. Department/Program & College Description: About Iowa State University and the Department of Art and Visual Culture As a land-grant and Research I institution, Iowa State University upholds and advocates for the impact of creative activities, scholarship, and education both on- and off-campus. The College of Design celebrates and builds on long-standing success as a comprehensive design school that embodies knowledge-sharing and innovation. The Department of Art and Visual Culture exemplifies these qualities through the creativity of its community of makers, educators, and scholars. With an integrated and cross-disciplinary approach to teaching and collaborating, the department is committed to contributing to the excellence of the academic community and to building a culturally vibrant environment. Iowa State University is located in Ames, IA, a community of approximately 66,000 located about 30 minutes north of Des Moines, one of the fastest-growing metro areas in the Midwest. For more information about the department’s programs, see design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/art-visual-culture . Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: December 31, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. To receive full consideration, applications should be received by November 1, 2026. All interested, qualified persons must apply online at http://jobs.iastate.edu to Job Requisition Number R19942. The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format: Letter of application addressing your interests and qualifications for this position, including your K-12 teaching experience Curriculum vitae, including current email contact information Teaching philosophy statement Contact information for three professional references, including name, mailing address, email address, and phone number Please direct questions regarding this position to Dr. Sarah Kyle, Professor and Chair, Department of Art and Visual Culture, at skyle@iastate.edu or 515-294-9985. Questions regarding the application process may be directed to employment@iastate.edu or 515-294-4800 (Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485). Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 18, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19942 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Term---Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Equine-Field-Services_R19970": {
      "title": "Clinical Term – Assistant or Associate Professor Equine Field Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Term – Assistant or Associate Professor Equine Field Services Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities :    Iowa State University’s College of Veterinary Medicine, in Ames, Iowa, invites applications for a full-time Clinical Assistant or Clinical Associate Professor faculty position in Equine Field Services in the Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences. The successful candidate will join 3 other equine ambulatory veterinarians (Drs. Joan Howard (ABVP), Lauren Hughes (ACVIM-LA) and Kara Frerichs to enhance the regional prominence of the Equine Field Services program at Iowa State University through activities in clinical service, teaching, and scholarship. As a practice group we value a collaborative and collegial work environment, strive to provide high-quality diagnostic and treatment options to clients, and place an emphasis on client communication and outreach activities. We have built a practice around clients that engage as an active and informed partner in their horses' care and appreciate the benefits our team can offer as a direct extension of the teaching hospital.    The majority of the position will be dedicated to professional ambulatory clinical practice based out of the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC), a state-of-the-art teaching hospital providing specialized care for companion and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. Clinical practice will include training veterinary students and house officers (interns) within our large animal rotating internship program. A commitment to practicing a customer-centric service philosophy and maintaining a collegial working environment is expected. As part of the general practice of equine ambulatory veterinary medicine, the successful candidate is expected to develop/establish their skills and caseload within a focused, or niche area of equine veterinary medicine. Participation in didactic and laboratory teaching, independent or collaborative creative scholarship, and academic service are expected in varying amounts dependent on the candidate's interest and departmental needs. The amount of research, and other activities will be commensurate with the experience, rank, interests, and Position Responsibility Statement (PRS) of the successful candidate. Some after-hours ambulatory on call for Equine Field Services will be shared with other EFS clinicians (average ~25-30%) and may be discussed with the current Veterinary Clinical Sciences department chair (Dr. Wong).     Required Minimum Qualifications :  DVM or equivalent degree  State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before first day of employment   At least 1 year of experience practicing equine veterinary medicine    Preferred Qualifications :  Experience with equine ambulatory veterinary medicine practice   Clinical interest or advanced training/continuing education in lameness/sports medicine   Experience in veterinary student didactic and clinical teaching   Experience in training house officers (interns/residents)   Diplomate of the American Board of Veterinary Practitioners (equine) or other equine specialty    Federal accreditation through the national veterinary accreditation program    Department/Program & College Description : The LVMC is a state-of-the-art facility designed to provide specialized care and comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. Our clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work collaboratively to provide 24-hour, high-quality care to animal patients. Equine Field Service clinicians regularly collaborate with or refer cases to in-hospital specialists offering a high level of care and case continuity to their clients. Additionally, the Equine Field Service clinicians are able to schedule appointments in the LVMC and use the facility.    Activity within the Equine Field Services unit is based out of the equine wing of the field services building including ambulatory veterinary trucks and truck bays, a fully functional storeroom, stocked pharmacy, and clinician offices. Equipment includes digital radiography, advanced dental equipment, ultrasounds, and a mobile endoscopic unit allowing both upper airway exams and gastroscopy. The Veterinary Clinical Sciences department offers highly competitive salary and benefit packages for new faculty. Ames is a great community to live in and was recently voted one of the best college towns in the nation. It has a population of 60,000, located in central Iowa, approximately 30 minutes North from Des Moines. Numerous activities are available including camping, bike paths, golf courses, state parks, aquatic center, farmers’ markets, and the excitement of Big XII sporting events and more.   Department Unit/Website : https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/small-animal/support-services/anesthesiology/ https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc Proposed Start Date: January 2, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: June 30, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for a minimum of three (3) external to Iowa State References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For questions regarding this position, please contact EFS search committee chair, Dr. Lauren Hughes, at lehughes@iastate.edu.   For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before October 24, 2026. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 25, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19970 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Student-Services-Specialist-II_R19987": {
      "title": "Student Services Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Student Services Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering (CBE) at Iowa State University is seeking a dedicated individual for the role of Student Services Specialist II. The Student Services Specialist II plays a key role in supporting the academic experience of undergraduate chemical (CHE) and biomedical (BME) engineering students, as well as the accreditation and continuous improvement processes of the department. The primary responsibilities of the Student Services Specialist II will be:   • Supporting CHE and BME undergraduate student advising for orientation, registration, and graduation appointments • Coordinating the first-year CHE student learning community, including supervising peer mentors • Supporting the CHE program accreditation and continuous improvement processes • Advising CHE and BME undergraduate students regarding degree planning, graduation requirements, academic support services, and academic policies • Referring CHE and BME students to appropriate resources for academic success, counseling, financial aid, career services, study abroad Preferred Qualifications: • Experience coordinating student programs, such as learning communities • Experience with Workday Student • Experience advising postsecondary or high school students • Experience organizing data and preparing charts in Microsoft Excel About the Department: The College of Engineering is committed to sustaining a positive and productive environment for each individual and for the collective benefit of all. The successful candidate will have effective management and organizational skills, and the ability to communicate effectively. All staff members have a common responsibility to support and sustain our core values. They are expected to interact collegially and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior. Additionally, all CBE employees must abide by all departmental policies and procedures, rules and advising expectations outlined by Iowa State University, and FERPA guidelines with respect for the professional, confidential nature of advising undergraduate students.   The position will remain open until filled; however, October 9, 2026, is the last day to apply and receive full consideration. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: September 25, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19987 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Medical-Laboratory-Technician_R20005": {
      "title": "Medical Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Medical Laboratory Technician Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Medical Laboratory Technician (MLT) certification Job Description: Are you a Medical Laboratory Technician looking to apply your clinical laboratory skills in a unique and rewarding environment? Iowa State University's College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking a Medical Laboratory Technician (MLT) to support diagnostic testing services within the Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory. This position is ideal for both experienced MLTs and recent graduates seeking to build their careers in laboratory medicine. Using the same core laboratory skills developed in human healthcare settings, the selected candidate will perform diagnostic testing on samples from a variety of animal species. No prior veterinary experience is required. We provide training on veterinary-specific procedures and species differences. Schedule: Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Rotating Saturday coverage from 9:00 a.m. to 12:00 p.m. Key Responsibilities: Perform diagnostic testing, including hematology, chemistry, urinalysis, serology, coagulation testing, and cytology. Operate, calibrate, maintain, and troubleshoot laboratory analyzers and instrumentation. Perform quality control procedures and routine maintenance to ensure accurate and reliable test results. Support blood banking and coagulation testing procedures. Enter, review, and maintain patient and specimen information within the Laboratory Information System (LIS). Prepare and coordinate samples for referral testing and external laboratory submissions. Train and assist students, residents, and new staff on laboratory procedures and equipment. Maintain laboratory inventory, supplies, reagents, and records to support daily operations. Collaborate with faculty, clinicians, pathologists, and laboratory staff in a fast-paced diagnostic environment. Why You'll Love This Role: Put your Medical Laboratory Technician training and skills to work in a veterinary diagnostic setting. Gain experience performing diagnostic testing across a variety of animal species. Work in a collaborative laboratory environment that supports patient care, research, and education. Receive training in veterinary diagnostic techniques and species-specific testing. Join a team dedicated to quality laboratory practices and continuous learning. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in a clinical, diagnostic, healthcare, research, or academic laboratory through employment, internships, clinical rotations, or coursework. Experience with laboratory techniques, including sample preparation, staining, microscopy, and specimen processing. Experience following laboratory procedures, quality control practices, and documentation requirements. Experience operating laboratory instrumentation and technical equipment. To receive full consideration, applications should be received by October 16, 2026 . Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: September 29, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 19, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20005 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Environmental-Systems-Mechanic-II_R20007": {
      "title": "Environmental Systems Mechanic II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Environmental Systems Mechanic II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Six years of experience in temperature and computerized building environmental automation systems, refrigeration or air conditioning work, including apprenticeship, or has two years of experience in computerized building environmental automation systems and meets the minimum eligibility requirements of ESM I; or four years experience in above plus Journeyman’s license; and • Has refrigeration certificate of at least type 2. • May need to possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. • Prefer 2 years of college/trade school. Job Description: Facilities Planning and Management at Iowa State University is seeking qualified candidates for the Environmental Systems Mechanic II position. Facilities Planning and Management (FPM) is an organization that is dedicated to the maintenance and enhancement of Iowa State University, one of the nation’s leading educational and agricultural institutes. But more importantly, FPM is dedicated to their employees and enhancing the lives of each team member through opportunities both professionally and personally. FPM is one of the largest departments on campus and currently employs over 400 full-time employees and students combined.   This position performs skilled installation, repair, replacement, troubleshooting, and maintenance of environmental and HVAC systems, including refrigeration, temperature control, heating, and related support systems. Uses computerized building automation systems to monitor equipment performance, collect and analyze mechanical system data, and support system reliability and efficient operation. Applies advanced technical knowledge, training, and experience to coordinate and complete maintenance, operational activities, system modifications, and related projects. Performs the full range of duties associated with the environmental systems/HVAC trade using recognized procedures, industry standards, specialized tools, equipment, and diagnostic technologies. Responds to equipment conditions and system data through established preventive and predictive maintenance practices to identify developing issues, perform initial diagnostics, and take appropriate corrective action to maintain equipment performance and reliability.   Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Performs all duties listed under Environmental Systems Mechanic I. • Installs and maintains environmental systems equipment and components such as air conditioning equipment, chillers, condensers, pumps, fume hoods, autoclaves, environmental chambers, scientific equipment, cascade cooling units, process water systems, compressors and other pneumatic and computerized controls. Installs and maintains cooling tower equipment, plate-frame heat exchangers, cooling water treatment equipment, heating systems (all fuel types) to include boilers, unit heaters, furnaces, radiant heating, heat pump systems (geothermal and air source), variable frequency drives, and other emerging technology equipment/systems. • Tests and evaluates performance of systems using specialized equipment, repairs or replaces defective valves, thermostats, sensor and other parts in both pneumatic and computerized building environmental automation systems. • Operates computerized building environmental automation systems that control heating and cooling systems. • Performs continuous commissioning and retro commissioning of various types of environmental equipment to assure these systems are meeting energy optimization efficiency goals, operating to desired baselines, and are meeting the expectations of the customer. • Utilizes energy monitoring devices and test equipment to establish predictive type maintenance repairs that extend the life of systems and eliminate out of service conditions. • Provides functional guidance and training to apprentices, replacements, students and other personnel as required. • Other duties as assigned by appropriate department or administrative personnel.  Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of the principles of operations, methods, materials, and tools utilized in the installation, troubleshooting, maintenance, calibration and repair of environmental systems. • Ability to properly braze refrigeration tubing and connections. • Knowledge of occupational hazards and safety precautions mandated by the Occupational Safety and Health Administration, National Fire Prevention Association, National Fire Code, the Environmental Protection Agency, etc. • Knowledge, skill and ability to evaluate and recommend equipment for either installation, repair, or replacement and determine the amount of time and materials necessary to accomplish the task with least expense and downtime of equipment. • Knowledge of computerized building environmental automation systems and ability to collect data for mechanical system performance. • Skill in the proper use and care of hand and power tools and test equipment. • Knowledge of proper bending and lifting techniques. • Ability to work in areas of high heat, dust and noise and in confined spaces or on a ladder. • Ability to interpret blueprints, diagrams and equipment specifications. • Ability to work independently during the normal workday and in an on-call status. • Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing.  • Ability to work in all types of environmental conditions or in areas where there is exposure to excessive noise, dirt, and fumes and at elevated heights from ladders, scaffolds, or hydraulic lifts. • Ability to work independently during normal work hours and after hours. • Knowledgeable of the operation and maintenance of variable frequency drives. • Knowledge of chilled water systems and maintenance requirements.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5091a Original Posting Date: September 29, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 28, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20007 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Cook-I_R20003": {
      "title": "Cook I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Cook I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. Job Description: Iowa State University Dining is seeking enthusiastic individuals to join our team as Cook I across multiple campus dining locations. These positions will be 9, 10, 11 and 12 month opportunities with varies schedules offered. This is a great opportunity for those with experience in food service, hospitality, or customer-facing roles who enjoy hands-on kitchen work and want to build their skills in a steady, team-focused environment. At ISU Dining, you’ll work alongside a dedicated group of culinary professionals in one of the largest dining programs in the country. With more than 20 dining locations on campus, our teams prepare fresh, high-quality food while supporting daily campus life. Positions may support a variety of service areas, including residential dining, retail locations, and catering operations. Learn more about Iowa State University Dining: https://www.dining.iastate.edu What You’ll Do Prepare and cook food by following recipes and production guidelines for a variety of menu items. Support service operations by assisting with daily meal service and/or catering events, as assigned. Maintain food safety standards by following proper sanitation, safety, and temperature requirements. Assist with training and team support by helping guide student employees and supporting coworkers during service. Handle supplies and inventory by monitoring food and supply needs and assisting with deliveries. Keep work areas clean and organized by maintaining kitchen equipment, utensils, and prep spaces. What You’ll Get Insurance benefits beginning on your first day, with timely enrollment. Retirement benefits with strong university contributions. Paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay. Tuition reimbursement available after one year of employment. Free meals provided during scheduled work shifts. A collaborative, service-oriented workplace dedicated to supporting students. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities Prepares and cooks meats, fish, vegetables, gravies, cereals, soups, fruits, bakery products and other forms of food. Prepares and cooks food for special diets from recipes formulated by qualified personnel. Assists in on-the-job training and assists in directing the work of food service workers, students and other employees within area of assignment. Assists in the preparation of salads and desserts. Notifies supervisor of food and supplies needed. Checks in food and supplies as necessary. Maintains food production records. Cleans kitchen, kitchen utensils and equipment; secures refrigerator and freezer. Serves food as required. Maintains maximum standards of sanitation and safety. Performs other related duties and responsibilities as required or assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to judge final food product for quantity (yield) and quality (color, taste, texture, etc.). Ability to determine the freshness and quality of raw and cooked food products by sight and taste. Knowledge of safe temperatures for serving food and storage of refrigerated and frozen storage of raw and cooked foods. Knowledge of principles of food sanitation, health hazards, and the necessary precautionary measures. Ability to stand for long periods of time. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds. Ability to provide on-the-job training in food preparation to lower level employees. Ability to maintain effective working relationships with others. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 0004a Original Posting Date: September 28, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 29, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20003 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Lecturer---Civil-Construction-and-Environmental-Engineering_R19967": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Civil Construction and Environmental Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Lecturer - Civil Construction and Environmental Engineering Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Civil, Construction and Environmental Engineering (CCEE) at Iowa State University invites applications for one or more part-time Lecturer positions to teach sophomore-level courses that introduce students to building construction materials, methods, and mechanical and electrical systems. These in-person courses emphasize plan reading and quantity takeoff techniques. The Individual(s) appointed would be responsible for coordinating and teaching one section of ConE 2410, Constructions Materials and Methods (3 credits), and one section of ConE 2510, Mechanical/Electrical Materials and Methods (1 credit). This would involve preparing lecture notes, attending class and delivering lectures, being available to meet with students when lectures and labs are delivered, preparing and grading homework, lab assignments, quizzes, exams, and projects for the classes, and working with other faculty as needed. Grading support may be available based on availability of resources and class size. In total, this position is 1/3 (.33) full-time equivalent of a 9-month position, or depending on applicant qualifications, one lecturer may teach ConE 2410 at (.25) FTE and one lecturer may teach ConE 2510 at (.08) FTE. The initial term would be for one semester with potential for renewal. Lecturers can transition into a Term faculty position. Lecturers and Term Faculty members are not eligible for tenure, but Term Faculty do have potential to be reviewed for advancement. Candidates are expected to have an excellent record of achievement in teaching or engineering practice in construction or civil engineering or a closely related discipline. They are expected to exhibit excellent communication skills and share in our commitment to achieving excellence through Iowa State's Principles of Community.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Candidates for this position must hold a Bachelor's degree in construction, civil, or architectural engineering, or a related engineering degree plus 5 years of relevant experience.   Preferred Qualifications: Industry experience related to the position. Previous teaching experience. Strong communication skills. Professional engineering licensure in the United States, or the ability to become licensed.   Department/Program & College Description: The CCEE Department offers B.S. degree programs in civil engineering, civil engineering with environmental emphasis, construction engineering, and environmental engineering, plus M.S., MEng, and Ph.D. graduate degree programs in civil engineering and maintains externally funded research of more that $18 million annually.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.ccee.iastate.edu   Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, application materials should be received by October 19, 2026. All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu. The following documents are required to be submitted as four separate PDF files (one for each required item number below): 1) Letter of application that briefly discusses how you, the candidate, meets each of the required and preferred qualifications. 2) Resume or Curriculum Vitae 3) Two-page statement explaining your qualifications to teach the courses described above and how you would bring your industry experience into the courses. 4) Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, and phone number, and other pertinent information. Direct questions to cceesearch@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-1676. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 28, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19967 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Industrial-and-Manufacturing-Systems-Engineering---Assistant-or-Associate-Professor_R19992": {
      "title": "Industrial and Manufacturing Systems Engineering - Assistant or Associate Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Industrial and Manufacturing Systems Engineering - Assistant or Associate Professor Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Industrial and Manufacturing Systems Engineering, in the College of Engineering at Iowa State University (ISU), invites applications for a tenured/tenure track hire at the rank of assistant professor OR associate professor to start in Fall 2027 in the area of automation and robotics with foundational expertise in either advanced manufacturing or human factors and ergonomics. Successful candidates will be expected to establish, sustain and grow a world-class externally funded research program that complements or aligns with the department's areas through independent and collaborative efforts. Successful candidates will also be expected to establish a record of scholarship at the highest levels, contribute to the teaching missions at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and engage in institutional service and service to the profession. Candidates should have strong communication skills and exhibit the potential for long-term leadership in supporting the mission of the department, college, and university. The Department of Industrial and Manufacturing Systems Engineering is committed to sustaining a collegial, positive, and productive environment for each individual and the collective benefit of all. All faculty members are expected to exhibit and convey good citizenship withing department, college, and university activities, interact collegially and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent degree in industrial engineering or a closely aligned field Associate Professor candidates must also meet the university standards for appointment to the rank, including significant experience/accomplishments in the candidate's area of expertise   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of ability to establish an independent research program in either advanced manufacturing or human factors Evidence of ability or potential for teaching excellence in either advanced manufacturing or human factors Evidence of collaboration in research and education   Department/Program & College Description: The IMSE Department offers B.S, MEng, M.S., and Ph.D. degree programs in Industrial Engineering, as well as M.Eng. programs in Systems Engineering and Engineering Management. IMSE has an undergraduate enrollment of more than 450 students and graduate enrollment of approximately 100 students. IMSE has maintained externally funded research expenditures of around $4 million annually and demonstrates a commitment to diversity among faculty, staff, and students who can enrich University objectives in the areas of research, teaching, and service. In May of 2025 the IMSE department moved into the newly constructed 75,354 square feet Therkildsen Industrial Engineering Building dedicated to the department's teaching, research, and outreach activities. Research laboratories include four human factors laboratories in a 3000-foot low- and high-bay space, the Slater Laboratory for Advanced Manufacturing, with capabilities that include Directed Energy Deposition (DED), Laser Powder Bed Fusion (LPBF), and Ultrasonic Metal 3D Printing, the Sukup Advanced Manufacturing Laboratory for automation, as well as the Laser-based Processing Lab. State-of-the-art laboratories currently under construction include the Robot Habitat and the Immersive Lab. Iowa State University and Central Iowa Iowa State University is a Carnegie Foundation R1 institution with a student enrollment exceeding 30,000 located in Ames, a progressive community just 30 miles north of Des Moines. Ames offers extensive parks and trails, strong public schools, a comparatively low cost of living and convenient access to the cultural and recreational opportunities of one of the fastest-growing metro areas in the Midwest. More information about the university and city can be found here: https://www.provost.iastate.edu/faculty-success/prospective   Department Unit/Website: For more information about our department's program, see https://www.imse.iastate.edu/ .   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Letter of application the briefly discusses each of the preferred qualifications 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information 4) Teaching Statement (2-page limit) 5) Research Statement (3-page limit) Direct questions to Dr. Siggi Olafsson at imsesearch@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-8908. Application Deadline (Full consideration date): For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before October 28, 2026. This position will be open until filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 28, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19992 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Advanced-Imaging-Technologist_R19988": {
      "title": "Advanced Imaging Technologist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Advanced Imaging Technologist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree or equivalent certification in a Joint Review Committee on Education in Radiologic Technology (JRCERT) accredited program and one year of related experience. Certified in general radiologic technology by the American Registry of Radiologic Technology, Radiography (ARRT) (R). Possession of current Iowa Permit to Practice. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Looking for a career that combines your diagnostic imaging expertise with hands-on work with animals? If so, the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC) in Iowa State University's College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking an Advanced Imaging Technologist to join our Radiology team! This is a unique opportunity for an imaging professional to apply advanced imaging skills in a dynamic veterinary teaching hospital while working with a wide variety of patients, including exotics, companion animals, equine patients, and food animal species. The LVMC provides specialized medical and surgical care to patients throughout Iowa and the surrounding region. Our clinicians, residents, interns, veterinary technicians, imaging professionals, staff, and veterinary students work collaboratively to provide high-quality, state-of-the-art patient care 24 hours a day. What You'll Do: The Advanced Imaging Technologist independently performs and supports a variety of advanced imaging procedures, including Radiography, Fluoroscopy, Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), and Nuclear Medicine. Working collaboratively with radiologists, clinicians, veterinary technicians, anesthesia personnel, students, and other hospital teams, this position produces high-quality diagnostic studies and adapts imaging techniques, protocols, and patient positioning to meet the unique needs of various species, anatomy, clinical conditions, and patient sizes while supporting efficient patient care throughout the imaging process. Every day brings new challenges and opportunities to expand your imaging expertise across multiple species. Additional Responsibilities: This position also contributes to the continued quality and development of the Radiology service by: Operating and maintaining complex diagnostic imaging equipment. Evaluating image quality and making appropriate technical adjustments to optimize diagnostic studies. Maintaining quality-control standards in accordance with hospital, departmental, and radiation-safety requirements. Assisting with equipment troubleshooting and preventative maintenance to minimize interruptions to patient care. Communicating effectively with clinicians and hospital services to coordinate imaging needs and priorities. Training and providing guidance to new employees, veterinary students, and others rotating through the Radiology service. Contributing to workflow improvements and a collaborative, team-oriented work environment. Who We Are Looking For : The successful candidate will be a self-motivated and adaptable imaging professional who is comfortable working independently while also collaborating closely with a multidisciplinary veterinary team. This position requires strong technical judgment, attention to detail, organization, and the ability to adjust quickly to changing patient and hospital needs. We are looking for someone who brings professional maturity, strong communication skills, and a positive approach to teamwork. The ideal candidate enjoys sharing their knowledge with others and is comfortable providing instruction and guidance to employees and veterinary students. Because our patients cannot always understand or cooperate with imaging procedures in the same way human patients can, patience, adaptability, creative problem-solving, and an interest in working with animals are particularly valuable in this role. Preferred Qualifications: Registration through ARRT in Computed Tomography (CT) and/or Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI). Experience performing CT, MRI, radiography, fluoroscopy, nuclear medicine, or other advanced imaging procedures. Experience working with or handling animals. Experience training, mentoring, or providing technical guidance to others. The scheduled work hours will generally be Monday through Friday during regular daytime business hours, with rotating weekday and weekend on-call responsibilities. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before October 23rd, 2026. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: September 30, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19988 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor---Agricultural-Education-and-Studies_R20021": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Agricultural Education and Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor - Agricultural Education and Studies Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Agricultural Education and Studies at Iowa State University located in Ames, Iowa, seeks applicants for a 9-month, tenure-track position at the rank of assistant professor. The focus of the position will be in agriculture teacher education. The position is 60% teaching and advising (undergraduate, MS and PhD students), 35% research, and 5% institutional and professional service. Responsibilities will include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses related to agriculture education, both resident and online, and coordinating, facilitating and supervising field experiences. The candidate will be expected to develop a productive research program of national scope that addresses current issues related to agriculture and life sciences education and aligns with departmental strengths and mission. Research effort will include securing external funding, publishing in peer-reviewed journals, presenting research at national conferences, and advising undergraduate and graduate students. Service on departmental, college, and/or university committees, engagement with professional organizations, and potentially advising a student organization is expected.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D., awarded by the start date, in Agricultural Education or closely related field. Three years of teaching experience in agriculture or closely related field at the school-based or college level. Preferred Qualifications: Completion of a teacher preparation program. Evidence of effective and innovative resident and online teaching. Documented experience conducting and disseminating research/scholarship. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Agricultural Education and Studies has its focus in the teaching and learning processes. All three elements of the land-grant philosophy -- learning, discovery, and engagement -- are part of the department's emphasis on the educational processes and how these processes impact our clientele in a variety of agricultural settings.   Department Unit/Website: For more information on the department, visit https://www.ageds.iastate.edu/ . Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of application/Cover letter 3) Contact Information for three professional references 4) Statement describing research goals 5) Statement of teaching philosophy Applications will be collected until the position is filled. However for full, guaranteed consideration, applications should be received by October 31, 2026. If you have questions regarding this vacancy, please contact Dr. Scott Smalley at 515-294-0047, or by email at smalle16@iastate.edu. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 1, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20021 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Ames-National-Laboratory_R20023": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ames National Laboratory",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ames National Laboratory Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Division of Materials Science and Engineering at Ames National Laboratory seeks a Postdoctoral Research Associate to conduct experimental research on measurements and understanding the microscopic origins of low-frequency (1/f) magnetic and electric noise in superconducting quantum circuits, with particular focus on transmon qubits. The primary experimental tool will be quantum sensing with nitrogen-vacancy (NV) centers in diamond, used as local, magnetically selective passive probes of the noise environment at the surfaces, interfaces, and thin films from which superconducting devices are built. The central research goal is to identify which physical mechanisms – surface and interface spins, magnetic defects, two-level systems, trapped flux and vortex motion, and nonequilibrium quasiparticles – generate the 1/f flux and charge noise that limits qubit coherence, and to determine what fraction of a qubit’s decoherence is magnetic in origin. This will be achieved by combining NV-based noise spectroscopy (spin relaxometry and dynamical-decoupling measurements of T1 and T2) and static-field ODMR magnetometry with standard transmon characterization and qubit-intrinsic noise spectroscopy (CPMG and spin-locking sequences) on the same devices, in the same cryostat and cooldown. The postdoctoral researcher will play a key role in commissioning a new cryogen-free dilution-refrigerator platform that integrates confocal optical access and NV positioning with filtered microwave wiring for qubit control and dispersive readout. Specific tasks include optimizing diamond sensor geometry, NV depth and NV-to-device standoff; developing pulse sequences, measurement protocols and analysis pipelines; and devising strategies that isolate the qubit from the optical and microwave excitation used for NV readout, including systematic characterization of light-induced quasiparticle effects. The work will complement the group’s established tunnel-diode resonator quasiparticle spectroscopy. The work will include planning and conducting experiments, critically analyzing measured noise spectra and modeling them in terms of microscopic fluctuator ensembles, and performing numerical calculations or simulations where appropriate. The researcher must be able to work both independently and collaboratively and to communicate effectively across condensed-matter physics, materials science, quantum sensing, and quantum information science. Required Minimum Qualifications (for temps/postdocs only, delete for all other positions): Ph.D. in experimental condensed-matter physics, applied physics, quantum science and engineering, atomic, molecular and optical physics, materials science and engineering, or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications: Hands-on experience with NV centers in diamond or other optically addressable spin defects, including optically detected magnetic resonance (ODMR), pulsed microwave spin control, confocal microscopy, and single-photon detection. Experience with shallow NV ensembles, near-surface sensing, T1 relaxometry or dynamical-decoupling noise spectroscopy is highly desirable, as is NV magnetometry of superconducting or magnetic materials. Solid understanding of noise physics and quantum noise spectroscopy: power spectral densities, filter-function analysis of pulse sequences, the fluctuation–dissipation relation, and microscopic models of 1/f flux and charge noise (surface spins, two-level systems, trapped vortices). Experience with superconducting qubits or high-Q superconducting resonators, including packaging, cryogenic microwave wiring, attenuation and filtering, dispersive readout, and coherence measurements (T1, Ramsey, echo, CPMG). Direct experience with both NV centers and qubits is rare; strong expertise in one area and a clear commitment to mastering the other is expected. Demonstrated hands-on experience with low-temperature experimental techniques, cryogenic systems, vacuum equipment, magnetic fields and magnetic shielding, low-noise electronics, and precision measurements. Experience with dilution refrigerators, millikelvin measurements, and cryogenic optics is strongly preferred. Experience with pulse-sequencing and control electronics (arbitrary waveform generators, FPGA-based quantum controllers, time taggers) and with scientific programming, quantitative data analysis, and simulation using tools such as Python, LabVIEW, MATLAB, Mathematica, Origin, or COMSOL Multiphysics. Background in superconductivity, magnetism, thin films, surfaces and interfaces, and effects of disorder, and familiarity with what conventional characterization (transport, PPMS/MPMS, X-ray scattering, electron microscopy) reveals. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in written reports, oral presentations, manuscripts, and interdisciplinary team discussions; collaborate with others; maintain accurate laboratory records; and meet project milestones. Department/Program & College Description: Would you like to work for a National Laboratory that conducts world-renowned research? Would you enjoy working on a beautiful university campus? Can you imagine yourself in a mid-sized location that regularly ranks as one of the U.S. Best Places to Live ? If you answered yes to any of these questions, you should consider a career with Ames National Laboratory!   Ames Laboratory is a U.S. Department of Energy federally contracted National Laboratory located in Ames, Iowa, on the campus of Iowa State University. We are dedicated to translating foundational science through applied research to create technological innovations. We create materials, inspire minds to solve problems, and address some of the most challenging issues facing our world today. We promote and believe in a culture of civility and shared ownership in support of the Laboratory's collective success. Department Unit/Website (if applicable): www.ameslab.gov Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter List of Professional References Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: January 4, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: September 30, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 30, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20023 Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory.   Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Senior-Scholarship-and-Student-Funding-Specialist_R20017": {
      "title": "Senior Scholarship and Student Funding Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Senior Scholarship and Student Funding Specialist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Advance Student Success Through Scholarship and Funding Excellence The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) at Iowa State University is seeking a highly organized, analytical, and student-focused professional to serve as our next Senior Scholarship and Student Funding Specialist.   This position will play a vital role in helping students access financial resources, ensuring donor-funded scholarships are administered effectively, and supporting college enrollment and student success goals through data-informed decision making and operational excellence.   If you enjoy solving complex problems, working across many stakeholder groups, improving processes, and making a meaningful impact on students' lives, we encourage you to apply.   Why This Role Matters Scholarships and student funding can be transformational for students and their families. This position serves as a critical resource for the college, connecting students with financial opportunities while ensuring hundreds of scholarship funds are administered accurately, responsibly, and in accordance with donor intent.   You'll join a highly engaged team united by a shared commitment to student success. Scholarships and student funding are fundamental to that work, helping students access the resources and opportunities they need to succeed at Iowa State University. In this role, your work will be at the foundation of some of CALS's most important strategic goals, helping ensure financial resources are aligned with student needs and college priorities and supporting the programs and opportunities that help students thrive.   As the college's scholarship administration expert, you will help advance effective stewardship of donor-funded resources and shape processes that improve access, efficiency, compliance, and service across the college.   About the Role The Senior Scholarship and Student Funding Specialist serves as the operational and subject matter expert for undergraduate and graduate scholarship administration across the college. The position provides consultation and guidance to departments and stakeholders, manages complex scholarship processes, monitors compliance and stewardship requirements, and analyzes data that support decision-making and continuous improvement.   This role combines student service, policy interpretation, financial stewardship, data analysis, and cross-functional collaboration in support of one of Iowa State University's largest and most impactful colleges.   The position offers the opportunity to serve as a trusted advisor and problem solver while helping shape processes that support students and the broader strategic goals of the college.   This position may be eligible for hybrid work of up to two business days, after completion of an initial orientation and training period.   Preferred Qualifications : Experience interpreting and applying donor agreements, funding restrictions, policies, regulations, or eligibility requirements to ensure financial resources are used appropriately and in alignment with intended purposes. Experience developing proposals, recommendations, or strategic plans and articulating and presenting goals, findings, and recommendations to leadership or other stakeholders. Experience analyzing financial, student, program, or utilization data to identify trends, evaluate outcomes, assess resource needs, and inform strategic decision-making. Experience building collaborative relationships and providing consultation, guidance, or training to stakeholders on complex programs, policies, funding processes, or organizational priorities.   The selected candidate will be hired as a Student Services Specialist III.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: October 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 18, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20017 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Kinesiology-and-Health_R20016": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Kinesiology and Health",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Kinesiology and Health Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Kinesiology and Health at Iowa State University invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, beginning August 16, 2027 . This open search welcomes applicants from any area of kinesiology and health. We seek an outstanding scholar whose research complements and extends our strengths, expands externally funded research through diverse sources, develops partnerships with industry, healthcare, or community organizations, and advances Iowa State's land-grant mission by improving health and well-being in Iowa and beyond. Candidates at the Associate Professor rank will also have opportunities to mentor early-career faculty and contribute to department leadership. The initial contract period is for up to four years with the possibility of renewal. About the Department The Department of Kinesiology and Health is one of five units in the College of Health and Human Sciences. The Department is committed to advancing the science of physical activity, human movement, and health through innovative and impactful research. Faculty maintain active research programs in exercise physiology, exercise psychology, biomechanics, neuromotor control, and physical activity and health, with departmental strengths in healthy aging, cardiovascular and brain health, skeletal muscle and space biology, immunology, occupational biomechanics, rural health, digital health, and translational intervention research across the lifespan. Studies range from cellular and molecular research to randomized controlled trials, and from community-based research to dissemination and implementation science, addressing critical questions related to health, performance, and quality of life. Indirect cost revenue is returned directly to principal investigators at a competitive rate. Undergraduate programs: More than 1,100 undergraduate majors, ranking in the top three for undergraduate enrollment among Iowa State's 61 academic departments. The BS in Kinesiology and Health offers options in Community and Public Health, Exercise Science, Physical Activity and Health Promotion, Physical Education Teacher Education, and Pre-Health Professions, with minors in Dance, Exercise Science, Health Promotion, and Kinesiology and Health. Graduate programs: More than 80 graduate students, with enrollment nearly doubling in recent years. Programs include the MS and PhD in Kinesiology, Master's in Athletic Training, and online Master's in Digital Health. Undergraduate research: Strong demand for research mentorship, with most students pursuing pre-health careers. Of student researchers surveyed, 86% of  rate their lab experience as very or extremely impactful. People and culture: The department includes 42 faculty and staff, including 13 tenure-track and tenured faculty, 17 term faculty, and 12 professional and scientific staff. A 2026 external program review recognized our collegial culture as a key strength. Facilities: The department’s 90,000-square-foot facility includes the Exercise Clinic, 15 research laboratories, and 5 teaching laboratories, with shared DEXA, cardiovascular, metabolic, and strength assessment spaces. Collaboration: Interdisciplinary teams connect department strengths with partners across campus, including the ISU Translational Research Network (U-TuRN), ISU Extension and Outreach serving all 99 Iowa counties, the Nanovaccine Institute, Center for Industrial Research and Service, Virtual Reality Applications Center, ISU Athletics, the Colleges of Veterinary Medicine and Engineering, as well as  healthcare, industry, and community partners across Iowa. The successful applicant for this position will: Establish or sustain an externally funded research program drawing on federal, foundation, industry, or other sources Publish in respected peer-reviewed journals Build partnerships that expand research, funding, and student opportunities, and share research findings with practitioners and the public Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the area of expertise Mentor graduate students and engage undergraduates in research Provide service to the department, college, university, and profession   Required Minimum Qualifications : Earned doctorate in Kinesiology or a related field by the start date Assistant Professor rank: A record of peer-reviewed publications and evidence of a research program with strong potential for external funding Associate Professor rank: A sustained record of peer-reviewed publications, extramural funding, and a nationally recognized research program sufficient to qualify for tenure at the rank of Associate Professor Preferred Qualifications :  Research that complements or extends one or more department research strengths Record of seeking funding from diverse sources, such as federal agencies, foundations, industry, or state and community partners Postdoctoral experience Experience building partnerships or translating research into practice Record of interdisciplinary collaboration Collegiate teaching and graduate mentoring experience Leadership experience in research, professional, or academic settings Department Unit/Website: https://kin.hs.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Cover letter (up to 2 pages) addressing the required and preferred qualifications 2) Curriculum vitae 3) Research statement (2 to 3 pages) describing how your research complements and extends the department's research strengths, and your plan for external funding 4) Contact information for three professional references   For guaranteed consideration, please submit your application materials by November 9, 2026 . This position will remain open until filled.   Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Elizabeth Stegemöller , Search Committee Chair, at esteg@iastate.edu.   Questions about the application process may be directed to employment@iastate.edu or 515-294-4800. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20016 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Music---Low-Strings--Cello-and-Double-Bass-_R20027": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Music - Low Strings (Cello and Double Bass)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor of Music - Low Strings (Cello and Double Bass) Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Music and Theatre at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa seeks a dynamic and experienced Assistant Teaching Professor of Music in low strings (cello and double bass) starting 8/16/27. The successful candidate will teach applied cello and double bass lessons, teach low strings techniques class, and perform as a member of the Ames Piano Quartet.  The successful candidate may also be assigned to teach additional courses within the department based on their qualifications and expertise.   This is a 7/8 full-time equivalent (FTE) term faculty, 9-month position with an initial 3-year term. Competitive salary, retirement options, and health benefits.  Staffing needs and budget availability may provide the opportunity in some semesters to increase to 1.0 FTE in exchange for teaching one additional course.   Responsibilities: Teach cello and double bass applied lessons Teach the low strings portion of the music education string techniques course Perform cello in the Ames Piano Quartet Teach additional courses as assigned based on qualifications and expertise   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications :  Master’s degree in Music or related discipline Demonstrated experience performing chamber music Demonstrated experience teaching low strings Preferred Qualifications :  Master’s degree or higher in music with an emphasis in cello performance or cello pedagogy Demonstrated experience and achievement in cello performance Demonstrated experience teaching low strings (cello and double bass) at the college/university level Demonstrated successful recruitment strategies Demonstrated experience teaching other areas of music Department/Program & College Description : The Department of Music and Theatre: prepares music and theatre students for professional life. creates high impact learning experiences for students across the university. serves as the central contributor to the artistic and creative vitality of the university, Iowa, and beyond. provides a welcoming community for all.    The Department of Music and Theatre is committed to a philosophy of education that draws its goals from the larger purposes of liberal arts education and from the guidelines of its accrediting agency, the National Association of Schools of Music (NASM). With strong undergraduate  music  and  theatre  programs, students study with full-time faculty professionals in a supportive environment that encourages students to become their best. The first documented mention of a Symphony Orchestra at Iowa State University is found in the student yearbook of 1894, meaning there has been an organized orchestra on campus for over 125 years. From its earliest days as a small, student-led group, the ensemble has since grown into a full-size orchestra led by distinguished faculty, performing major symphonic, choral and operatic repertoire.  Learn more about the ISU Symphony Orchestra here: https://www.music.iastate.edu/ensemble/symphorch   In various iterations, the Ames Piano Quartet has been the ensemble-in-residence at Iowa State University since its inception in 1976. The ensemble has an extensive discography, including fourteen CDs under the Ames name and a further two as Amara. Labels for which the group has recorded include Musical Heritage, Dorian, Sono Luminus, Albany, and Fleur de Son Classics. The Ames Piano Quartet has appeared in concert throughout the United States and Canada, as well as in France, Austria, Taiwan, South Africa, and Russia. The Ames Piano Quartet’s recording of George Tsontakis’ Piano Quartet #4 has been released, August 7, 2026 by Navona Records. Learn more about the Ames Piano Quartet here: https://www.music.iastate.edu/ensemble/apq   Department Unit/Website : music.iastate.edu Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Links to two performance video samples (can be within the cover letter) 4) Contact Information for Three References   *Second round candidates will be asked for teaching video samples For guaranteed consideration, please submit your application by November 9, 2026. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20027 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Motor-Vehicle-Operator-II---Delivery-Driver_R20045": {
      "title": "Motor Vehicle Operator II - Delivery Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Motor Vehicle Operator II - Delivery Driver Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • One year experience driving trucks. • Possession of the class (class A, B, C or D) of drivers license appropriate to vehicle driven and/or materials transported. Job Description: Are you looking for a Monday-Friday, day shift position that offers excellent work-life balance? Are you looking to join an organization with excellent benefits? If so, Iowa State University is seeking a Motor Vehicle Operator II to work as a delivery driver within the Central Receiving operation! Iowa State University Central Receiving provides a single-point delivery network for the ISU campus. Central Receiving will receive, track, and redistribute university funded materials to ISU departments.  This position is responsible for daily delivery of packages and palletized goods and equipment to the Iowa State University community. This is a physical position that involves climbing stairs along with lifting and carrying packages daily. The successful individual will have the ability to lift up to 100 lbs. This person will need to make sound judgements, have a sense of urgency, and provide high-level customer service. They will perform as a laborer when not driving in a fast-paced warehouse environment. The successful candidate will possess the ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions; knowledge of hazards and safety precautions related to warehousing and delivery work; the ability to perform heavy manual labor; and the ability to work in a varying weather conditions. Preferred Qualifications: Delivery experience; specifically within package and freight delivery Warehouse receiving experience Experience using electronic devices, such as smart phones, tablets, and computers Experience using forklifts and electric pallet jacks Hours: Monday - Friday, 7:30 am - 4:00 pm Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Reads work order to determine materials to be transported. • Consults with person responsible for materials to be hauled in order to determine special needs. • Verifies load with suppliers against order request. • Loads and unloads cargo including hazardous materials or sensitive instrument.  • Secures cargo using chains, rubberized straps, padding to prevent damage. • Assembles furniture or exhibits. • Services vehicles, both interior and exterior, including cleaning and washing with power equipment, refueling, and other minor items of vehicle maintenance as required.  • Performs as a Laborer when not driving. • Responds to calls for emergency service, including snow removal, as required.  • May require occasional in-state and out-of-state overnight travel. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to lift up to 100 pounds. • Ability to read, write, follow instructions, and communicate orally. • Ability to operate moving equipment such as pallet movers and forklifts. • Ability to make sounds judgments and decisions. • Ability to safely operate and insure proper maintenance of vehicles. • Knowledge of proper loading/securing techniques for specialized cargo. • Knowledge of the rules and regulations governing operation of state vehicles. • Knowledge of motor vehicle laws. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 06 Original Posting Date: October 5, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 18, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20045 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor---Environmental-Engineering_R20069": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Environmental Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor - Environmental Engineering Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Civil, Construction and Environmental Engineering (CCEE) at Iowa State University (ISU) seeks candidates for a tenure-track assistant professor faculty position in environmental engineering. Applications from candidates in all areas of environmental engineering are welcome, but areas of particular interest include novel materials for environmental applications, One Health applications to environmental engineering, resource recovery, and air pollution. The successful candidate will establish and sustain an externally funded research program and complement the current research and education efforts in the CCEE Department through interdisciplinary collaboration. The candidate will teach courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, mentor both graduate and undergraduate students, generate a scholarly publication record, participate in technical committees and outreach activities, and exhibit a commitment to the ISU Principles of Community. Candidates should communicate well, collaborate effectively, and contribute to the mission of the department. We especially welcome candidates that can contribute to the department's ABET-accredited Environmental Engineering B.S. program. For more information about out department's engineering program, see www.ccee.iastate.edu .   Required Minimum Qualifications: Candidates for this position must hold a Ph.D. in civil engineering, environmental engineering or a closely related field. The Ph.D. must be conferred by the employment start date.   Preferred Qualifications: Agenda of research that compliments existing strengths in the department and University. Agenda of teaching that contributes to the department's degree programs, especially Environmental Engineering. A strong record of peer-reviewed publications in related technical areas. A professional engineering license or the ability to become licensed. Professional experience (e.g., academic, postdoctoral, industry) in a related field   Department/Program & College Description: The CCEE Department offers B.S. degree programs in civil engineering, civil engineering with environmental emphasis, construction engineering, and environmental engineering, plus M.S., MEng, and Ph.D. graduate degree programs in civil engineering and maintains externally funded research of more than $21 million annually. CCEE is committed to faculty, staff and students who can enrich University objectives in the areas of research, teaching, and service. Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will begin to be reviewed on November 15, 2026 with full consideration given to applications received by that date. The posting will remain open until the position is filled. All interested, qualified people must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu . Please be prepared to attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 12, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20069 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate-in-Watershed-Hydrology-and-Water-Quality_R20068": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Watershed Hydrology and Water Quality",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate in Watershed Hydrology and Water Quality Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to conduct interdisciplinary research focused on watershed hydrology, agricultural water quality, and antimicrobial resistance (AMR) in agricultural landscapes. The successful candidate will develop and apply watershed models, deploy and manage environmental monitoring systems, analyze complex datasets, and collaborate with multidisciplinary research teams to advance conservation and water quality solutions. This position offers opportunities to publish in peer-reviewed journals, contribute to proposal development, and engage with stakeholders across academic, governmental, and agricultural sectors. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Agricultural Engineering, Biosystems Engineering, Environmental Engineering, Civil Engineering, Hydrology, Water Resources, Environmental Science, or a closely related field. Demonstrated research experience in watershed hydrology, antimicrobial resistance (AMR), environmental monitoring, agricultural water quality assessment, and the development, calibration, and application of SWAT+ or comparable watershed models. Experience with environmental data analysis and scientific programming (e.g., Python, R, MATLAB, SQL, or C++), large-scale environmental datasets, automated data processing and QA/QC procedures, and operation of environmental monitoring instrumentation and data acquisition systems. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with GIS, remote sensing, geospatial analysis, GNSS/GPS technologies, or watershed-scale environmental modeling. Experience with antimicrobial resistance (AMR) sample collection, laboratory processing, and analysis of antibiotic resistance indicators. Experience integrating environmental monitoring data with machine learning, predictive analytics, or decision-support tools. Experience developing dashboards and data visualization platforms using Power BI, Tableau, R Shiny, Dash, Streamlit, or similar tools. Demonstrated experience managing large multidisciplinary environmental datasets and conducting advanced statistical, geospatial, and temporal analyses to support peer-reviewed publications, environmental reporting, grant-funded research, and stakeholder engagement. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering at Iowa State University advances innovative solutions to challenges involving agriculture, water resources, environmental sustainability, and biological systems. Through interdisciplinary research and collaboration, faculty, staff, and students develop technologies and management practices that improve the quality of life while safeguarding natural resources. Department Unit/Website: Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering - Graduate College Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 12, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 18, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20068 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor--Technology---Urban-Analytics-and-Planning_R20075": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor: Technology - Urban Analytics and Planning",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor: Technology - Urban Analytics and Planning Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Urban Planning and Development (UPD) in the College of Design at Iowa State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in technology, urban analytics and planning. We seek a scholar and educator whose research and teaching connect data and emerging technologies to contemporary urban and regional issues. The successful candidate will strengthen the department’s capacity in planning methods while developing a forward-looking research agenda that explores how emerging technologies can enhance the ways planners understand, analyze, visualize, and shape places. This work should demonstrate careful attention to the ethical and responsible use of data and technology in planning research and practice. Areas of Interest This position provides an opportunity to strengthen and modernize core departmental capacity in planning methods while building new strength in AI, urban analytics, visualization, and using technology in planning. Areas of research and teaching interest may include: urban analytics and data-driven planning, artificial intelligence and emerging technologies in planning, PlanTech and digital planning tools, quantitative planning methods, data visualization and geovisualization, emerging issues in technology and planning, and ethical and responsible applications of AI and data in planning. The position is intended to connect analytical and technological innovation with planning practice. Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: Develop and maintain a nationally recognized program of research and scholarship, including pursuing external funding appropriate to the defined research agenda. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in planning methods, urban analytics, technology in planning, and/or related areas. Contribute to other planning courses, studios, and other departmental curricular needs. Integrate emerging technologies and contemporary analytical methods into planning education. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students and serve on graduate thesis committees. Collaborate with faculty across the College of Design, ISU Extension and other units at Iowa State University. Contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service.   In addition, faculty in UPD have an opportunity to work with ISU Extension and Outreach, Community and Economic Development, during the summer. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in urban and regional planning, community and regional planning, geography, urban studies, or a closely related field by the time of appointment.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of potential for effective undergraduate and graduate teaching. Research and teaching expertise in two or more of the following: urban analytics, AI and emerging planning technologies, quantitative methods, and data visualization. Evidence of potential to develop a strong program of research and scholarship and secure external research funding. Experience with interdisciplinary, applied, or community-engaged research. Experience integrating emerging technologies into teaching and/or professional planning practice.   Department/Program & College Description: About Department of Urban Planning and Development The Department of Urban Planning and Development (UPD) at Iowa State University prepares students to address the complex challenges facing cities, towns, and regions. Through teaching, research, and community engagement, UPD faculty focus on areas such as land-use planning, housing, transportation, community and economic development, environmental resilience, local governance and planning technologies, with a strong emphasis on applying planning knowledge to real-world community needs. Please visit the departmental website for more information: https://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/upd/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: The guaranteed consideration date is December 15, 2026 and application reviews will continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027 . Candidates should submit: 1) Letter of application describing their interest in the position and alignment with research and teaching responsibilities. 2) Curriculum vitae. 3) Research statement describing current scholarships, future research and funding agenda. 4) Teaching statement describing teaching philosophy. 5) Contact information for three professional references. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Carlton Basmajian , Search Committee Chair, at carlton@iastate.edu . Questions about the application process may be directed to employment@iastate.edu or 515-294-4800. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20075 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoc-Research-Associate---Plasmodium-Cell-Biology_R20072": {
      "title": "Postdoc Research Associate – Plasmodium Cell Biology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoc Research Associate – Plasmodium Cell Biology Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will lead, and support research focused on Plasmodium falciparum cell biology, with an emphasis on gametogenesis and malaria transmission. The successful candidate will develop and conduct independent research utilizing genetic, molecular, and microscopy-based approaches to investigate parasite development and fertility. Responsibilities include experimental design, data analysis, preparation of manuscripts and reports, presentation of research findings, and contribution to grant-funded projects. The position will also provide opportunities to mentor undergraduate and graduate students while working in a collaborative research environment focused on advancing the understanding of malaria parasite biology and identifying innovative approaches to disease intervention. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Life Sciences or a closely related field by the start date. Evidence of first-author publications in peer-reviewed scholarly journals. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in genetic manipulation and microscopy-based imaging approaches. Research experience in molecular parasitology, molecular genetics, RNA biology, chromatin biology, or related disciplines. Department/Program & College Description: Department of Biomedical Sciences, College of Veterinary Medicine, Iowa State University. The department conducts innovative research and graduate training in cellular, molecular, and biomedical sciences to advance animal and human health. Department Unit/Website: Biomedical Sciences - Biomedical Sciences Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: December 1, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 23, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20072 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Violence-Prevention-Specialist_R20032": {
      "title": "Violence Prevention Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Violence Prevention Specialist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 3 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Are you passionate about creating a holistic student experience that supports mental, physical, and emotional wellbeing? Are you interested in an opportunity where you get to engage with students and help them reach their full potential—academically and beyond? If so, Student Wellness with the Division of Student Affairs at Iowa State University is currently seeking applicants for a Violence Prevention Specialist. This individual plays a key role in advancing student health and wellbeing through strategic communication, data-informed storytelling, and health promotion initiatives. This position will be hired as a Wellness Program Specialist II. This position will focus on violence prevention education and outreach. This position includes work in areas such as sexual violence, stalking, and hazing. What You’ll Do: Develop, implement, and evaluate violence prevention and health promotion programs, initiatives, and educational campaigns Plan, facilitate, and assess trainings, workshops, presentations, and outreach efforts focused on violence prevention, consent education, bystander intervention, and student wellbeing Coordinate and support campus-wide prevention initiatives, awareness campaigns, events, and programs that foster a safe and healthy campus community Build and maintain collaborative partnerships with campus departments, student groups, community organizations, and external stakeholders to advance prevention efforts Support the implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of university violence prevention strategies, programs, and strategic priorities Recruit, train, supervise, and support peer educators and student leaders engaged in prevention education and outreach activities Develop and disseminate educational materials, resources, digital content, and marketing strategies to increase awareness, engagement, and access to support services Collect, analyze, and report program data and assessment outcomes to measure effectiveness, demonstrate impact, and inform continuous improvement Serve on university and community committees, workgroups, and collaborative initiatives that support prevention, safety, and wellbeing goals Occasional weekend/evening hours will be involved in this role. Preferred Qualifications: Specialized training or coursework in violence prevention, sexual assault prevention, healthy relationships, etc. Certification in bystander intervention, violence prevention, trauma-informed practices, or similar prevention-focused approaches. Experience facilitating workshops, presentations and health promotion training. Experience coordinating, facilitating, and training teams; preferably focused on prevention education and outreach efforts. Experience using tools such as Smartsheet and/or Qualtrics. Department Description: Student Wellness at Iowa State University provides leadership in university strategy for health promotion and provides support programs aimed at creating a campus culture of wellbeing so that all students can thrive. Student Wellness plans, implements, and evaluates health education and prevention strategies that focus on health and wellness issues that directly affect student success, higher learning, and personal development such as: violence prevention, suicide, mental health, substance use, and more. To learn more, please visit Student Wellness . This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before October 23rd, 2026. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: October 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20032 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Financial-Aid-Technical-Lead_R20051": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Technical Lead",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Financial Aid Technical Lead Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Power the systems that help students move forward. Iowa State University is seeking a Financial Aid Technical Lead (Business Systems Analyst III) to guide the technology behind a critical part of the student experience: financing a college education. Your work will strengthen the systems that support financial aid and scholarships, helping our Cyclones in the Making—and current students—pursue their Iowa State education.   We’re a “creative yes” organization. We approach challenges with curiosity, explore what’s possible, and work together to find a path forward. If you enjoy solving complex problems and building technology solutions with a clear human purpose, you’ll find meaningful work here.   Your impact You’ll serve as the functional and technical owner of Student Financial Aid systems, connecting financial aid needs with reliable, effective technology. Working with Financial Aid leadership, Enrollment Solutions, campus technology teams, and vendors, you will: Own and improve essential systems. Guide the configuration, administration, and integration of financial aid and scholarship platforms, collaborating with campus partners on Workday Student. Turn needs into solutions. Translate business requirements into technical plans, build automated processes, and develop queries, reports, and dashboards that support financial aid operations. Keep services dependable. Troubleshoot complex issues, monitor system performance, and address process gaps before they disrupt work. Lead change with confidence. Coordinate upgrades, regulatory updates, testing, and releases while supporting compliance, security, and data governance requirements. Move projects forward. Lead financial aid technology initiatives from planning through implementation, coordinating resources, dependencies, and stakeholder communication. Help people succeed. Serve as a trusted technical resource, create clear documentation, and train staff to make effective use of new tools and functionality.   What will help you thrive You combine technical judgment with an understanding of financial aid processes and the people who depend on them. You’re comfortable investigating a system issue, translating a complex requirement, and helping colleagues understand what comes next. You build strong partnerships, anticipate challenges, and balance opportunities for improvement with the precision that financial aid work demands.   Why Iowa State Behind every financial aid process is a student making decisions about their future. Your expertise will help keep those processes reliable and responsive while giving staff better tools to support students.   You’ll have opportunities to shape essential technology, guide projects across teams, and see your solutions become part of everyday university operations. Conferences, training, and a national peer network will support your continued professional growth.   Bring your technical expertise and instinct for solving problems. Help us make the path forward clearer for students.   Preferred Qualifications: Experience translating business requirements into technical solutions Previous experience in a higher education setting Enrollment management experience Experience with Workday, Docfinity, and/or NextGen   For more information about what Enrollment Solutions does, please visit: https://www.iastate.edu/admission-and-aid   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS811 Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20051 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Project-Manager-Enrollment-Solutions_R20050": {
      "title": "Project Manager Enrollment Solutions",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Project Manager Enrollment Solutions Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 8 years of related experience Job Description: Move ideas forward. Help shape the student experience. Iowa State University is seeking a Project Manager (Program Specialist IV) to turn Enrollment Management priorities into results. As part of our Enrollment Solutions team, you’ll lead complex initiatives, connect people and technology, and improve enrollment processes that support our Cyclones in the Making.   We’re a “creative yes” organization. We approach challenges with curiosity, explore what’s possible, and work together to find a path forward. If you enjoy bringing clarity to complexity and helping ambitious ideas take shape, you’ll find meaningful work here. Your impact You’ll shape both the projects we deliver and how we deliver them. Working with Enrollment Management leadership, campus partners, technical teams, and vendors, you will: Build stronger project practices. Develop standards, tools, and processes for evaluating, prioritizing, and managing work across Enrollment Management. Turn strategy into action. Lead projects from planning through implementation, defining scope, schedules, budgets, resources, and outcomes. Keep priorities moving. Coordinate a portfolio of initiatives, anticipate risks and dependencies, and help leaders make informed decisions. Connect people and technology. Guide cross-functional teams through system implementations, integrations, and operational improvements. Make change successful. Coordinate communication, testing, training, and launch readiness, then measure adoption and results. Make progress clear. Create dashboards and reporting that highlight accomplishments, risks, and decisions needed.   What will help you thrive You bring structure to complex work and build trust across teams. You ask thoughtful questions, communicate clearly with technical and nontechnical partners, and balance big-picture priorities with the details that keep projects moving. You find practical paths through challenges and help people embrace new ways of working.   Why Iowa State Your work will help create a smoother, more connected experience for Cyclones in the Making as they explore Iowa State and take their next steps toward becoming students.   You’ll have opportunities to influence how Enrollment Management works, partner with university leaders and specialists, and see ideas through to everyday use. Conferences, training, and a national peer network will support your continued professional growth.   Bring your curiosity, judgment, and ability to make things happen. Help us turn a creative yes into meaningful progress. Preferred Qualifications: Significant project management experience Previous experience in a higher education setting Enrollment management experience For more information about what Enrollment Solutions does, please visit: https://www.iastate.edu/admission-and-aid Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS811 Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20050 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Enrollment-Reporting-Lead_R20053": {
      "title": "Enrollment Reporting Lead",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Enrollment Reporting Lead Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Turn data into understanding. Help shape what comes next.   Iowa State University is seeking an Enrollment Reporting Lead to help teams turn complex data into clear insights and informed decisions. Your work will support recruitment, enrollment planning, and student success—helping us better serve our Cyclones in the Making and the students they become.    We’re a “creative yes” organization. We approach challenges with curiosity, explore what’s possible, and work together to find a path forward. If you enjoy uncovering what people need to know and building the tools that help them act, you’ll find meaningful work here.    Your impact   You’ll serve as Enrollment Management’s primary data storyteller, lead a reporting team, and shape how enrollment information is delivered and understood. Working across Admissions, the Registrar’s Office, Financial Aid, and campus partners, you will:  Make data meaningful. Translate complex enrollment information into clear, accurate, visually compelling reports and dashboards that help people make decisions.  Build useful solutions. Develop SQL queries, automated reports, and dashboards using tools such as Excel, Salesforce, and Power BI. Turn recurring requests into reliable, accessible reporting.  Connect questions to answers. Guide reporting requests from intake through delivery, clarifying needs, setting priorities, and keeping partners informed.  Lead and develop people. Supervise, coach, and support reporting staff, creating clear expectations and opportunities to grow.  Deliver reporting projects. Coordinate requirements, timelines, testing, and stakeholder input for cross-functional dashboards, executive analytics, and regulatory reporting support.  Build confidence in the data. Lead development of an Enrollment Management data dictionary, establish consistent definitions with campus partners, and help colleagues use reporting tools effectively.    What will help you thrive   You pair technical skill with a storyteller’s instinct. You ask thoughtful questions, care about accuracy, and explain findings in ways that resonate with different audiences. You bring a project leader’s discipline to the work by turning requests into clear plans, coordinating people and priorities, and following through from initial requirements to a tested, useful solution. You communicate proactively, address roadblocks, and keep projects moving. You enjoy developing people as much as improving processes and can balance immediate reporting needs with solutions that make everyone’s work easier over time.    Why Iowa State   Your work will help university leaders and campus teams understand enrollment trends, evaluate strategies, and make decisions that support students throughout their Iowa State experience.  You’ll have opportunities to shape reporting practices across Enrollment Management, develop your team, and see your work inform university decisions. Conferences, training, and a national peer network will support your continued professional growth.  Bring your curiosity, technical expertise, and talent for making data make sense. Help us turn insight into action.    Preferred Qualifications:    Experience with higher education or Enrollment Management data.  Experience with data governance, data dictionaries, or data quality.  Experience supervising, mentoring, or developing staff.  Experience applying data visualization and user-centered design principles to create clear, intuitive, and effective reports and dashboards.  Experience leading and managing projects from conception through development, implementation, and completion. About Enrollment Management Enrollment Management brings together key university functions that support students throughout their enrollment journey, including Admissions, Financial Aid, and the Registrar. The division works collaboratively across campus to recruit and enroll students, support their success, and provide the information and services they need from application through graduation. By connecting people, processes, technology, and data across these areas, Enrollment Management plays an important role in helping the university understand its enrollment landscape and make informed decisions that support students and institutional goals. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20053 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Track-or-Tenure-Track---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor---Anatomic-Pathology_R20034": {
      "title": "Clinical Track or Tenure Track - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Anatomic Pathology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Track or Tenure Track - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Anatomic Pathology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Veterinary Pathology in the College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University (ISU) invites applications for a full-time, clinical-track or tenure-track faculty position in Anatomic Pathology at the Assistant, Associate, or Professor level. Appointment rank and track will be based on the selected candidate’s qualifications, documented experience, and interests.  The successful candidate will join 6 ACVP Anatomic Pathologists, 3 ACVP Clinical Pathologists, 2 ACVM Veterinary Parasitologists and 1 specialist in medical education assessment.  This position has a primary commitment to teaching and professional practice. This position is devoted primarily to teaching and professional practice, with a limited portion of effort allocated to research and scholarly activities. The specific distribution of responsibilities will be established with the department chair based on departmental needs, appointment track, and the successful candidate’s qualifications and interests. The successful candidate will participate in the department’s surgical biopsy and necropsy services. The biopsy service receives submissions from the ISU Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC) and practicing veterinarians in the surrounding region. The necropsy service evaluates diverse species submitted through the LVMC small and large animal clinics. Responsibilities include diagnostic interpretation and communication of findings to clinicians and referring veterinarians, with an emphasis on accurate, timely, and clinically useful reports. Teaching responsibilities include instruction of senior veterinary students and pathology residents through diagnostic service, including necropsy techniques, lesion recognition and interpretation, and clinicopathologic correlation. The successful candidate will also contribute to didactic and laboratory instruction in anatomic pathology and related disciplines for undergraduate, professional (DVM), and graduate students, as assigned, and participate in resident training and mentorship. The successful candidate will advance anatomic pathology through scholarship appropriate to the appointment track and assigned effort. Clinical-track scholarship may include case reports, case series, educational scholarship, and collaborative research. Tenure-track faculty are expected to contribute anatomic pathology expertise to research collaborations resulting in peer-reviewed publications. Scholarly expectations will be consistent with the position’s substantial teaching and professional practice commitment. The successful candidate will demonstrate a collegial and collaborative approach, effective communication with learners and veterinary colleagues, and commitment to student education. All faculty are expected to uphold high standards of integrity and ethics, contribute to a positive work environment, and approach clients and patients with professionalism and compassion. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent degree. Board certification in anatomic pathology through the American College of Veterinary Pathologists (ACVP), European College of Veterinary Pathologists (ECVP), or Japanese College of Veterinary Pathologists (JCVP). In addition to the requirements above, the following minimum qualifications apply by rank and track: Clinical Associate Professor. A graduate degree; Diplomate status in anatomic pathology in the ACVP, ECVP, or JCVP; and a minimum of five years of professional practice experience emphasizing companion animal, production animal, and equine pathology. Clinical Professor . A graduate degree; and a minimum of ten years of professional practice experience emphasizing companion animal, production animal and equine pathology.   Assistant Professor on the tenure track. A PhD.   Associate Professor on the tenure track. A PhD; a minimum of five years of professional practice experience emphasizing companion animal, production animal, and equine pathology; a record of scholarship and teaching; and experience with resident training. Professor . A PhD; and a minimum of ten years of professional practice experience emphasizing companion animal, production animal and equine pathology; a record of scholarship and teaching; and experience with resident training. Candidates for appointment at the Associate Professor and Professor level must demonstrate accomplishments in scholarship, teaching, and clinical service appropriate to the rank and appointment track.   Preferred Qualifications: Experience in diagnostic anatomic pathology, including biopsy and necropsy services involving companion animals, production animals, and horses. Experience teaching anatomic pathology in didactic, laboratory, or clinical settings. Research experience demonstrated through publications, grants, or graduate student mentorship. An MS, PhD, or equivalent graduate degree in veterinary pathology, microbiology, virology, education, or a related veterinary field, where not already required for the appointment rank.   Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Veterinary Pathology contributes to the teaching, professional practice, and research missions of the ISU College of Veterinary Medicine. Its diagnostic services support patient care through the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center and provide opportunities for instruction of veterinary students and pathology residents. Departmental research areas include animal models of human disease, infectious diseases, carcinogenesis, toxicology, host-pathogen interactions, parasitology, educational scholarship, and comparative pathology.   The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center provides specialized care and comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion and large animals from Iowa and surrounding states. Clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and veterinary students work collaboratively in patient care and clinical education. As the nation’s first public veterinary school, Iowa State University’s College of Veterinary Medicine has a longstanding commitment to veterinary professional practice, education, research, and service. The college works to improve the health and well-being of animals and people. Iowa State University is located in Ames, Iowa, approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines.   Department Unit/Website: Department of Veterinary Pathology: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vpath/ College of Veterinary Medicine: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of application addressing the required and preferred qualifications and including a statement of teaching. 3) Contact Information for Three Professional References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before November 08, 2026. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20034 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Marketing-Specialist-III_R20040": {
      "title": "Marketing Specialist III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Marketing Specialist III Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Shape the Future of Graduate Education Marketing The Graduate College at Iowa State University is seeking a strategic marketing and communications professional to lead marketing efforts that advance graduate education, support enrollment goals, and strengthen the College’s visibility and reputation. Working independently under broad direction, this position develops and implements integrated marketing strategies that engage prospective and current graduate students, faculty, staff, alumni, and external partners. The Marketing Specialist III serves as a key marketing liaison with Enrollment Management and University Marketing and Communications and collaborates across academic colleges, graduate programs, and university partners to support recruitment, student success, and institutional priorities. The successful candidate will bring strategic thinking, strong communication and organizational skills, and the ability to translate complex academic and research topics into compelling communications for a range of audiences. What You’ll Do Establish and implement a unified marketing and communications vision for the Graduate College that aligns with university-wide enrollment and branding objectives. Develop a compelling and differentiated Graduate College brand narrative that supports Iowa State University's strategic priorities and graduate enrollment goals. Create integrated marketing plans that support graduate student recruitment, enrollment growth, retention, engagement, and program visibility. Utilize enrollment trends, audience insights, market research, and performance metrics to inform marketing strategy and decision-making. Build strong collaborative partnerships with Enrollment Management, academic colleges, and university marketing leaders to provide seamless and student-centered experience. Identify opportunities to strengthen alignment between Graduate College marketing efforts and broader university recruitment, marketing, and communication initiatives.   Why You’ll Love This Role This new role offers the opportunity to make a significant contribution to the Graduate College and help shape its marketing and communications efforts. You’ll join a close-knit team that values collaboration, strong working relationships, and supporting one another. With a lot of opportunities to build and strengthen the Graduate College’s marketing presence, you’ll have the chance to develop strategies and initiatives that support graduate enrollment, engagement, and the College’s broader goals. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, journalism, public relations, or a related field. Experience developing and leading integrated marketing or communications strategies from planning through execution and evaluation. Experience creating and managing content across websites, social media, email, and other digital channels. Experience using analytics, audience insights, market research, or other data to inform marketing strategy and evaluate results. Experience building collaborative partnerships across teams or organizations to advance shared goals. Experience developing marketing or communications strategies that support enrollment, recruitment, engagement, or other organizational goals.   This is a 3-year term position that may have the possibility of renewal. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: November 8, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 18, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20040 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Research-Technician-II_R20042": {
      "title": "Research Technician II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Research Technician II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 3 years of related experience Job Description: The Department of Animal Science at Iowa State University is seeking a Research Technician II to support innovative research investigating how environmental exposures, including per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS), affect ovarian function and reproductive health. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to research with potential implications for human health, addressing important questions in reproductive health that affect roughly half of the population, while developing expertise across animal research, molecular and cellular laboratory techniques, and research data analysis. You'll join a team that invests in professional development, provides opportunities to work with researchers across Iowa State and other universities, and supports individual career goals. You'll be part of a collaborative environment where strong organization, communication, and teamwork are essential to keeping research moving forward. What You'll Do Coordinate laboratory activities, prepare reagents and experimental materials, and maintain accurate research records and inventories. Perform animal research procedures, including dosing, breeding colony management, tissue collection, necropsy support, and biological sample processing in accordance with approved research protocols. Conduct molecular and cellular laboratory techniques such as RNA isolation, protein extraction, Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, histological processing, microscopy, and follicle quantification. Collect, organize, analyze, and maintain research data from animal studies and laboratory experiments, ensuring data quality, accuracy, and integrity. Prepare datasets, summaries, figures, and reports to support research publications, presentations, grant reporting, and other project needs. Operate, calibrate, maintain, and troubleshoot laboratory instrumentation and specialized research equipment, addressing technical issues that may affect experimental outcomes. Assist with developing, optimizing, and validating laboratory protocols and research methods and recommend improvements to laboratory processes. Train and provide technical guidance to undergraduate researchers, graduate students, and other laboratory personnel on research techniques, laboratory procedures, and safety practices. Communicate research findings, technical concerns, and recommendations with the principal investigator and research team. Preferred Qualifications : Bachelor's degree in biology, animal science, biochemistry, molecular biology, reproductive physiology, or a related field. Experience with molecular or cellular laboratory techniques such as RNA isolation, protein extraction, Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, histology, or microscopy. Experience with animal handling, dosing, tissue collection, or other animal-based research procedures. Experience collecting, organizing, analyzing, or interpreting research data. Experience troubleshooting laboratory procedures, assays, or research equipment. Experience training or providing technical guidance to students or other laboratory personnel. This is a term appointment that may have opportunity for renewal. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: November 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS805 Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 21, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20042 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-GDCB_R20038": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor GDCB",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor GDCB Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Genetics, Development and Cell Biology (GDCB) at Iowa State University seeks to hire an assistant professor to start in August 2027. The faculty member should use model organisms such as zebrafish, Drosophila and/or human cell and organoid systems to investigate the molecular mechanisms underlying the cell and developmental biology of human health and disease . Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, developmental and cell biology, cancer biology, neurobiology, stem cell biology, and related fields. Research interests that integrate modern experimental biology, including genome engineering and single cell biology, with emerging computational approaches such as artificial intelligence (AI) will be given priority. The new faculty member will also contribute to undergraduate and graduate education by teaching Biology, Genetics, or Integrated Health Sciences courses and/or developing new offerings in their area of interest that integrates AI, quantitative biology, and modern biomedical research. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD or equivalent in biological sciences before August 16, 2027   Preferred Qualifications: Research experience aligned with position description Well-developed research plan Postdoctoral training with evidence of independent research Strong supporting publications Potential to secure external funding Potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring   Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Genetics, Development, and Cell Biology (GDCB) at Iowa State University advances life sciences through innovative research, personalized education, and interdisciplinary collaboration. We investigate the genetic, molecular and cellular foundations of life to prepare the next generation of leaders and professionals to address global challenges in biotechnology, medicine, health, food security, and sustainable agriculture. Our dynamic programs bridge scientific discovery with real-world impact, empowering all students to shape a healthier and more resilient future.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.gdcb.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum Vitae (CV) 3. Research plan (no more than 3 pages) 4. Teaching statement and/or interests (1 page) 5. Names and contact information of 3-5 references If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before December 01, 2026. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20038 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Occupational-Safety-Specialist-I_R20052": {
      "title": "Occupational Safety Specialist I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Occupational Safety Specialist I Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Job Description: Iowa State University is seeking an Occupational Safety Specialist I to play a vital role in campus emergency preparedness, recovery, mitigation and occupational safety programs. In this position, you will help strengthen the University's ability to prepare for, respond to, and recover from emergencies while promoting a safe learning, research, and work environment. Working closely with faculty, staff, students, campus leadership, and external emergency responders, you will support preparedness initiatives, lead training and exercises, conduct safety inspections, and contribute to programs that protect people, property, and University operations. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who is passionate about emergency management, safety, and public service and wants to make a meaningful impact across a large and diverse campus community. What You'll Do Support the University's Emergency Operations Plan by maintaining emergency planning documents, coordinating preparedness activities, and assisting campus stakeholders in emergency readiness efforts. Develop, coordinate, and deliver emergency preparedness training, tabletop exercises, drills, Emergency Operations Center training, after-action reports, and corrective action plans. Conduct life safety and occupational safety inspections to identify hazards, evaluate compliance, and recommend corrective actions. Support fire and life safety programs through building inspections, fire pump testing, evacuation planning, emergency drills, and safety signage reviews. Administer the campus fire extinguisher program, including inspection, maintenance coordination, inventory management, recordkeeping, and compliance tracking. Supervise and direct student employees who assist with fire extinguisher inspections and related program activities. Collaborate with university departments to assess emergency planning needs and prepare for incidents involving fire, chemical, biological, radiological, compressed gas, and other hazards. Develop and maintain emergency procedures, guidance documents, compliance materials, and safety resources. Respond to campus emergencies and support emergency operations in coordination with university leadership, public safety personnel, and external emergency response agencies. Participate in after-hours emergency response activities and serve in an on-call duty officer capacity as assigned. Additional Information This position is 100% on-site and based in Ames, Iowa with no opportunity for remote work. Standard work hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Due to the nature of emergency preparedness and response operations, occasional evening, weekend, holiday, and after-hours work may be required. This position serves as a departmental Duty Officer for designated periods throughout the year and is responsible for coordinating emergency response activities outside of normal business hours during assigned rotations. Why Iowa State? Your work will directly contribute to the safety, preparedness, and resilience of one of the nation's leading public research universities. From coordinating emergency response efforts to helping departments prepare for potential hazards, you will have the opportunity to make a visible impact while building strong partnerships across the University community. Preferred Qualifications : Education in Emergency Management, Occupational Safety, Environmental Health and Safety (EHS), Fire Protection, Public Safety, Homeland Security, or a related field. Experience participating in emergency preparedness activities, drills, exercises, emergency response operations, or incident management. Experience conducting safety inspections, hazard assessments, compliance reviews, or risk identification activities. Knowledge of emergency management, occupational safety, or fire and life safety principles, including familiarity with OSHA, NFPA, NIMS, or ICS concepts. Experience maintaining records, databases, reports, or documentation related to safety, compliance, emergency management, or operational programs. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: October 7, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 21, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20052 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Pre-Award-Grants-Specialist-II_R20037": {
      "title": "Pre-Award Grants Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Pre-Award Grants Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Thrive in a dynamic environment where you can manage a variety of projects while playing a key role in advancing impactful research in renewable resources, food, energy, bioproducts, and associated services? Are you looking for a role that offers variety, challenge, and the opportunity to contribute to the success of cutting-edge research? If so, the Bioeconomy Institute (BEI) at Iowa State University is hiring a Pre-Award Grants Specialist II position! This position will manage all outgoing proposal activity for the institute, coordinating many simultaneous submissions with a variety of internal/external faculty, staff, departments, collaborators, & agencies. Proposals may vary significantly in size and complexity, ranging from small, single-PI submissions to multi-million-dollar transdisciplinary research efforts. This position will be classified as a Grants Specialist II. What You'll Do: Represent the Bioeconomy Institute as a first point of contact for all new proposal efforts, liaising between ISU Principal Investigators (PIs) & collaborators and other ISU departments. Provide services tailored to each proposal team, based on PI experience, communication style and preferences. Prepare and revise budgets and budget justifications for large, complex research proposals. Proposal routing in coordination with the Office of Sponsored Programs Administration. Develop action-item focused timelines and checklists of required documentation. Collect, draft, and distribute templates; prepare forms and attachments for submission. Pre-submission, financial and administrative (non-technical) review of application package for completeness. Proposal file uploads and final submission to a variety of federal and non-federal web portals. Work with BEI administration to market pre-award services to new and existing internal customers. Contribute to process improvement and assist institute administration and post-award counterpart during annual reviews and as needed, providing proposal statistics and trends. Locate and/or review funding opportunities aligned with institute priorities, disseminate to institute affiliates. This position is a key contributor to the BEI administrative, shared services team and will provide support to our interdisciplinary research teams. Candidates should possess excellent written and verbal communication skills, the ability to work independently and manage competing priorities while meeting deadlines, and a strong attention to detail. Additional strengths include effective time management, adaptability, and the ability to perform successfully in both high-volume and low-volume work environments. This is a two-year fixed term position with the opportunity for renewal. Preferred Qualifications: Experience supporting proposal development activities, including preparation, coordination, review, and submission of grant or sponsored project proposals. Experience developing, reviewing, or managing budgets related to grants, contracts, sponsored projects, or other complex funding sources. Experience working directly with faculty, researchers, principal investigators, industry contacts, or research support staff in a higher education, government, or research setting. Certified Research Administrator (CRA), Certified Pre-Award Research Administrator (CPRA), or related professional certification; or active progress toward obtaining certification. Knowledge of Uniform Guidance (2 CFR 200), federal sponsor regulations, and/or policies and procedures related to sponsored funding administration. About Iowa State University Centers and Institutes and the Bioeconomy Institute: Centers and Institutes at Iowa State University bring together faculty, staff, students, and external partners to advance research and engagement around shared areas of expertise. While similar to academic departments in their focus on specific subject areas, centers and institutes are designed to be flexible and collaborative, emphasizing transdisciplinary research, external partnerships and funding, and connections between the university and industry, government, and community stakeholders rather than administering degree programs. The Bioeconomy Institute is a national leader in advancing the bioeconomy, \"where society obtains food, energy, bioproducts, and associated services from renewable sources.\" Celebrating more than 20 years as the \"front door\" to biorenewables at Iowa State University, the institute fosters collaboration among departments, colleges, and research units across campus. Together with more than 50 industry partners and over 150 affiliated faculty and staff, the institute drives innovation and research focused on renewable resources, including feedstock development, waste utilization, biobased products, and related services. To learn more, please visit the Bioeconomy Institute website . Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: November 29, 2028 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: October 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 19, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20037 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-of-Criminal-Justice_R20044": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Criminal Justice, as a 9-month position, starting August 16, 2027. The Department is particularly interested in candidates with research and/or teaching experience in the area of emerging technologies in criminal justice (e.g., artificial intelligence, digital forensics, surveillance, etc.), especially as used in policing and courts.   The successful candidate will have a strong research portfolio and demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate criminal justice courses, with modalities as determined by the department (in-person, hybrid, or online); developing and maintaining an excellent, nationally recognized research program; contributing service to the department and the broader discipline; and pursuing external research funding.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.     Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Criminology/Criminal Justice or a closely related discipline by the appointment start date   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of high quality, peer-reviewed publications in criminology/criminal justice Expertise in the area of emerging technologies in criminal justice (e.g., artificial intelligence, digital forensics, surveillance, etc.). Record of highly effective undergraduate teaching in criminal justice, supported by student/peer evaluations and/or applicant statement of teaching philosophy Potential to secure external funding from federal/state agencies, private sector, and/or foundations   Department/Program & College Description: The Department’s ( http://www.soc-cj.iastate.edu/ ) current and future research, teaching, and extension scholarship is centered on creating new knowledge and preparing the next generation of scientists, teachers, professionals, and citizens to apply social science skills to societal challenges. The Department has a pedagogical mission to prepare undergraduate and graduate students with skills to launch professional careers that address the major challenges of society and engage in civic life as well-educated global citizens. The Criminal Justice program enrolls more than 400 majors and minors.    Department Unit/Website: http://www.soc-cj.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter that briefly discusses how the applicant aligns with each of the preferred qualifications, especially a substantive focus on emerging technologies in criminal justice; specific sections should address research (e.g., research interests and publication experience, potential for grant-funding including trainings and/or experience with previous funded projects) and teaching in criminal justice (e.g., supported by student/peer evaluations and/or applicant statement of teaching philosophy) 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before November 1, 2026. This position is open untill filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20044 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate-in-Electrochemical-Engineering_R20055": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Electrochemical Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate in Electrochemical Engineering Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to support research focused on NOx electrooxidation and electrolyzer development as part of the DARPA program. The successful candidate will advance innovative electrochemical technologies through catalyst and electrode development, reactor design and optimization, and analytical evaluation of reaction products to enhance nitrate and nitric acid production processes. The research will involve synthesizing and characterizing carbon-based electrodes and catalysts, evaluating electrochemical reactions in flow-cell systems, optimizing electrode structure and reaction environments to improve product yield, and performing product quantification using analytical techniques such as NMR, UV-Vis, HPLC-MS, GC-MS, and DEMS. The successful candidate will be a self-motivated researcher with a strong desire to pursue scientific and technical breakthroughs, possess excellent written and verbal communication skills, and demonstrate the ability to work effectively in a collaborative research environment. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications: Strong background in electrochemistry, electrocatalysis, materials synthesis, and characterization. Experience synthesizing and characterizing carbon-based electrodes and catalysts. Experience evaluating electrochemical reactions in flow-cell systems. Ability to optimize electrode structure and reaction environments to improve product yield. Experience with analytical techniques such as NMR, UV-Vis, HPLC-MS, GC-MS, and/or DEMS. Department/Program & College Description: This is where you can impact the world in countless ways – because chemical engineering is involved with nearly every aspect of your life. Foods. Fuels. Renewable energy. Consumer products of all kinds. Medical and health care technology, and more. Discover how many ways your career in the making can start here! Department Unit/Website: Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering – College of Engineering, Iowa State University Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 20, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20055 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Ovarian-Biology-and-Toxicology_R20036": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ovarian Biology and Toxicology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ovarian Biology and Toxicology Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will contribute to a collaborative research program focused on understanding the molecular and phenotypic ovarian responses to PFAS exposure. The successful candidate will conduct animal exposure studies, perform ex vivo ovary culture experiments, and collect phenotypic and biochemical data. Responsibilities include molecular analyses, ovarian follicle assessment, steroid hormone quantification, experimental design, data analysis, manuscript preparation, and training and mentoring graduate students. The position also includes maintaining detailed research records, managing laboratory sample inventories, and supporting a collaborative research environment. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Reproductive Biology, Toxicology or related field.  Preferred Qualifications: Experience in ovarian biology, female reproductive biology, and/or toxicology. Experience with animal handling, exposure studies, and biological data collection. Experience performing molecular laboratory analyses, including western blotting and immunofluorescent staining. Experience with histology, ovarian follicle counting, and/or ex vivo ovary culture. Experience with statistical analysis and coding in Python or R, bioinformatic analyses, and/or proteomic analyses.     Department/Program & College Description: Our commitment is to educate and prepare students for productive and gratifying careers in animal production, veterinary medicine and the diverse areas of animal business and industry. Instruction, research and outreach programs are led by 46 faculty , many of whom are internationally recognized, with expertise in breeding and genetics, genomics, nutrition, physiology, meat science and meat processing, animal well-being and management. These programs and disciplinary focus areas include beef cattle, dairy cattle, horses, poultry, swine, sheep, companion animals, laboratory animals and zoo animals. Department Unit/Website: Department of Animal Science Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: November 16, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 6, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20036 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---PFAS-Analytical-Chemistry_R20035": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - PFAS Analytical Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - PFAS Analytical Chemistry Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will contribute to a collaborative, multidisciplinary research program focused on understanding the molecular and phenotypic ovarian responses to PFAS exposure. The successful candidate will conduct animal exposure studies, perform molecular and analytical laboratory techniques, and support the collection, analysis, and interpretation of research data. Responsibilities include PFAS quantification using HPLC-MS/MS and LC-MS/MS, molecular analyses, steroid hormone quantification, experimental design, and manuscript preparation. The position also includes maintaining detailed research records, managing laboratory sample inventories, and training and mentoring graduate students in a collaborative research environment. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Reproductive Biology, Toxicology or related field.  Preferred Qualifications: Experience in analytical chemistry, including HPLC-MS/MS, LC-MS/MS, and chemical extraction techniques. Experience in PFAS research and/or toxicology. Experience with animal handling, exposure studies, and biological data collection. Experience with molecular laboratory analyses, including western blotting and immunofluorescent staining. Experience with statistical analysis and coding in Python or R. Department/Program & College Description: Our commitment is to educate and prepare students for productive and gratifying careers in animal production, veterinary medicine and the diverse areas of animal business and industry. Instruction, research and outreach programs are led by 46 faculty , many of whom are internationally recognized, with expertise in breeding and genetics, genomics, nutrition, physiology, meat science and meat processing, animal well-being and management. These programs and disciplinary focus areas include beef cattle, dairy cattle, horses, poultry, swine, sheep, companion animals, laboratory animals and zoo animals. Department Unit/Website: Department of Animal Science Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: November 16, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 6, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20035 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Sprayer-Systems-and-Application-Technology-Lead_R20015": {
      "title": "Sprayer Systems and Application Technology Lead",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Sprayer Systems and Application Technology Lead Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 8 years related experience Job Description: Build the Future of Agriculture If you want your work to matter beyond the lab - on real equipment, in real farm fields, with measurable impact - this is the role for you. Who We Are The Digital Ag Innovation Lab at Iowa State University partners with leading agricultural companies to design, build, and deploy next-generation technologies for agriculture. Our team works at the intersection of applied engineering, industry collaboration, and the land-grant mission, moving ideas from concept to prototype to field deployment. Our vision is bold: to be the premiere thought leader and partner in ag innovation . Our mission guides everything we do: Innovate. Educate. Outreach . We operate with four core values: Passion. Innovation. Collaboration. Excellence . This is a place for builders, problem-solvers, and systems thinkers who want their work to move from idea → prototype → field → industry adoption. The Opportunity We are seeking a Sprayer Systems and Application Technology Lead to build and lead a growing program focused on the development, testing, and field evaluation of agricultural application systems.  This role connects application technology, agronomy, and field operations to evaluate how equipment design, application parameters, crop conditions, and management practices affect application performance and agronomic outcomes. This is not a desk-only leadership position.  Successful candidates enjoy spending time in the shop, lab, and field working directly with equipment while also leading people, projects, and sponsor relationships. Working with engineers, agronomists, researchers, and industry partners, you will lead applied research from technical requirements and prototype development through field validation and analysis.  The role combines hands-on engineering, field research, project leadership, and industry collaboration to advance liquid, dry, targeted, and variable-rate application technologies.  What You'll Do Lead development, testing, and field validation of agricultural application systems, including spray, fertilizer, and targeted delivery technologies Define technical and agronomic requirements and develop field and laboratory test methods, performance measures, and validation plans. Evaluate how application systems and operating parameters affect application performance, crop response, input use, and field productivity. Analyze field and system data to guide technology development and improve application performance. Lead and mentor engineers, technicians, students, and research staff while coordinating work across agronomy, engineering, and industry partners. Lead research projects and develop new industry opportunities, including scope, resources, budgets, schedules, sponsor communication, and delivery. What You Bring Experience with agricultural application systems, precision agriculture, agriculture equipment, agronomy, crop production, or related technology development. Working knowledge of agricultural application systems and the engineering principles affecting application performance, such as droplet size, pressure, flow, and speed. Experience with field trials, lab testing, product evaluation, or system benchmarking. Ability to connect engineering performance to agronomic outcomes. Experience leading technical projects, research initiatives, sponsor relationships, and cross-functional teams. Experience with agricultural equipment, agricultural inputs, or production agriculture. Technology & Systems You May Work With Spray systems, nozzles, pumps, and flow control Targeted and variable-rate application technologies Drone and aerial application systems Lab and field-testing platforms Agricultural equipment and precision application systems Preferred Qualifications Advanced degree in agricultural engineering, agronomy, or related field, or equivalent industry experience Background in agriculture application technology, precision agriculture, agricultural equipment, crop input technology, or related industry Experience conducting field trials, in-field testing, or performance benchmarking of ag application systems Experience defining technical requirements, planning test programs, and managing work across cross-functional projects and teams Demonstrated ability to connect engineering parameters (e.g., pressure, droplet size, duty cycle, travel speed) to biological efficacy and input-use efficiency Experience leading or mentoring cross-functional teams in lab and field environments This is a term position with the expectation of long-term renewal. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. The candidate will be hired as an R&D Engineer IV. https://digitalag.iastate.edu/ Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: October 25, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS813 Original Posting Date: October 5, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20015 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Materials-Science-and-Engineering---Assistant-Associate-Teaching-Professor_R20029": {
      "title": "Materials Science and Engineering - Assistant/Associate/Teaching Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Materials Science and Engineering - Assistant/Associate/Teaching Professor Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Materials Science & Engineering (MSE), in the College of Engineering at Iowa State University (ISU), invites applications for an open-rank term faculty position (Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor). Rank will be determined based on the successful candidate's qualifications and record of accomplishment. The appointment is anticipated to begin 16 August 2027, and the initial appointment length will be consistent with College and University policy for the rank offered. The department seeks an educator with the breadth to contribute across the undergraduate Materials Engineering curriculum. Teaching assignments will be based on departmental needs and may include introductory, core, advanced, laboratory, experiential, and design-based courses spanning the undergraduate program. The successful candidate will provide high-quality undergraduate instruction; contribute to course coordination, curriculum assessment and continuous improvement; mentor and engage students; and participate in department, college, and university service and outreach/engagement activities. Candidates should demonstrate strong communication skills, collegiality, instructional clarity, and a commitment to student learning. A central expectation is the ability and willingness to teach broadly across materials science and engineering rather than within a single specialized teaching area.   Required Minimum Qualifications: For the rank of assistant teaching professor, candidates must hold a minimum of a Master's degree in MSE, materials engineering, or a closely related engineering/science discipline and 3 years of relevant work experience or a Doctoral degree in engineering or related discipline. have demonstrated teaching or instructional experience in MSE or a related STEM field. In addition to the above, candidates seeking Associate or Full Teaching Professor rank must also have a record commensurate with appointment at that rank. Namely, Associate: Record of teaching experience and 5 years of relevant work experience beyond the requirements for assistant teaching professor. Full: Record of teaching experience and 10 years of relevant work experience beyond the requirements for assistant teaching professor. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in MSE, materials engineering, or a closely related field. Demonstrated effectiveness and breadth in undergraduate MSE instruction across multiple core subject areas, with the capacity to teach broadly across the program. Experience with laboratory, experiential, project-based, and/or design-focused engineering instruction. Experience with course coordination or development, curriculum assessment or continuous improvement, and effective use of instructional technologies. Evidence of effective student mentoring and engagement, clear (oral or written) communication, collaboration, and educational leadership or service. Experience with large-sized classes and related online-automated assessments.   Department/Program & College Description: About the Materials Science and Engineering Department: The Department of Materials Science and Engineering offers an undergraduate degree in Materials Engineering and graduate degrees in Materials Science and Engineering. The department integrates education and research across the relationships among materials structure, processing, properties, and performance, with strong emphasis on hands-on learning, materials characterization, design, student mentoring, and continuous improvement of the undergraduate curriculum.   Department Unit/Website: For more information about our department's program or people, see www.mse.iastate.edu . Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by 1 December 2026. All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu to Job Requisition Number R20029. The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format: 1) Letter of application (including the desired rank) that briefly discusses how the candidate meets each minimum and preferred qualification. 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information. 4) One-page teaching statement addressing the candidate's approach to undergraduate MSE teaching, breadth across the curriculum, hands-on laboratory learning, and experience with student learning and mentoring. Direct questions to Dr. Duane D. Johnson at ddj@iastate.edu and will be answered as is possible. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 5, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20029 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/R-D-Systems-Engineering-Lead_R20030": {
      "title": "R&D Systems Engineering Lead",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: R&D Systems Engineering Lead Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 8 years related experience Job Description: Build the Future of Agriculture If you want your engineering work to move beyond the lab—onto real machines and into real farm fields—this is the role for you. Who We Are The Digital Ag Innovation Lab partners with leading agricultural companies to imagine, design, and deploy next-generation technologies for agriculture. Our team works at the intersection of applied engineering, industry collaboration, and the land-grant mission, moving ideas from concept to prototype to field deployment and ultimately into industry adoption.    Our vision is bold: to be the premier thought leader and partner in ag innovation . Our mission guides everything we do: Innovate. Educate. Outreach .  We operate with four core values: Passion. Innovation. Collaboration. Excellence.   The Opportunity We are seeking an R&D Systems Engineering Lead to develop people, grow technical capability, and lead projects focused on the development, integration, and field validation of advanced digital agriculture systems with industry partners. As Digital Ag continues to grow, this hands-on engineering leadership role will strengthen both team capability and project execution. You will lead and develop engineers, technicians, and students, manage team capacity and resource planning, and advance technical quality while remaining actively engaged in engineering and technical decision-making. You will also lead selected projects from planning through delivery, managing schedules, resources, sponsor communication, technical decisions, and project outcomes across multiple technologies, equipment platforms, and industry sponsored programs. What You'll Do Manage, coach, mentor, and develop engineers, technicians, graduate students, and student employees through clear expectations, feedback, performance management, and professional development. Build technical capability by establishing engineering standards, best practices, knowledge sharing, and workforce development across digital systems, embedded computing, sensing, automation, robotics, connectivity, and data systems. Provide hands-on technical leadership for integrated digital agriculture systems spanning embedded systems, sensing, robotics, connectivity, computing, and agricultural equipment. Support delivery across multiple concurrent engineering efforts through project planning, estimation, technical reviews, risk management, and resource coordination. Build trusted relationships with sponsors, OEMs, technology partners, and research collaborators by aligning technical work to customer objectives and supporting reviews, roadmap planning, and future opportunities. Assess workload, capability, and staffing needs while improving technical quality, collaboration, accountability, and the processes needed to scale the organization.   What You Bring   Strong systems thinking and technical depth across integrated hardware and software systems Experience leading complex engineering work from concept through deployment or field validation Experience managing, developing, and mentoring engineers and technical staff Ability to balance competing priorities across people, projects, resources, and technical objectives Strong communication and relationship-building skills with technical teams, customers, and industry partners A hands-on leadership style centered on coaching, collaboration, ownership, and continuous improvement with the ability to balance technical work and project delivery   Preferred Qualifications Experience developing and integrating complex digital, embedded, automation, or connected systems Experience with agricultural, off-highway, automotive, robotics, or other complex equipment platforms Experience working with OEMs or industry partners on product development, applied research, or technology validation Experience leading customer-driven or externally funded engineering projects and working directly with external sponsors or customers   This is a term position with the expectation of long-term renewal. Candidate will be hied as an R&D Engineer IV. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: October 25, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS813 Original Posting Date: October 5, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20030 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Public-Safety-Security-Officer_R20098": {
      "title": "Public Safety Security Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Public Safety Security Officer Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Two years experience in security and safety, or • One year of post-high school education related to security and safety and one year of experience in security and safety, or • Two years of post-high school education related to security and safety. • Possession of appropriate driver's license as required. • Ability to obtain Certified Protection Officer certification from the International Foundation of Protection Officers and/or International Association for Healthcare Security and Safety certification within 6 months of hire and maintain certification for duration of employment. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Ames Laboratory is seeking applicants for a Public Safety Security Officer. Under general supervision, this position performs duties to protect property and provide for the safety and security of the personnel of Ames National Laboratory. Main duties include: conducting facility security/safety tours, monitoring and responding to fire/security system alarms, monitoring surveillance cameras, and performing shift-specific assignments (i.e., fire extinguisher program, first aid kit/closet inventories, emergency response equipment inspections, emergency response postings, creating incident reports, visitor and employee identification validation and providing personnel, visitor, and subcontractor escorts).   The successful candidate will need to be detail oriented and able to communicate effectively with Laboratory staff, researchers, students, visitors, and the general public.   Schedule for this position is 12:00 a.m. – 8:00 a.m. with rotating weekends and holidays. Position is eligible for a shift differential, and a valid REAL ID Driver’s License is required.   Public Safety Security Officer must be able to obtain a Certified Protection Officer through the International Foundation for Protective Officers within 6 months of starting employment.   Preferred Qualifications: Additional experience with industrial safety, fire safety, and security Experience with Simplex fire systems Experience with C-Cure security systems Experience with modern surveillance systems Department/Program & College Description: Would you like to work for a National Laboratory that conducts world-renowned research? Would you enjoy working on a beautiful university campus? Can you imagine yourself in a mid-sized location that regularly ranks as one of the U.S. Best Places to Live ? If you answered yes to any of these questions, you should consider a career with Ames National Laboratory!   Ames Laboratory is a U.S. Department of Energy federally contracted National Laboratory located in Ames, Iowa, on the campus of Iowa State University. We are dedicated to translating foundational science through applied research to create technological innovations. We create materials, inspire minds to solve problems, and address some of the most challenging issues facing our world today. Department Unit/Website (if applicable): www.ameslab.gov Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory.   Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter List of Professional References Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 08 Original Posting Date: October 16, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20098 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Graphic-Design-Assistant-II_R20091": {
      "title": "Graphic Design Assistant II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Graphic Design Assistant II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 2 years of related experience Job Description: Printing Services is seeking a Prepress & Print Design Technician II (Graphic Design Assistant II) to join our creative, fast-paced printing environment. This position combines graphic design, prepress, variable-data production, department marketing, and webstore support, including the development of dynamic product templates for online ordering. You’ll work on a wide variety of print, wide-format, mailing, and creative projects from concept through production. Working within established workflows and guidelines, you’ll independently resolve prepress issues and collaborate with customers, customer relations staff, and production teams to ensure files are accurate, consistent, and properly prepared for efficient downstream production. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in a printing services environment Experience working in a higher education environment Experience with print prepress software for digital and wide-format print production Experience with promotional and marketing materials Experience with mail list processing and variable-data printing workflows Experience with web-to-print, online ordering, or digital storefront platforms for print services About the Department: Do you enjoy a dynamic work environment where every day brings new projects and technical challenges? Are you interested in hands on work that supports meaningful communication across a large and diverse campus community? Printing Services at Iowa State University plays a critical role in supporting the university’s academic, research, and outreach missions by providing high quality print and design services. The department’s mission is to efficiently meet Iowa State’s core printing needs while delivering reliable, cost effective solutions with prompt turnaround times and top quality results. Printing Services combines technical expertise in prepress, production, and finishing with a strong focus on accuracy, accessibility, and consistency. As part of an integrated communications workflow, the department supports emerging digital print solutions, helping translate the knowledge and messaging of Iowa State University into effective visual communications for campus partners and the broader Iowa community. Team members work closely with production staff, customer-facing colleagues, and clients across campus in a collaborative, service oriented environment where precision, problem solving, and continuous improvement are valued. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by October 25, 2026. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: October 16, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20091 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Remote---Iowa/Pre-Award-Project-Manager---Grants-Hub_R20102": {
      "title": "Pre-Award Project Manager - Grants Hub",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Pre-Award Project Manager - Grants Hub Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 3 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Enjoy bringing people, ideas, and resources together to turn ambitious research concepts into competitive funding proposals? Looking for a role where you can collaborate with researchers and stakeholders across a wide range of disciplines? If so, the Grants Hub is seeking a Pre-Award Project Manager to support the successful development of interdisciplinary research (IDR) teams and proposals at Iowa State University! This position will coordinate the preparation and submission of large, complex grant proposals involving multiple stakeholders and provide project management support to IDR teams, starting from team formation and continuing through handoff to a post-award project manager. This position will be classified as a Research Administrator II. The Pre-Award Project Manager will work with researchers from all colleges and disciplines, with an emphasis on large, center-type proposals that involve researchers and stakeholders from multiple colleges, institutions, and sectors. This role will also serve as the primary point of contact to coordinate the Grants Hub’s comprehensive team-based proposal development support for selected IDR teams. What You'll Do: Develop proposal checklists and calendars, identify key milestones and deadlines, assign tasks, and track progress towards deliverables. Work with IDR teams to identify and manage project scope, goals, risks, resources, and stakeholders. Develop project communications and reporting plans. Manage proposal-related communications with IDR teams, collaborators, stakeholders, and other sponsored funding support staff and actively participate in and facilitate working group meetings. Manage preparations and logistics for site visits and reverse site visits. Provide back-up and supplemental pre-award administration support, including budget development, document collection and review, and proposal routing and submission. Collaborate with other Grants Hub staff and external consultants to coordinate proposal-strengthening activities such as strategic intelligence analyses and color team reviews. Identify and implement improvements to project management and pre-award research administration processes, including through development of AI agents and automated workflows. The successful candidate will have exceptional organizational and time management skills; strong oral and written communications skills; a proactive and collaborative approach to customer service and relationship building; a high attention to detail; and the ability to adjust to shifting deadlines and priorities. The successful candidate must reside in the state of Iowa on or before their start date. This position offers the flexibility to work on-site in Ames or in a hybrid work arrangement as well. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated experience in managing the development and submission of complex research grant proposals and budgets involving multiple investigators and subcontracts. Experience with Federal regulations and agency policies and guidelines for sponsored research, proposal submission, and budgeting. Demonstrated experience working with interdisciplinary research teams, preferably in a university environment. Experience developing and managing strategic partnerships and collaborating with multiple stakeholders. Experience and/or formal training or certification in project management methodologies, frameworks, and best practices applied to complex research projects, grant development, or strategic initiatives involving interdisciplinary teams and multiple stakeholders. Experience leveraging technology, AI tools, and/or automated workflows to improve project management, grant development, research administration, or other complex administrative processes. About Grants Hub at Iowa State University: The Grants Hub is Iowa State’s central research development unit, located within the Office of the Vice President for Research. We are proactive and future-focused, providing strategic pre-award support and consultation to help researchers successfully compete for funding and build high-impact research teams. Our broad range of services are available to new and experienced investigators from all colleges, departments, and disciplines. To learn more, please visit Grants Hub . Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: October 15, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 28, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20102 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Environmental-Systems-Mechanic-I_R20092": {
      "title": "Environmental Systems Mechanic I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Environmental Systems Mechanic I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Four years of experience in refrigeration, heating or air conditioning work, including apprenticeship; and • Obtains refrigeration certificate of at least type 2 within first six months of employment. • May need to possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. Job Description: Required Minimum Qualifications • Four years of experience in refrigeration, heating or air conditioning work, including apprenticeship; and • Obtains refrigeration certificate of at least type 2 within first six months of employment. • May need to possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. Job Profile Description Under direct supervision, performs skilled work in the area of installation, repair, alteration, replacement and maintenance of components of refrigeration, air conditioning and heating (all fuel types) equipment. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Installs and maintains air-moving, heating, cooling, humidification and filtering equipment and systems such as fans, heat pumps, gas unit heaters, forced air equipment, furnaces, radiant heating, condensers, compressors, pumps, fan coil units, rooftop package air conditioning units, computer room cooling units, etc. • Installs and maintains various styles and types of refrigeration equipment and systems. • Installs and maintains equipment related to heating and cooling, such as air compressors, air dryers and associated non-automated controls. • Tests and evaluates performance of air-moving, heating, cooling, humidification and filtering equipment such as fans, heat pumps, forced air, radiant heating, condensers, compressors, pumps, fan coil units, rooftop package air conditioning units, computer room cooling units, etc. using specialized equipment; repairs or replaces defective valves, thermostats and other parts. • Reads and interprets blueprints, schematics and other drawings, diagrams and specifications. • Prepares records and service reports. • Uses chain falls, hoists and chokers to safely lift large heavy components into position. • Provides guidance to apprentices and/or students as required. • Other duties as assigned by appropriate department or administrative personnel. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities •  Knowledge of the principles of operations, methods, materials and tools utilized in the installation, troubleshooting, maintenance, calibration and repair of air-moving, heating, cooling, humidification and filtering equipment and systems such as fans, heat pumps, gas unit heaters, forced air equipment, furnaces, radiant heating, condensers, compressors, pumps, fan coil units, rooftop package air conditioning units, computer room cooling units, etc. • Ability to properly braze refrigeration tubing and connections. • Knowledge of occupational hazards and safety precautions mandated by the Occupational Safety and Health Administration, National Fire Prevention Association, National Fire Code and the Environmental Protection Agency, etc. • Knowledge, skill and ability to evaluate equipment for either repair or replacement and determine the amount of time and materials necessary to accomplish the task with least downtime of equipment. • Ability to interpret blueprints, diagrams and equipment specifications. • Knowledge of proper bending and lifting techniques. • Skill in the proper use and care of hand and power tools and test equipment. • Ability to work in areas of high heat, dust and noise and in confined spaces or on a ladder. • Ability to work independently during the normal workday and in an on-call status. • Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. • Ability to work in all types of environmental conditions or in areas where there is exposure to excessive noise, dirt, and fumes and at elevated heights from ladders, scaffolds, or hydraulic lifts. • Ability to work independently during normal work hours and after hours.  • Basic Computer Skills Schedule: Monday-Friday 7:00am-4:30pm Preferred Qualifications: Experience installing, maintaining, and repairing commercial HVAC and refrigeration systems.  (Including compressors, condensers, heat pumps, rooftop units, fan coil units)  Experience installing, maintaining, and repairing commercial HVAC and refrigeration systems.  (Including compressors, condensers, heat pumps, rooftop units, fan coil units)  Demonstrated experience working with computerized or specialized HVAC diagnostic and testing equipment  Experience working collaboratively in an on-call environment and responding to emergency equipment failures  Experience troubleshooting HVAC and refrigeration equipment using specialized testing and diagnostic equipment Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5090a Original Posting Date: October 15, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20092 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Facilities-Mechanic-III_R20090": {
      "title": "Facilities Mechanic III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Facilities Mechanic III Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Must possess a basic knowledge of plumbing, electricity, maintenance of steam and mechanical equipment. • Must have four years of work experience in the listed crafts, including apprenticeship or technical training. • At least two years of that experience must be in the same craft. Job Description: Required Minimum Qualifications • Must possess a basic knowledge of plumbing, electricity, maintenance of steam and mechanical equipment. • Must have four years of work experience in the listed crafts, including apprenticeship or technical training. • At least two years of that experience must be in the same craft. Job Profile Description Under general supervision, performs skilled and semi-skilled work in the repairing, servicing, and maintaining of buildings and electrical, mechanical and plumbing equipment.   Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities   • Performs preventive maintenance on motors, pumps, and other equipment, and maintains appropriate records. • Constructive sanitizers, installs oxygen outlets and system according to engineering specifications. • Performs preventive maintenance and emergency repair work. • Reads and interprets blueprints, diagrams, and equipment specifications. • Performs work in related crafts areas as assigned. • Assists in directing the work of others. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of the hazards involved and safety precautions necessary in the electrical, mechanical and plumbing trades. • Knowledge of work practices, methods, and processes utilized in the electrical, mechanical and plumbing trade. • Knowledge of preventive maintenance necessary for equipment and ability to maintain appropriate records. • Knowledge of proper lifting and bending techniques. • Ability to operate safely the tools and equipment used in the electrical, mechanical and plumbing trades. • Ability to interpret blueprints, diagrams and equipment specifications. • Ability to understand and follow verbal and written instructions. • Ability to work in a variety of environments including confined spaces, low light areas, at heights, with exposure to temperature extremes. • Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. Schedule: Monday-Friday 7:00am-4:30pm Preferred Qualifications: Experience performing preventative maintenance and troubleshooting on commercial or institutional mechanical, electrical, and plumbing systems  Demonstrated ability to read and interpret blueprints, schematics, equipment specifications, and technical manuals Experience maintaining records, work orders, or computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS) Experience responding to emergency maintenance repairs and prioritizing multiple service request in a fast-paced environment Experience providing work direction, or guidance to other employees, apprentices, or student workers Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5311a Original Posting Date: October 15, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20090 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
