    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Instruction-Librarian-I_R20070": {
      "title": "Instruction Librarian I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Instruction Librarian I Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree Job Description: The Iowa State University Library invites applications for an Instruction Librarian I to join its Instruction Unit. This role will collaborate with the instruction team to coordinate and teach the undergraduate information literacy course. As part of the Research and Instruction Department, the Instruction Unit also develops and delivers workshops and instructional sessions focused on information literacy, AI literacy, and research skills. The Instruction Librarian will also contribute to the development and delivery of these instructional initiatives.   The successful candidate will have a customer-service focus, be skilled in organization and time management, possess the ability to interact effectively with library staff and the university community, and work independently as well as collaboratively in a rapidly changing, team-based environment.   The Iowa State University Library is committed to supporting librarians through mentoring, training, and professional development opportunities that foster professional growth and success. The Instruction Librarian will be encouraged and supported in pursuing continued learning relevant to their role, as well as sharing their knowledge and expertise with colleagues at Iowa State University and the broader library community.   Example of Duties: Teaching the library’s credit bearing information literacy course for undergraduate students.  Work with the instruction team to centrally coordinate the course and manage student learning accommodations. Actively participate in development of content and learning materials for the information literacy course. Ensure digital accessibility of the course learning materials. Co-manage the course’s learning management system, Canvas. Coordinate library’s LibGuides system and provide support to librarians on using LibGuides. Participate in the development of guides, tutorials, and other learning modules that support AI literacy, information literacy, and research skills. Contribute to the ongoing evaluation of instruction programs, providing recommendations for improvement.   Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching or providing information literacy instruction. Experience delivering reference and research services in an academic or research library. Experience using course management systems, such as Canvas. Experience using instructional technologies and content creation software. Knowledge of accessibility standards and practices for creating digitally accessible learning materials. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, please apply before October 30th, 2026. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: October 15, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20070 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Dean-of-Students-for-Student-Support_R20006": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean of Students for Student Support",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Dean of Students for Student Support Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 7 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Interested in making a meaningful impact on the lives of students by helping them navigate challenges and achieve success throughout their college journey? Looking for a leadership role where you can balance strategic planning, relationship building, crisis response, and student support? If so, the Dean of Students Office (DSO) with Iowa State University is seeking applicants for an Assistant Dean of Students for Student Support! This individual will provide leadership for the Office of Student Assistance, Parent and Family Programs, Off-Campus Student Support Program, and the Sloss House operations. This position will be classified as an Assistant Dean of Students. What You'll Do: Provide leadership and oversight for student assistance, care/case management, parent and family programming, off-campus student support, and other student support services. Manage complex student support cases and coordinate interventions for students experiencing academic, personal, behavioral, or crisis-related challenges. Supervise, mentor, and evaluate professional staff and student employees. Lead student case review and support processes to promote student success and well-being. Coordinate responses to critical student situations and provide guidance on crisis intervention and case management practices. Collaborate with faculty, staff, administrators, and campus partners to address student concerns and connect students with appropriate resources. Develop, implement, and assess programs, services, and initiatives that support student retention, success, and well-being. Establish goals, priorities, and operational plans aligned with departmental and institutional objectives. Manage departmental budgets, resources, and operational activities. Build and maintain strong partnerships with campus and community stakeholders to enhance student support efforts. Oversee physical space of Sloss House. Provide consultation, training, and educational outreach related to student well-being, care strategies, and student support resources. Analyze data and assessment results to identify trends, evaluate effectiveness, and drive continuous improvement. Serve on university committees, task forces, and leadership groups, representing the Dean of Students Office. Interpret and apply policies, procedures, and best practices to support effective student case management, well-being, and success. Contribute to strategic planning efforts and support departmental and institutional priorities. The ideal candidate is a trusted relationship builder with strong leadership skills and a genuine commitment to student well-being. They will be comfortable balancing strategic thinking with hands-on support while fostering partnerships that strengthen the student experience. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Student Affairs, Higher Education Administration, Counseling, Psychology, Social Work, or a related field. Experience working in a higher education environment supporting student success, well-being, retention, or student affairs initiatives; experience supporting non-residential, off-campus, or commuter student populations is a plus. Experience supervising, mentoring, and developing professional staff. Experience providing case management, care coordination, or crisis intervention; preferably in a college or university setting. Experience developing, implementing, and assessing programs, services, or initiatives that support student retention, success, and well-being. About Dean of Students Office at Iowa State University: The Dean of Students Office's primary goal is to empower every Cyclone to thrive at Iowa State University. Whether through our academic enrichment initiatives, programs designed to help all students experience a sense of community and belonging, or support resources we provide to help students navigate challenges that sometimes arise during their college journey, we seek to help students experience success in every aspect of their college experience. We also serve as a resource and partner with other campus departments, recognizing that students benefit from a collaborative network of resources. To learn more, please visit DSO . Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: October 15, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 29, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20006 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Grants-Specialist-I_R20076": {
      "title": "Grants Specialist I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Grants Specialist I Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Job Description: Come join the Research and Graduate Studies team within Iowa State University's College of Veterinary Medicine as a Grant Specialist I . Help advance research that improves animal health, veterinary medicine, and scientific discovery. As a central resource for faculty, researchers, and students, our team supports external funding, research development, and graduate education across the college. In this role, you will serve in a pre-award research administration capacity, partnering with faculty throughout the grant proposal development and submission process. Responsibilities include identifying funding opportunities, developing proposal budgets, coordinating proposal submissions, assisting with sponsor guidelines and requirements, preparing proposal materials, and supporting other pre-award research administration activities. You will collaborate with faculty, researchers, and university partners to help secure external funding that advances the college's research mission. This is an excellent opportunity for an early career professional interested in research administration. We are committed to providing training and development to help the successful candidate build expertise in pre-award grant administration and research support. Working closely with faculty, researchers, students, and university partners, you'll gain experience in funding opportunity identification, proposal development, budget preparation, proposal coordination, and sponsor submission requirements while helping transform innovative ideas into competitive funding proposals. Additional Details Location: Ames, Iowa Schedule: Monday-Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. What You'll Do Coordinate the preparation, internal review and submission of grant proposals. Develop proposal budgets, justifications and supporting documentation. Enter and maintain proposal information in university systems. Coordinate proposal routing, approvals, and submission timelines. Assist faculty with interpreting sponsor guidelines, preparing proposal materials, and meeting submission requirements Support post-submission activities, including sponsor requests and required documentation. Collect, maintain, and verify research-related data and records. Assist with research programs, events, workshops, and student initiatives. Monitor and distribute funding opportunities to faculty and staff. Collaborate with university partners to support research administration activities. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Finance, Accounting, Public Administration, Higher Education Administration, Research Administration, or a related field. Experience developing budgets, financial reports, or financial projections. Experience preparing or submitting grant, contract, or sponsored project proposals. Proficiency in Microsoft Excel skills, including formulas, pivot tables, and data reporting. Experience reviewing and applying policies, procedures, funding requirements, or compliance guidelines. Why Join Us? Join a collaborative and supportive team that helps advance research, innovation, and graduate education within Iowa State University's College of Veterinary Medicine. This entry-level role offers the opportunity to build expertise in research administration while working alongside faculty, researchers, students, and university partners to support impactful research initiatives. Iowa State University offers a comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off, professional development opportunities, and flexible work arrangements where business needs permit. Learn more about our benefits: https://jobs.iastate.edu/benefits . Join a team where your contributions support groundbreaking research while providing opportunities to learn, grow, and make a lasting impact. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: October 14, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 28, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20076 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Student-Services-Specialist-II_R20077": {
      "title": "Student Services Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Student Services Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: Are you passionate about helping students grow as leaders, build community, and make the most of their Iowa State experience? The Memorial Union is seeking a Student Services Specialist II to support student organizations, advise student leaders, and coordinate leadership development programs that enhance campus life. This role offers the opportunity to work directly with highly engaged students as they pursue projects, events, and initiatives they care deeply about. You'll serve as a trusted resource, helping student organizations navigate university processes, develop leadership skills, and successfully bring their ideas to life. No two days are exactly alike. From advising student leaders and organizing leadership retreats to managing communications and supporting campus-wide events, you'll play an important role in creating a vibrant and connected student experience. What You'll Do Coordinate student organization operations, including recognition processes, record management, database administration, office and storage assignments, funding opportunities, annual awards, and related training. Plan and facilitate leadership development opportunities, including retreats, workshops, conferences, and programs such as LEAD Retreat and the Iowa Student Leadership Experience (ISLE). Advise the First-Year Council and other student leaders on topics such as leadership, budgeting, event planning, marketing, and organizational success. Connect students with campus resources and help them navigate university policies, procedures, and organizational requirements. Develop and distribute newsletters, campus-wide communications, website content, and other program materials that support student engagement. Support student organization events and major Memorial Union initiatives, including ClubFest, WelcomeFest, Art Mart, and AfterDark. Supervise graduate assistants and occasional practicum students. Assess program effectiveness, identify opportunities for improvement, and collaborate with colleagues and campus partners to enhance student involvement and leadership development. Why Join Our Team? The Memorial Union is the heart of student life at Iowa State University. In this role, you'll work in a collaborative and student centered environment where your efforts directly support student growth, involvement, and success. You'll partner with motivated student leaders who are passionate about making an impact on campus while enjoying a position that offers meaningful responsibility, variety, autonomy, and the opportunity to see the results of your work firsthand. Preferred Qualifications Experience developing and facilitating leadership development programs, trainings, or workshops. Experience administering a database, CRM, or information management system. Experience coordinating funding, grant, scholarship, or application review processes. Experience planning and executing events, conferences, retreats, or large-scale programs. Experience creating and distributing newsletters, email campaigns, website content, or other organizational communications. Work Schedule and Location Work Location: Primarily on-site in the Memorial Union at Iowa State University. Schedule: Typical hours are Monday through Friday during regular business hours. Occasional Evening & Weekend Work: Required to support student organization meetings, leadership programs, campus events, and special activities. Flexibility: Work hours may vary based on student availability, program schedules, and departmental needs. About the Memorial Union The Memorial Union is a central hub for student life at Iowa State University, providing opportunities for students to connect, participate in campus activities, and develop leadership skills beyond the classroom. Through student organization support, leadership development, and campus programming, the Memorial Union helps students build relationships, pursue their interests, and contribute to the university community. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: October 14, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 28, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20077 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate-in-Electrical-and-Computer-Engineering_R19752": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate in Electrical and Computer Engineering Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Iowa State University invites applications for an immediate Postdoctoral Research Associate position. The successful candidate will participate in cutting-edge research projects focused on optimization, data analytics, and control of power distribution systems. This position offers the opportunity to collaborate closely with utility company partners and national laboratories, utilizing real-world utility data and models to address practical and impactful challenges in modern power systems. The selected candidate will contribute to the development of innovative solutions that enhance the reliability, efficiency, and resilience of electric power distribution networks. Required Minimum Qualifications : PhD in Electrical Engineering Preferred Qualifications:   Demonstrated research experience in power distribution systems, optimization, data analytics, or control through doctoral research, postdoctoral research, industry experience, or funded research projects. Authorship or co-authorship of at least one peer-reviewed journal article or conference paper in a relevant field. Demonstrated analytical and problem-solving skills through completion of independent research projects, dissertation research, or development of technical solutions in a relevant discipline. Evidence of research initiative and creativity, such as first-author publications, leadership of research activities, proposal development, or significant contributions to collaborative research projects. Experience presenting technical or research findings to academic, industry, or professional audiences through conference presentations, seminars, workshops, or invited talks. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering is part of Iowa State University's College of Engineering, one of the nation's leading engineering colleges. The department is recognized for excellence in research, education, and innovation across areas including electric power and energy systems, communications, cybersecurity, microelectronics, and systems and controls. Faculty and researchers collaborate with industry, government agencies, and national laboratories to develop solutions that address pressing technological and societal challenges. Department Unit/Website: Engineering Graduate Studies - College of Engineering Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: November 1, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: August 12, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 17, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19752 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Lecturer-in-Journalism-and-Mass-Communication_R20088": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Journalism and Mass Communication",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Lecturer in Journalism and Mass Communication Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Greenlee School of Journalism and Communication in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University seeks a lecturer to teach JLMC 2010: Reporting and Writing for the Mass Media. The successful candidate will teach two 3-credit sections of the course, required for majors in advertising, digital storytelling, journalism, public relations, and sports media. The course develops students’ skills in reporting, interviewing, research, writing, and Associated Press style.   Required Minimum Qualifications :   Master’s degree in related field. Two years of professional experience in advertising, public relations, journalism, or sports media.   Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated teaching excellence in higher education; Demonstrated ability to mentor students and/or emerging professionals; Additional professional experience beyond the required amount in advertising, journalism, public relations, or sports media.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Department/Program & College Description : The Greenlee School of Journalism and Communication has a dynamic ACEJMC-accredited undergraduate program and a strong master’s program. The school has undergraduate majors in advertising, journalism and mass communication, public relations, and sports media and communication, as well as a new interdisciplinary major in digital storytelling. Additional information about the school is available at www.greenlee.iastate.edu.   Department Unit/Website :  www.greenlee.iastate.edu Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following:\n \n1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae \n2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter \n3) Contact Information for Three References \n\nIf you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485.\n\n Why Choose ISU? \n\nIowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as:\n• Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans\n• Generous leave plans\n• Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa)\n• Life insurance and long-term disability\n• Flexible Spending Accounts\n• Various voluntary benefits and discounts\n• Employee Assistance Program\n• Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 14, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 15, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20088 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Senior-Manager-of-Marketing-and-Analytics_R20071": {
      "title": "Senior Manager of Marketing and Analytics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Senior Manager of Marketing and Analytics Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 7 years of related experience Job Description: The Ivy College of Business is seeking a qualified Senior Manager of Marketing and Analytics to provide strategic leadership for the college’s marketing, communications, and audience engagement efforts. This role leverages data analytics, market intelligence, and digital marketing technologies to inform strategy and drive results.   The Senior Manager will oversee integrated marketing initiatives that strengthen the college’s brand visibility and advance its strategic goals. Additionally, this position will serve as a strategic advisor to college leadership, providing insights into marketing performance, audience trends, and communication effectiveness to support data-informed decision-making. Example of Duties: Develop and implement a comprehensive data-driven marketing and communications strategy that aligns with the college's strategic goals and enhances its visibility and reputation. Lead audience research, marketing intelligence, and data analytics to identify growth opportunities, evaluate campaign effectiveness, and inform resource allocation. Design, execute, and optimize integrated digital marketing campaigns across email, web, social media, and paid advertising channels using data-driven insights and performance metrics. Oversee the development of marketing content, publications, and promotional materials, ensuring alignment with institutional standards and objectives. Partner with other college units and University Marketing to align messaging and maximize the impact of marketing initiatives. Manage marketing technologies, digital marketing platforms, vendor relationships, and advertising partnerships to enhance operational effectiveness. Lead marketing planning, budgeting, and ROI assessment efforts, providing data-driven insights and actionable recommendations to the Dean. Supervise and develop marketing staff, fostering a culture of collaboration, innovation, continuous improvement, and evidence-based decision making. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, or a related field. Master’s degree in marketing, communications, or a related field. Demonstrated leadership and management experience overseeing marketing and communications strategies, digital marketing analytics, and integrated marketing initiatives. Experience in higher education marketing and communications. Experience using customer relationship management (CRM) platforms to support marketing campaigns, audience engagement, data analysis, and strategic decision-making. The Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University, established in 1984, furthers Iowa State University’s land-grant ideals by training students to be knowledgeable and ethical communicators, leaders, collaborators, and problem solvers through impactful research, innovative teaching, and community engagement.   With the largest undergraduate business program in the state of Iowa and nationally ranked graduate programs, the Ivy College of Business is home to over 5000 students with a strong growth trajectory. We pride ourselves on our high ethical standards and our drive to promote an environment where all individuals may succeed academically, professionally, and personally. Each member of our community is committed to the college’s mission to link theory with practice for tomorrow’s business leaders.   The college offers undergraduate, graduate, and Ph.D. programs and is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). Less than five percent of business schools worldwide receive this accreditation. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS812 Original Posting Date: October 13, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 23, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20071 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Senior-Psychologist_R20064": {
      "title": "Senior Psychologist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Senior Psychologist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Doctorate Degree from an American Psychological Association (APA) or Canadian Psychological Association (CPA) accredited program or certified equivalent in counseling or clinical psychology and 1 year of related experience, which may include a doctoral internship. Licensed as a psychologist. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Impact Student Well-Being in a Collaborative and Supportive Environment Are you looking to make a real difference in the lives of university students while working in a dynamic and team-oriented environment? Iowa State University’s Student Counseling Services (SCS) is seeking a skilled Senior Psychologist to provide essential mental health services to students. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to the personal and academic success of students through a variety of counseling, crisis intervention, and educational programs. Why Iowa State University and SCS? Team-Oriented, Collaborative Environment At ISU’s Student Counseling Services, we value teamwork and collaboration. Our staff works closely together to provide high-quality care for students. You will be part of a dedicated team of professionals, collaborating to offer counseling, crisis support, and outreach programming aimed at improving student well-being. Engaging and Varied Work Each day brings new opportunities to support students as they navigate their college experience. From individual and group therapy to managing crises, you’ll engage in meaningful work that helps students overcome challenges and meet their personal and academic goals. As part of a center with a robust training program, you’ll also have the opportunity to provide supervision and mentorship to trainees, contributing to the development of future professionals in the field. Excellent Work-Life Balance and Benefits We understand the importance of maintaining balance in life. Iowa State University is committed to creating a workplace where your professional responsibilities are balanced with your personal needs. The university offers a flexible, supportive environment, including access to a fantastic benefits package which includes wellness programs and generous vacation time, allowing you to recharge and maintain your well-being while helping others. What We Offer: Work/Life Balance: primarily a Monday-Friday, day hours position! Generous Vacation and Sick Leave – 24 vacation days, 18 sick days, and 11 paid holidays. Excellent Health Insurance Options – including dental and vision coverage. Paid Professional Development opportunities. Retirement Plans with Employer Contributions – choose from multiple plans to secure your future. Tuition Reimbursement and Professional Development Support – grow with us! Wellness Programs and Work-Life Resources – including mental health and counseling support. Key Responsibilities: Provide individual and group therapy within a brief treatment model. Conduct intake assessments and make recommendations for appropriate services. Deliver crisis intervention and manage urgent student needs. Provide presentations and outreach programming on mental health topics for students, staff, and faculty. Provide supervision to trainees. Maintain thorough documentation of client interactions and services. Take part in crisis coverage as part of a rotating staff schedule. Why You’ll Love Living in Ames Ames, Iowa, offers an outstanding quality of life. Known for its welcoming community, Ames is home to a vibrant blend of cultural, athletic, and social events, thanks in part to Iowa State University. Whether you're attending concerts, art exhibitions, or theater performances, there's always something happening. The city also hosts a wide variety of athletic events, from Cyclone football and basketball games to other university sports that bring the community together. Plus, Ames frequently offers festivals, farmers’ markets, and university-sponsored lectures and events, ensuring there’s something for everyone. In addition to the exciting local atmosphere, Ames provides an affordable cost of living and excellent schools, making it a great place to live and thrive. Plus, with Des Moines just 30 minutes away, you’ll have easy access to everything a larger city has to offer without sacrificing the charm and convenience of a smaller town. Special Requirements: Applicants must be licensed as a psychologist before their start date. Applicants must also obtain an Iowa psychologist license within six months of the start date. For more information about our services, visit: Iowa State University Student Counseling Services . This position serves at the pleasure of university administration and is exempt from certain P&S policies. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before November 4th, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. This position serves at the pleasure of university administration and is exempt from certain P&S policies. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: October 13, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20064 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoc-Research-Associate---Veterinary-Field-Services_R19565": {
      "title": "Postdoc Research Associate – Veterinary Field Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoc Research Associate – Veterinary Field Services Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The position emphasizes training in food animal medicine, with a substantial focus on bovine health and production systems, including both beef and dairy cattle. The selected candidate will gain production medicine–based clinical experience and have opportunities to participate in applied research activities. The primary work will be with the Veterinary Field Services unit, with opportunities to collaborate with and gain additional clinical and diagnostic experience through the ISU Food Animal and Camelid Hospital and the ISU Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory. This position is designed to support candidates pursuing board certification as a Beef Cattle Diplomate or Food Animal Diplomate through the American Board of Veterinary Practitioners (ABVP) and to provide advanced clinical, teaching, and research experience for careers in academia, food animal practice, and veterinary clinical scholarship. Responsibilities include active participation in ambulatory food animal care through ISU Veterinary Field Services; involvement in the clinical instruction of veterinary students within the professional DVM program; participation in applied research in food animal medicine; and development of observational research studies, such as case reports and case series, to support scholarly productivity and ABVP board certification. Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent veterinary degree by the start date of employment. Possession of, or eligibility to obtain by the start date of employment, a State of Iowa veterinary license and Category II accreditation through the USDA National Veterinary Accreditation Program (NVAP). Possession of, or eligibility to obtain by the start date of employment, U.S. Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) registration and State of Iowa controlled substance registration. Valid U.S. driver's license and ability to meet University requirements for authorization to operate University vehicles by the start date of employment. Preferred Qualifications: One year of clinical experience in a food animal veterinary practice or comparable clinical food animal setting. Demonstrated experience working effectively with herd managers, animal care providers, and/or students at various levels of training. Department/Program & College Description: The Iowa State University College of Veterinary Medicine Food Animal and Camelid Field Services provides on-farm services to livestock producers in the general Ames area. Equipped with four fully stocked mobile veterinary trucks and eight full-time clinicians, Veterinary Field Services provides individual animal and herd health veterinary care for beef, dairy, swine, sheep, goats, and camelids (alpacas and llamas). The Field Services unit serves to educate veterinary students on farm animal medicine while providing high-quality veterinary services to local producers. Our services provide students with additional hands-on training in best practices for management of a wide variety of clinical cases to help prepare them for their future veterinary careers. Department Unit/Website: Veterinary Field Services - Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. To be guaranteed consideration, applications must be received by October 22, 2026. This is a one-year term position with the possibility of renewal. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027 . Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: July 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: July 17, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19565 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Custodian-I_R20083": {
      "title": "Custodian I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Custodian I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. Job Description: The Facilities Planning & Management Department is seeking applicants for full-time Custodian I positions. Under direct supervision, performs custodial work required for the general maintenance of buildings.  ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT:    Facilities Planning & Management (FP&M) is an organization that is dedicated to the maintenance and enhancement of Iowa State University, one of the nation’s leading educational and agricultural institutes. But more importantly, FP&M is dedicated to their employees and enhancing the lives of each team member through opportunities both professionally and personally. FP&M is one of the largest departments on campus and currently employs over 450 full-time employees and students combined.  Preferred Qualifications: At least 1 year of experience in custodial work or a related field  Experience operating commercial cleaning equipment such as floor scrubbers, vacuums, or buffers  Experience using a work order or work management systems Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Performs cleaning in all areas of a building. • Performs cleaning of all floor areas such as vacuuming, shampooing, sweeping, mopping, stripping, scrubbing, waxing, and buffing. • Cleans and polishes all bathroom fixtures. • Cleans and washes all glass surfaces, ceilings and walls. • The use of a ladder up to 12 feet in height may be required. • Replaces light bulbs and cleans light fixtures, using a ladder as required. • Makes beds and handles both clean and soiled linens. • Refills holder of disposable items, such as soap, bathroom tissue, paper towels, etc. Cleans and disinfects beds, bedside tables, overbed tables, etc., and other equipment and areas. • Reports breakage and needed repairs. • Moves furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment; removes draperies and rugs periodically for cleaning; delivers supplies to various areas. • Collects trash from receptacles throughout the building and empties it into various areas. • Performs duties in the immediate exterior of building such as sweeping sidewalks, snow and ice removal at entrances, cleaning ash pits, cleaning debris from grounds and window wells, and cleaning exterior windows. • Locks and unlocks doors as required. • Assists in unloading trucks, unpacking, assembling, and moving equipment and furniture. • Picks up and returns equipment for repair by maintenance. • Delivers housekeeping supplies to designated areas. • Operates high pressure, water-cleaning apparatus to clean and disinfect rug runners, hospital equipment and showers. • Maintains inventory of linen and record of lined laundering; maintains inventory of custodial supplies, and keeps and prepares other records and reports as directed. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of standard cleaning techniques and characteristics of surfaces to be cleaned, and equipment and supplies required. • Ability to move furniture and objects in preparation for cleaning; to load and unload trash receptacles; to operate safely and properly care for power machinery; to use arm muscles in hand cleaning, mopping, and scrubbing for protracted periods of time; to work on ladders. • Knowledge of proper bending and lifting techniques and ability to lift and carry 50 pounds. • Ability to work in a variety of environments including crowded public areas and high and low temperature areas. • Knowledge of the safe use if chemical cleaning agents and possible hazards relating to environmental sanitation. • Ability to communicate effectively with others. • Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 0003a Original Posting Date: October 13, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 23, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20083 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor--Land-Use---Resilience-Planning_R20147": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor: Land-Use & Resilience Planning",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor: Land-Use & Resilience Planning Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Iowa State University Extension and Outreach Community and Economic Development (CED)in partnership with the Department of Urban Planning and Development (UPD) in the College of Design, invites applications for a 12-month tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Land-Use & Resilience Planning.   We seek a scholar and educator whose research and teaching focus on how communities can use land-use planning to address changing conditions in Iowa, manage natural resources, and build long-term community resilience. The successful candidate will contribute to UPD's teaching and research mission while developing an applied extension and outreach program through CED that responds to the needs of Iowa communities.   With a joint appointment in UPD and CED, the candidate will work with local governments, regional organizations, state agencies, community organizations, and other partners. The successful candidate will translate research and planning knowledge into practical tools, programs, technical assistance, and educational resources. A start-up package will be available to initiate research and statewide engagement.   About ISU Extension and Outreach, Community and Economic Development Iowa State University Extension and Outreach Community and Economic Development (CED) works with communities across Iowa to strengthen local economies, leadership, and quality of life. CED connects university expertise with community needs through applied research, education, technical assistance, and partnerships in areas such as community planning, economic development, housing, and local governance. Website: https://www.extension.iastate.edu/communities/programs-and-services   Department of Urban Planning and Development The Department of Urban Planning and Development (UPD) at Iowa State University prepares students to address the complex challenges facing cities, towns, and regions. Through teaching, research, and community engagement, UPD faculty focus on areas such as land-use planning, housing, transportation, community and economic development, environmental resilience, local governance and planning technologies, with a strong emphasis on applying planning knowledge to real-world community needs. Please visit the departmental website for more information: https://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/upd/ .   Areas of Interest We welcome candidates whose scholarship and practice address one or more of the following areas: land-use planning; land-use law and regulation; planning for rural, regional and community resilience; natural-resource and watershed planning; or economic development.   Candidates whose work connects multiple areas and demonstrates the application of planning knowledge to community challenges are particularly encouraged to apply. The position provides an opportunity to integrate research, teaching, and community engagement around some of the most consequential challenges facing urban and rural communities in Iowa.     Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will contribute to Iowa State University’s land grant mission and the teaching, research, extension, and service imperatives of the Department of Urban Planning and Development, the College of Design, and ISU Extension and Outreach.     The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in areas such as land-use planning, planning law, community resilience, and natural resources and watershed planning, as well as contribute to innovative planning courses and studios consistent with departmental needs and aligned with the work program of ISU Extension and Outreach.   A major component of this position will be developing an applied research and extension program focused on land-use planning and resilience in Iowa communities. The future faculty member will be expected to pursue external funding; disseminate scholarship through appropriate academic, extension, and professional venues; translate research to community needs and for public audiences; develop interdisciplinary collaborations within and beyond Iowa State University; establish a leadership role in statewide land use matters; and engage communities throughout Iowa.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in urban and regional planning, environmental planning, geography, law, policy, public administration, or a closely related field by the start date.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of research or scholarly potential related to land-use planning and resilience. Evidence of the ability to contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in planning. Experience with community-engaged research or applied planning practice. Ability to translate research into practical tools, programs, or decision-support resources for communities and practitioners. Experience working with local governments, residents, regional organizations, extension systems, public agencies, or community-based organizations. Evidence of or potential for developing an externally funded research program. Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Candidates should submit: 1. Letter of application describing their interest in the position and alignment with its teaching, research and extension responsibilities. 2. Curriculum vitae. 3. Community engagement philosophy statement. 4. Teaching statement describing teaching philosophy and experience. 5. Contact information for three professional references. Guaranteed consideration date is December 15, 2026 and application reviews will continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027 . Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Carlton Basmajian , Search Committee Chair, at carlton@iastate.edu . Questions about the application process may be directed to employment@iastate.edu or 515-294-4800. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20147 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-or-Tenure-Track---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-Small-Animal-Emergency-and-Critical-Care-Medicine_R20140": {
      "title": "Clinical or Tenure Track – Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Small Animal Emergency and Critical Care Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical or Tenure Track – Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Small Animal Emergency and Critical Care Medicine Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University (ISU), located in Ames, Iowa, is seeking qualified applicants for a full-time, clinical or tenure track faculty appointment in the area of Small Animal Emergency and Critical Care Medicine in the Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS) at the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC). The LVMC is a state-of-the-art teaching hospital providing specialized care for companion and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. The candidate will join a department with over 50 diverse faculty and staff members, allied in teaching, research, and clinical efforts relevant to companion animals, equids, and other large animals . The successful candidate will provide clinical service and teaching at the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC). The primary focus for all aspects of the position will be on veterinary emergency and critical care for patients in the Hixson-Lied Small Animal Hospital. Clinical duties may include weekend and after-hours obligations which are divided among all ECC faculty. Supervision and instruction of interns and residents, instruction of clinical-year students, and primary case supervision is expected, in addition to participation in and contribution to weekly resident boards review and journal clubs. The successful candidate will also have a collegial, collaborative attitude and willingness to participate in all levels of technician, student, and house officer education. Remaining effort may include participation in research, scholarship, and traditional didactic and laboratory teaching. Appointment rank will be determined based on the qualifications, documented experience, and interests of the selected candidate. The successful candidate will join a program currently supported by four small animal ACVECC diplomates, six residents, one ECC specialty intern, nine rotating interns, and three large animal ACVECC diplomates as well as registered veterinary technicians; including two VTS-ECC .  The emergency and critical care department is a young yet established service that is continuing to experience steady growth. Centered in the State of Iowa, just 30 minutes from the capital, Des Moines, the LVMC serves a large geographic region (Iowa and surrounding states), providing a diverse and challenging caseload that allows the ECC service to practice cutting edge medicine. Services and technology supporting the ECC service include but are not limited to digital radiography, point of care ultrasound, advanced imaging (1.5T MRI, 32-Slice CT), interventional radiology, mechanical ventilation (Servo-u, and Servo-i), high velocity nasal insufflation (three Vapotherm units), therapeutic plasma exchange (Amicus device), multi-parameter monitoring systems, an in-house blood bank, VCM, and three pharmacists with compounding capability. Continuous renal replacement therapy (Prismaflex) is also available with the goal of onboarding hemoperfusion capabilities in the future. The successful candidate will share oversight of the ICU, Critical Care Service and the Emergency Service with the other ECC faculty members. The 43-cage ICU is currently managed in an open style with all services providing primary care, utilizing a collaborative approach to maximize case management. The 24/7 Emergency Service sees approximately 5,000 cases/year, including first opinion cases as well as referrals. The LVMC is AAHA accredited, a VetCOT Level 2 trauma center and a Level I VECCS certified facility.   Ames, Iowa is often found at the top of lists for best college towns and most livable cities in the US. A low cost of living and friendly midwestern hospitality help maintain a small-town feel, with easy access to college sports, the arts, and countless parks and outdoor activities.   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent degree. Successful completion of an American College of Veterinary Emergency and Critical Care (ACVECC) or European College of Veterinary Emergency Care (ECVECC) residency. Individuals in their final year of residency training are also encouraged to apply and will be considered. Eligible for a State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before first day of employment. Eligible to register under the state Controlled Substances Act with the Iowa Board of Pharmacy upon employment. In addition, positions at the following ranks will require: CLINICAL ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR: Must have experience in academia and a record of contributions of an appropriate magnitude and quality in the clinical specialty. There should be evidence of promise for further academic development and contributions to their field.  CLINICAL PROFESSOR : Must have substantial academic experience and contributions to their professional field. TENURE track : Must hold credentials in a specialty field (i.e. DACVECC)   Preferred Qualifications: ACVECC/ECVECC diplomate Demonstrated experience in didactic and clinical teaching of veterinary students. Experience in modern, veterinary emergency and critical care practices and standards of care. Demonstrated experience and willingness to train interns Demonstrated experience and willingness to train residents for successful completion of the ACVECC certifying exam. A record of, or notable potential of, scholarship production through manuscript publication/preparation, preparation/success in granting activity, an advanced academic degree (MS or PhD), or national scholarly, clinical, or educational presentations.   Department/Program & College Description: The LVMC is a state-of-the-art facility designed to provide specialized care and comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion, exotic, and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. Our clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work collaboratively to provide 24-hour, high-quality care to animal patients.   Department Unit/Website: www.vetmed.iastate.edu/vcs ; https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc Proposed Start Date: June 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three (3) external to Iowa State References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before November 23, 2026. This position is open until filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20140 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Deputy-Athletics-Director---Chief-Revenue-Officer--CRO-_R20143": {
      "title": "Deputy Athletics Director - Chief Revenue Officer (CRO)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Deputy Athletics Director - Chief Revenue Officer (CRO) Appointment Type: Contract Job Description: Iowa State Athletics seeks an innovative and results-driven executive to serve as Deputy Athletics Director and Chief Revenue Officer to help position the department for continued success in an evolving collegiate athletics environment. Reporting directly to the Director of Athletics, this position serves as a member of the executive staff and provides strategic leadership for Iowa State Athletics’ revenue generation and external-facing operations. The position oversees strategic communications, marketing and fan experience, communications, digital media, licensing, Cyclone Sports Properties, creative services, broadcast/television, and will serve as a sport administrator. Working closely with the Director of Athletics and executive staff, the CRO develops integrated strategies to grow commercial revenue, maximize CYTown monetization, strengthen the Iowa State brand, expand fan engagement, and enhance the experience of student-athletes, fans, alumni, and corporate partners. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Executive Leadership: Serves on the executive staff and advises the Director of Athletics on revenue strategy, brand positioning, external communications, fan engagement, and commercial partnerships. Establishes goals, budgets, performance measures, and cross-functional priorities for assigned units; recruits, develops, and evaluates staff. Collaborates with the ISU Foundation, University Marketing, and other campus partners to align messaging, relationships, and institutional priorities. Areas of Direct Responsibility: Revenue Generation: Leads integrated commercial revenue strategy, including sponsorship, multimedia rights, licensing, digital platforms, and new revenue opportunities, including CYTown-related commercial opportunities; coordinates with leaders responsible for ticketing, premium seating, fundraising, and other revenue streams. Strategic Communications: Directs long-range external communications strategy, institutional messaging, reputation management, and coordinated communications on major department initiatives. Marketing & Fan Experience: Oversees marketing campaigns, attendance and engagement initiatives, promotions, game presentation, and the overall fan experience across athletics venues. Communications: Provides leadership for athletics communications, media relations, public information, storytelling, and crisis communications in coordination with university partners. Digital Media: Oversees digital content strategy, athletics websites, social media channels, audience development, and digital engagement and monetization opportunities. Licensing: Leads athletics licensing strategy, brand usage, merchandise-related partnerships, and licensing revenue in coordination with university stakeholders and licensees. CYTown Monetization: Leads athletics-related commercial strategy and revenue opportunities associated with CYTown, including sponsorships, naming rights, advertising, event programming, experiential activations, and other partnership opportunities; collaborates with university leadership, project stakeholders, and Cyclone Sports Properties to coordinate inventory, agreements, activation, and long-term revenue performance. Cyclone Sports Properties: Provides executive oversight of the multimedia rights relationship, including sponsorship sales strategy, inventory, activation, partner servicing, contractual performance, and revenue goals. Creative Services: Oversees creative direction, graphic design, video production, photography, and consistent visual identity across departmental platforms and campaigns. Broadcast/TV: Provides strategic oversight of athletics broadcasting, television production, live event coverage, and related distribution and content partnerships. Sport Administration: Serves as sport administrator for assigned programs, supporting head coaches, student-athlete experience, competitive planning, budget oversight, and alignment with departmental priorities. Other Duties: Performs other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. Progressive leadership experience in intercollegiate athletics, sports business, or a related field, including oversight of revenue or external operations. Demonstrated success in revenue generation, strategic leadership, marketing, communications, media, or commercial partnerships.   Preferred Qualifications: Executive-level leadership experience in intercollegiate athletics. Experience overseeing multimedia rights, brand and communications, digital content, broadcast operations, or multiple external units. Master's degree in business, sport management, communications, marketing, or a related field.   About ISU Athletics: As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, Iowa State University Athletics sponsors 18 NCAA Division I varsity sports and is committed to providing a transformational student-athlete experience centered on competitive excellence, academic achievement, leadership development, health and well-being, and personal growth. Iowa State student-athletes have produced 10-consecutive years of record-setting Graduation Success Rate scores in the classroom, while athletically, the Cyclones have captured numerous national team championships, national individual titles, and conference team championships in its rich history.  ISU Athletics employs over 250 talented and dedicated full-time staff members, more than 500 hourly and student employees, and multiple auxiliary partners who collaboratively work within a culture to support and enhance the experiences of Cyclone student-athletes and our amazing fan base, while advancing the mission and strategic priorities of Iowa State University. www.cyclones.com   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an on-going basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume Cover letter Contact Information for references   Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program   If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: November 16, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Contract Original Posting Date: October 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 29, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20143 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoc-Research-Associate---Bee-Ecology-and-Conservation-in-Farmland_R20145": {
      "title": "Postdoc Research Associate - Bee Ecology and Conservation in Farmland",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoc Research Associate - Bee Ecology and Conservation in Farmland Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology at Iowa State University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Scholar to join a USDA-NIFA-funded research project investigating how reconstructed native habitat within agricultural landscapes affects managed and wild bees. This is a full-time Postdoctoral Scholar position located at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa. The initial appointment is for one year, with the possibility of renewal. Funding may be available for up to three years, contingent upon satisfactory performance and continued project funding. The position includes Iowa State University benefits. The anticipated start date is between January 2027 and May 2027. The successful candidate will work with Professors Amy Toth (direct supervisor), Lisa Schulte Moore , and Matthew O'Neal , along with an interdisciplinary team at Iowa State University on the project, \"Evaluating Benefits of Reconstructed Habitat in Farmland Across Bee Species and Landscapes.\" The overarching goal of the project is to determine when and where prairie strips and other reconstructed habitats provide net benefits to bee communities in intensively farmed landscapes. Research activities integrate field ecology, pollinator health, landscape ecology, pesticide exposure, floral resource assessment, and the management of honey bee and bumble bee colonies. This multi-year project involves extensive fieldwork at Iowa farms utilizing prairie strips within corn-soybean production systems. The Postdoctoral Scholar will be expected to: Travel to field sites and collect ecological and bee health data on wild bees, managed bumble bees, and honey bees. Assist with the management and monitoring of honey bee and bumble bee colonies used in the study. Analyze data; prepare manuscripts for peer-reviewed publication; and present research findings at scientific conferences. Collaborate with project investigators, research staff, graduate and undergraduate students, farmer cooperators, and other project partners. Assist with plant surveys, floral resource measurements, including the use of drone imagery, and pollen sampling and analysis. Contribute to interdisciplinary research efforts focused on pollinator conservation in agricultural landscapes. This position provides substantial opportunities for intellectual leadership. The successful candidate will be encouraged to contribute to research planning, mentor students and junior researchers, and develop professional skills relevant to future careers in ecology, entomology, conservation science, and related disciplines. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in biology, entomology, ecology, or a closely related field by the appointment start date.   Prior research experience relevant to the goals and activities of this project. Preferred Qualifications: Experience conducting ecological or entomological field research, especially related to Hymenoptera.   Experience with plant and/or bee identification.   Experience with beekeeping or honey bee research.   Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology (EEOB) at Iowa State University is dedicated to advancing understanding of the natural world through research, teaching, and outreach. EEOB explores the interactions among organisms and their environments, the diversity of life, evolutionary processes, and the structure and function of living organisms. Faculty, staff, and students conduct innovative research addressing critical challenges in ecology, conservation, biodiversity, evolutionary biology, and environmental sustainability while preparing the next generation of scientists and leaders. Department Unit/Website: Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology (EEOB) Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: January 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 15, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20145 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Digital-Scholarship-Librarian-II_R20004": {
      "title": "Digital Scholarship Librarian II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Digital Scholarship Librarian II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Iowa State University Library is seeking applications for a Digital Scholarship Librarian II. Housed in the Digital Scholarship and Initiatives department, this position provides leadership and expertise in digital scholarship, supporting the creation, discovery, access, and sustainable stewardship of research outputs in an evolving technological landscape.   The role applies expertise in web and open-source technologies, data, and emerging technologies such as AI to develop digital scholarship projects and strengthen digital research methods in support of student learning and faculty research.   The successful candidate will demonstrate strong collaboration and communication skills, a commitment to user-centered approaches to technology, and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team in a rapidly evolving digital environment. Example of Duties: Develop and support digital scholarship projects involving static web technology, web-based storytelling, digital collections, open access research, and open educational resources. Enhance the Digital Scholarship and Initiatives department's digital infrastructure to improve the discoverability, accessibility, and sustainability of its digital projects and platforms. Support and expand open access initiatives by enhancing the discoverability and reach of research outputs and archival material in the institutional repository and digital collections. Provide instruction and outreach in areas such as AI literacy, web technologies, and computational and data-informed research methods. Contribute to external partnerships and initiatives that strengthen the library's role in research and teaching. The library is committed to supporting all librarians through mentoring, training, and professional development opportunities to foster success and growth in their work. The Digital Scholarship Librarian will be supported in the pursuit of continued learning relevant to their position and encouraged to share their skills with their colleagues at ISU and beyond. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with digital scholarship tools and technologies, including web development technologies and platforms, data-focused approaches, digital collections, or institutional repositories. Ability to teach and support research using digital methods, AI and digital literacy concepts, and emerging technologies. Demonstrated experience using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Git/GitHub, or related web development technologies. Experience supporting the discoverability and access of digital projects through metadata and structured data, APIs, or user-centered design. Strong collaboration, communication, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work effectively with a wide range of collaborators, learn new technologies, and address technical challenges creatively. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, please apply before November 9th, 2026. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20004 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Director-Student-Recruitment_R20121": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Student Recruitment",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director Student Recruitment Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Lead Strategic Student Recruitment at Iowa State University The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) at Iowa State University is seeking an Assistant Director for Student Recruitment to lead undergraduate recruitment strategy and advance enrollment growth. Reporting directly to the Associate Dean for Academic Innovation, this highly visible role will use data, team leadership, and strategic partnerships to strengthen enrollment outcomes across CALS academic programs.   Why This Role Matters CALS academic departments bring a range of strengths, priorities, and opportunities for student recruitment. You'll have the opportunity to shape college-wide recruitment strategy, lead an energetic, collaborative team, and work with academic departments and campus leaders to develop approaches that connect more students with CALS programs.   Success in this role depends on building relationships, sharing insights, and turning ideas into action to advance shared recruitment goals.   What You'll Do Develop and implement undergraduate recruitment strategies aligned with university and college enrollment priorities. Analyze recruitment trends, conversion rates, and enrollment outcomes to identify opportunities, set goals, and improve student yield across academic programs. Lead, coach, and develop the CALS recruitment team, fostering collaboration, accountability, and continuous improvement. Oversee recruitment planning, budgeting, staffing, and performance management to align resources with college priorities. Build partnerships with department leaders, faculty, staff, Admissions, Marketing, Extension, and external organizations to coordinate recruitment efforts and expand outreach. Present recruitment data, strategies, and recommendations to college leadership to inform decisions and resource allocation. Lead recruitment events, campus visits, admitted-student experiences, and outreach initiatives that showcase CALS programs to prospective students. Guide scholarship strategy by evaluating fund utilization and outcomes and advising leadership on investment priorities that support recruitment, enrollment, and student success. Collaborate with campus partners to support prospective students through recruitment and transition to Iowa State and contribute to student retention and success.   The Leader We Are Looking For Strategic thinking and analytical skills to interpret enrollment trends and translate insights into effective recruitment strategies. Leadership and team development skills to guide staff, establish priorities, and foster accountability and collaboration. Communication and relationship-building skills to engage stakeholders, influence decisions, and build productive partnerships. Planning and resource management skills to align recruitment activities and resources with college priorities. Adaptability and initiative to address departmental needs, respond to enrollment challenges, and identify opportunities for improvement. Preferred Qualifications : Experience leading, supervising, or developing teams, including setting priorities, guiding performance, and supporting team effectiveness. Experience developing or implementing strategies related to student recruitment, enrollment, admissions, or student engagement. Experience using data and performance metrics to inform strategic decisions and improve outcomes. Experience building partnerships with academic departments, faculty, staff, or external stakeholders. Experience presenting data, recommendations, or strategic plans to support planning, resource allocation, or organizational priorities. About Us The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at Iowa State University offers nationally recognized academic programs, impactful research, and extensive Extension outreach. CALS prepares students to address challenges in agriculture, food systems, natural resources, health, and community development. You'll join a collaborative college community where strong partnerships help students discover pathways to meaningful careers. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS809 Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 8, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20121 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Micro-Credential-Program-Specialist-II_R20079": {
      "title": "Micro-Credential Program Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Micro-Credential Program Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning is currently accepting applications for a Micro-Credential Program Specialist II. This position plays a critical role in advancing Iowa State University's expanding micro-credential initiative by supporting the development, implementation, administration, and continuous improvement of non-credit and credit-bearing micro-credentials and digital badges. This position serves as a central resource for faculty, staff, and program partners, coordinating project workflows, managing digital credential operations through the Accredible platform, supporting communications and outreach efforts, and maintaining program data and reporting processes. The successful candidate will collaborate with stakeholders across the university to facilitate micro-credential development and approval processes, administer digital credentials, create and maintain program resources and training materials, support marketing and promotional initiatives, and analyze program metrics to inform decision-making and program enhancement. This position requires strong organizational, communication, project coordination, and technology management skills, along with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a collaborative environment. Some key responsibilities include: Coordinate micro-credential proposals, development projects, approvals, revisions, and implementation activities. Administer and maintain the university's digital credentialing platform, including digital badge and micro-credential issuance. Partner with faculty, staff, and university stakeholders to support program development and operations. Create and maintain program communications, training resources, web content, and outreach materials. Conduct workforce and industry research to inform micro-credential development and alignment with in-demand skills. Track, analyze, and report program performance data, learner engagement, and credential outcomes. Identify opportunities to improve processes, workflows, and operational efficiencies. Represent the micro-credential program through presentations, workshops, meetings, and various outreach activities. The ideal candidate is a detail-oriented and highly organized professional who enjoys managing projects, supporting technology-enabled initiatives, working collaboratively with various stakeholders, and leveraging data to drive continuous improvement. They are comfortable balancing multiple priorities while providing exceptional service and support in a dynamic higher education environment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with project management and workflow tools to coordinate processes Experience with developing promotional materials or other program communications using Adobe Creative Suite Understanding of workforce development, skills-based hiring, labor market research and trends Familiarity with Micro-credentialing and digital badging Previous experience working in a higher education setting For more information about Micro-Credentials and what we do, please visit: Micro-Credentials – CELT This is 2-year fixed term position. Potential renewal contingent on future funding. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by November 8, 2026. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: January 3, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20079 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
