    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Open-Term-Faculty-Position-in-Civil-Construction-and-Environmental-Engineering_R20126": {
      "title": "Open Term Faculty Position in Civil Construction and Environmental Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Open Term Faculty Position in Civil Construction and Environmental Engineering Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Civil, Construction and Environmental Engineering (CCEE), in the College of Engineering at Iowa State University ( www.ccee.iastate.edu ) invites applications for term faculty position(s) involving in-person instruction in construction engineering, geotechnical engineering, and/or structural engineering. Candidates must have the qualifications and ability to teach courses in at least two of these three areas. Appointments may be made at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor or Professor of Practice, based on relevant industry and teaching experience, demonstrated accomplishments, and applicability toward department standards. Responsibilities include preparing and delivering lectures; developing course materials, homework, laboratory assignments, quizzes, examinations, and projects; evaluating student work and assigning grades; maintaining office hours; and meeting with students to support their learning. Successful candidates will collaborate with other faculty as needed to coordinate instruction and support course delivery. Grading support may be available depending on class size and availability of resources. Additional responsibilities include departmental and university service, such as serving on committees, attending meetings, and advising student organizations or competition teams. This position is described as a full-time equivalent (1.0 FTE), nine-month appointment. Appointment rank will depend on applicant qualifications. The initial term is expected to be three years, with the possibility of renewal. Term Faculty members are not tenure-eligible, but faculty members may be considered for advancement in rank in accordance with applicable policies. Candidates should demonstrate a strong record of achievement in teaching, professional engineering practice, or both in construction engineering, civil engineering, or a closely related discipline. Successful candidates will have excellent communication skills and share Iowa State University’s commitment to excellence and its Principles of Community.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Candidates for this position must hold a Bachelor’s degree in civil, construction, or architectural engineering or a related degree and have at least 5 years of relevant experience.  Candidates must demonstrate relevant industry or educational experience qualifying them to teach in a minimum of two of the three identified areas. Candidates at Associate or Full Teaching Professor rank are required to meet department standards for appointment to the rank.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of an impactful career in related professional practice outside of traditional academic roles. Previous teaching experience. Strong communication skills. Professional engineering licensure in the United States, or the ability to become licensed. Ability to teach in all three areas of interest (construction engineering, geotechnical engineering, and structural engineering)   Department/Program & College Description: The CCEE Department offers B.S. degree programs in civil engineering, civil engineering with environmental emphasis, construction engineering, and environmental engineering, plus M.S., MEng, and Ph.D. graduate degree programs in civil engineering and maintains externally funded research of more than $21 million annually. CCEE is committed to faculty, staff and students who can enrich University objectives in the areas of research, teaching, and service.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.ccee.iastate.edu/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will begin to be reviewed on November 22, 2026, with full consideration given to applications received by that date. The posting will remain open until the position is filled. All interested, qualified people must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu . The following documents are required to be submitted as four separate PDF files (one for each required item numbered below):  1) Letter of application/cover letter that briefly discusses how you, the candidate, meet each of the required and preferred qualifications 2) Resume or Curriculum Vitae 3) Two-page statement explaining your qualifications to teach courses in construction, geotechnical, or structures and how you would bring your experience into the courses 4) Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information Direct questions to cceesearch@iastate.edu . Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20126 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Digital-Accessibility-Analyst-II_R20108": {
      "title": "Digital Accessibility Analyst II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Digital Accessibility Analyst II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 3 years of related experience Job Description: Information Technology Services (ITS) is currently accepting applications for a Digital Accessibility Analyst II (Systems Analyst II) position. ITS Digital Accessibility leads efforts to make course content, websites, apps, and other university digital media accessible. As part of this work, ITS Digital Accessibility guides cross-functional collaboration, engages stakeholders, and supports the adoption of institution-wide accessibility practices. You will lead the ISU Digital Accessibility Community of Practice comprising technical personnel from across campus who are embedding digital accessibility into our work as a university. You will engage key stakeholders in conversations on why digital accessibility is critical and how it is achieved on campus. You’ll share accessibility guidance suitable for institution-wide use with assistance from subject matter experts and cross-functional strategic partners. Together with the rest of the ITS Digital Accessibility team, you’ll support the use of accessibility tools, testing, compliance efforts, and vendor partnership to improve accessibility across university digital services. To be successful in this role, you should have strong oral communication, business writing, and presentation skills. You’ll be working with many different stakeholder groups, so your ability to guide and influence them is another important skill. Every university environment presents unique accessibility needs, and success in this role depends on the ability to listen carefully, build relationships with campus partners, and develop tailored solutions. Some key responsibilities include: Build and sustain partnerships with campus units to advance digital accessibility initiatives. Facilitate collaboration among technical professionals with accessibility responsibilities to share knowledge, resources, and best practices. Provide regular updates to community members on all things digital accessibility at Iowa State using online collaboration tools. Convert engagement into support for digital accessibility by sustaining partnerships with campus leaders and ensuring their voices are heard. Accept and prioritize requests for participation at meetings where an improved understanding of digital accessibility can help key groups better contribute to the university’s mission (i.e. workshops, conferences, retreats, executive meetings etc.). Support senior university leaders addressing accessibility issues by providing information, answers, and talking points about efforts in this space at Iowa State. Work with digital accessibility subject matter experts and learning and development professionals to create training materials for technical and non-technical audiences.  Collaborate with communications professionals to craft campus-wide communication, such as the digital accessibility newsletter and major project updates. Update and maintain how-to articles addressing technical accessibility challenges within the university’s library of Knowledge Base Articles. Assist IT professionals effectively use cloud-based content quality tools such as Siteimprove and Anthology Ally to detect accessibility barriers. Provide technical expertise on accessibility standards, WCAG requirements, and enterprise accessibility solutions. Preferred Qualifications: Experience communicating technical concepts in-person, virtually, and in writing to audiences of varying technical ability at different organizational levels. Knowledge of the ADA Title II Web and Mobile Apps Accessibility Rule, the WCAG 2.1 AA standard, and common tools and techniques used to meet these requirements. Be Certified Professional in Accessibility Core Competencies (CPACC) through the IAAP. Experience facilitating group collaboration using online tools   Understanding of change management in a large organization  Knowledge of learning, development, or course design Experience working higher education  Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS809 Original Posting Date: October 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 29, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20108 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoc-Research-Associate---Veterinary-Pathology_R20067": {
      "title": "Postdoc Research Associate - Veterinary Pathology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoc Research Associate - Veterinary Pathology Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Veterinary Pathology at Iowa State University is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to support interdisciplinary research focused on prion biology, transmissible spongiform encephalopathies, and disease-associated protein misfolding. The successful candidate will contribute to the development, optimization, and evaluation of innovative methods for the isolation, recovery, and detection of disease-associated proteins in complex biological samples. This position involves designing and conducting laboratory experiments, developing antibody-based and biochemical assays, evaluating protein capture and detection approaches, and analyzing quantitative research data. The researcher will work with tissues, biological fluids, and other potentially infectious materials while adhering to established biosafety and containment protocols. Additional responsibilities include maintaining accurate research records, preparing protocols and reports, contributing to scientific publications and presentations, and collaborating on the evaluation of emerging diagnostic and detection technologies. The position offers the opportunity to work within a multidisciplinary research environment alongside scientists in veterinary medicine, biomedical sciences, and engineering, while developing independent research skills and contributing to impactful research conducted at both Iowa State University and the National Animal Disease Center. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Microbiology, Biomedical Sciences, or a closely related field, completed by the anticipated start date. Research experience in protein biochemistry, immunological assays, or related molecular and cellular laboratory methods. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with prion biology, transmissible spongiform encephalopathies, or other protein misfolding disorders. Experience developing, optimizing, or validating immunoassays and other protein detection methods. Experience with protein purification, affinity capture, magnetic bead methods, or related biochemical techniques. Experience working with infectious materials under established biosafety procedures. Record of peer-reviewed publications and effective interdisciplinary collaboration. Department/Program & College Description: Veterinary pathology provides a critical link between the basic and clinical sciences. Our faculty fill essential roles in teaching veterinary and graduate students, diagnosis of animal diseases, and scientific research. Department Unit/Website: Veterinary Pathology - Veterinary Pathology Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a federal security background check and authorization to access a federal research facility. The selected candidate must maintain the required access authorization and complete all required biosafety, prion-handling, and security training. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: November 2, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 4, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20067 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Student-Services-Specialist-II_R20125": {
      "title": "Student Services Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Student Services Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Ivy College of Business Career Services Office is seeking a Student Services Specialist II to provide customer service and data analysis in a fast-paced, student-centered environment. This position serves as a primary point of contact for the office and plays a key role in delivering exceptional service to students, faculty, staff, employers, and visitors. Additionally, this role collects employment outcomes for Ivy College of Business undergraduates, both internship and post-graduation. To achieve the goals of this position, this person oversees a small team of undergraduate student assistants.     The ideal candidate is professional, dependable, and highly organized, with the ability to positively interact with others, manage multiple priorities, and adapt to changing needs. They demonstrate curiosity and a desire to learn, taking initiative to explore new approaches, ask thoughtful questions, and identify opportunities for improvement. They anticipate requests and demonstrate strong ownership of their work. Success in this role requires excellent communication skills, attention to detail, technical proficiency, and the ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented environment.   Example of Duties: Serve as the first point of contact for visitors to the Business Career Services office. Greet students checking in for appointments as well as provide hospitality to external partners visiting for recruitment events, on-campus interviews, etc. Interact with customers by answering the main phone line and manage the email inbox for general inquiries. Collect employment outcomes, both internship and post-graduation – at graduation, 3-months following graduation, and 6-months following graduation – of three graduating classes per academic year – August, December and May (~1,000 graduates/year). Communicate with graduates by phone, text, and email, persisting until a strong knowledge rate is achieved (~90%). Utilize technology - 12twenty data management platform and Excel – to record, cleanse, and analyze data. Answer requests from colleagues for specialized data analysis as well as submit data to accrediting bodies such as the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB). Hire, train, supervise, evaluate, and celebrate the work of ~3 student Career Services Assistants (CSAs). Oversee office needs, including processing checks, inventorying/ordering supplies, and sorting mail. Plan meetings, reserve rooms, and order meals as needed for team members. Maintain relationships with vendors who have contractual relationships with the office. Support team members with special projects, classroom programming, and event coordination. Preferred Qualifications: Experience delivering exceptional customer service in a fast-paced environment with a variety of stakeholders.   Experience collecting, cleansing, analyzing, and reporting data with a high degree of accuracy. Experience hiring, training, supporting, supervising, evaluating and celebrating the work of others.  Demonstrated ability to contribute positively to a team while independently managing responsibilities and priorities. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, and experience working with Customer Relationship Management (CRM) or database systems. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: October 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 1, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20125 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Budget-and-Finance-Specialist-III_R20115": {
      "title": "Budget and Finance Specialist III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Budget and Finance Specialist III Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Specialty Business Services & Cultural Arts (SBSCA) at Iowa State University seeks a highly analytical and collaborative professional to serve as a Budget and Finance Specialist III . This position reports to the Assistant Vice President for SBSCA and serves as the SBSCA budget officer, providing advanced budget planning, financial management, reporting, analysis, and decision support for a diverse portfolio of business and cultural arts units.   The position plays a key role in supporting sound financial decision-making by preparing financial statements, forecasting budget performance, analyzing budget results, monitoring financial trends, and developing reports for university leadership and external stakeholders.   The successful candidate will work closely with division leadership on strategic budget planning, financial initiatives, and long-range forecasting while ensuring compliance with university, state, and federal requirements. The successful candidate will possess strong and current knowledge of budgeting, financial management, and accrual accounting principles; exceptional analytical and problem-solving abilities; and excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Successful candidates will demonstrate strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities. They will also possess sound judgment and the ability to interpret and apply complex financial information, policies, regulations, and contractual requirements. A collaborative approach and the ability to build effective relationships across a diverse organization are essential.   What You'll Do Prepare monthly and annual financial statements, budget reports, trend analyses, and other financial reporting tools used to support operational and strategic decisions. Research, analyze, and prepare ad hoc reports addressing financial position, budget variances, efficiencies, and other issues for university leadership, the Iowa Board of Regents, legislative requests, and other stakeholders. Coordinate development and entry of the division's approximately $50 million budget within Workday Adaptive Planning. Serve as the SBSCA budget officer, assisting with budget development, monitoring, forecasting, and long-range financial planning. Provide consultation and financial guidance to division leadership regarding budget, financial, and contractual matters. Assist in evaluating financial performance and identifying opportunities to improve efficiency and effectiveness of operations. Interpret and apply university policies, contract provisions, and applicable federal and state regulations. Support special projects and strategic initiatives as assigned. Preferred Qualifications: Certified Public Accountant (CPA), Master of Business Administration (MBA), or Master's degree in a finance- or accounting-related field Experience developing, monitoring, and forecasting complex budgets Experience analyzing financial data, preparing reports, and providing recommendations to leadership to support strategic and operational decision-making Experience using financial planning and reporting systems, such as Workday, Adaptive Planning or similar ERP platforms Experience working with multiple funding sources, including general funds, revenue funds, designated accounts, and grants Budgeting experience in higher education, government, non-profit, corporate, or similarly complex organizations Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Excel and financial modeling Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by November 1, 2026. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: October 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20115 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Term-Faculty-of-Practice-for-Finance_R20107": {
      "title": "Term Faculty of Practice for Finance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Term Faculty of Practice for Finance Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Finance in the Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University located in Ames, IA is now accepting applications for a part-time term faculty position at the rank of Lecturer or Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Practice to teach courses at the undergraduate level in Actuarial Science, Risk Management, or Finance beginning Spring semester, January 2027. Anticipated course load is one course per semester. This position will consist primarily of in-person classroom instruction on the Ames campus, with the possibility of some online course delivery. The successful candidate will additionally contribute to departmental service activities. The initial term length will be for one year, ending December 31, 2027, with the possibility for renewal. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s Degree Qualified candidates must meet the college’s standards to be qualified under AACSB accreditation standards. Preferred Qualifications: Professional credentials in Actuarial Science, Risk Management, or Finance (e.g., Fellow in the Society of Actuaries , CFA) Professional industry experience (e.g., financial services, corporate finance) Prior collegiate teaching experience   College Description: The Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University, established in 1984, furthers Iowa State University’s land-grant ideals by training students to be knowledgeable and ethical communicators, leaders, collaborators, and problem solvers through impactful research, innovative teaching, and community engagement. With the largest undergraduate business program in the state of Iowa and nationally ranked graduate programs, the Ivy College of Business is home to over 5000 students with a strong growth trajectory. We pride ourselves on our high ethical standards and our drive to promote an environment where all individuals may succeed academically, professionally, and personally. Each member of our community is committed to the college’s mission to link theory with practice for tomorrow’s business leaders. The college offers undergraduate, graduate, and Ph.D. programs and is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). Less than five percent of business schools worldwide receive this accreditation.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.ivybusiness.iastate.edu/about-ivy/academic-departments/finance/ Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: December 31, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References To be fully considered for this position, please apply on or before October 28, 2026 . For questions regarding this position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Truong Duong at: tduong@iastate.edu . If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20107 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Lecturer---Clarinet_R20112": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Clarinet",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Lecturer - Clarinet Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Music and Theatre at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa seeks a dynamic and experienced temporary instructor in clarinet from 1/1/2027 through 5/15/2027 at the rank of lecturer. The successful candidate will teach applied clarinet lessons, teach the clarinet portion of the woodwind techniques class, teach a weekly studio class, and direct the clarinet choir.   Responsibilities: Teach clarinet applied lessons Teach the clarinet portion of the music education woodwind techniques course Teach weekly studio class Direct the clarinet choir   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an on-going basis without sponsorship .   Required Minimum Qualifications :  Master’s degree in music or related discipline Demonstrated experience teaching clarinet Preferred Qualifications :  Doctoral degree in music with an emphasis in clarinet performance or clarinet pedagogy Demonstrated experience teaching clarinet at the college/university level Demonstrated experience and achievement in clarinet performance Department/Program & College Description : The Department of Music and Theatre: prepares music and theatre students for professional life. creates high impact learning experiences for students across the university. serves as the cultural life force for the university, Iowa, and beyond. provides a welcoming community for all.    The Department of Music and Theatre is committed to a philosophy of education that draws its goals from the larger purposes of liberal arts education and from the guidelines of its accrediting agency, the National Association of Schools of Music (NASM). With strong undergraduate  music  and  theatre  programs, students study with full-time faculty professionals in a supportive environment that encourages students to become their best.   Department Unit/Website : music.iastate.edu Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following:   1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Links to two performance samples (can be within the cover letter) 4) Contact Information for Three References For guaranteed consideration, please submit your application by November 20, 2026.   If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 20, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20112 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
