    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Web-Content-Specialist---Temporary_R20104": {
      "title": "Web Content Specialist - Temporary",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Web Content Specialist - Temporary Appointment Type: Professional & Scientific Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: We are seeking a Web Content Specialist to help manage and enhance our organization's digital presence. This position will work a minimum of 15 hours and up to 40 hours per week, depending on business needs and candidate availability.   In this role, you will publish weekly news stories, produce monthly digital newsletters, and ensure website content remains current, accurate, and engaging.    You will manage a web support ticket queue, complete content updates, and coordinate with the web development team to resolve technical issues and website bugs.   This position also plays a key role in maintaining and improving the user experience through page layout updates, content organization, and website enhancements. The ideal candidate is highly organized, detail-oriented, and able to successfully manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Strong communication skills, a commitment to content quality, and a user-focused mindset are essential for success in this role. Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent  Experience creating, editing, and publishing digital content for websites, newsletters, or other online platforms.   Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Communications, Journalism, English, Marketing, Public Relations, Web Design, Information Technology, or a related field. Experience managing website content for a large or complex organization. Experience writing and editing news stories, feature articles, or digital communications. Experience producing email newsletters or other digital communications. Knowledge of website accessibility and usability best practices. Experience using web analytics tools and data to inform content decisions. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: October 26, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: P&S Temporary Original Posting Date: October 16, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20104 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
